[{"sha":"3f82114c374f71f740c37a990cd96b1578a318ac","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDNmODIxMTRjMzc0ZjcxZjc0MGMzN2E5OTBjZDk2YjE1NzhhMzE4YWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T19:48:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T19:48:59Z"},"message":"refactor(code): drop `config list`/`ls` aliases for `config show` (#4783)\n\n`dcode config list`/`dcode config ls` are removed; use `dcode config\nshow` (add `--verbose` to see all option keys).\n\n---\n\n`config list`/`config ls` duplicated `config show`, so this removes both\nparser aliases and makes `config show` the sole command for displaying\neffective config values and their sources. Drops `list_mode`, the\n`config list` JSON label/catalog special-casing, backward-compat\ncomments, and now-dead paths; `config show --json` keeps effective-only\nfields (catalog folded in only with `--verbose`) and always labels the\npayload `\"config show\"`. User-facing suggestions now point at `config\nshow`/`config show --verbose`. Backward compatibility is intentionally\nnot preserved.\n\n### Breaking change\n\n`config list --json` was the machine-readable catalog endpoint (its JSON\nenvelope `command` field was `\"config list\"` and it always folded in\ncatalog fields). It is gone: the command no longer parses, and the\ncatalog fields are now available via `config show --verbose --json`\n(payload labeled `\"config show\"`). Any machine consumer of `config list\n--json` must migrate.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7351f382-9468-b4dc-2df4-03eaf75ef12f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9fbd9a92172de44d2d873f46dc9652b08be65d27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9fbd9a92172de44d2d873f46dc9652b08be65d27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3f82114c374f71f740c37a990cd96b1578a318ac","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWocrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1BUQAI6Vu3jBbM8GMXVb+VkNEtsy\nTqUZBZsr3TVczlBOvI0r+8zUa777tq02CuZhCk5PVNo1kcNW9FUvE2qBEDjTayrO\njqGHue79+2AQi20WiDBQwJ0q6z6LySQ3A8yZ49gj5RgQBPkIhbHVg01o/xZrlIIm\nYRDlHr9dGhjKNmuubtlpvEVyY6Fy0Ucnzt1dCbln3R8VyqsIX45+RKvoBWU8XsTS\n2crhpSQbCj5DWQFPHdxG33RihB01BgXcWMd9vJ45quYPxfV+n1lt6Bx4YOJWXwgt\n1Ahoae/3Y3WBFyIEBvdM7qep+6+8cfVZs28Fb9eaLCMlvhPXfq9+GtjKD+5dfi1E\nGbW/RY8AhVzrLT5O4cSQseAf9fEHg/wbyaqCqGMcZPy/HL96jANry6UroUPBThRu\nrGpDWrojMZLtmFVFxO+zEHD61hfx5qqeDLT+bznI8EL/v8V8z2tlMIOgnacilSs2\nG1GRnMmx1cJJ+AdRT7IDN9D4eqcVmqCzA+XiFgd1i8JG0dbntysRUUSwgpNpJsaK\nRBfp2ncub2wCAmj1D/VtQ/yPDY8luF6PPM3bE4EaF/NNpG9TopDeTNJltPJr9d3a\nn4rUbkdk3EN7zpDA+I9TTicgbqDuyzE4nvAB0O/oK3GGXf0L0dclEpTwqlj9v5GC\nh5bTMBP6wdI4o1mt2Z26\n=YDzN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9fbd9a92172de44d2d873f46dc9652b08be65d27\nparent 66048202355ab758c72fdaeb57c1ab9168305129\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784317739 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784317739 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): drop `config list`/`ls` aliases for `config show` (#4783)\n\n`dcode config list`/`dcode config ls` are removed; use `dcode config\nshow` (add `--verbose` to see all option keys).\n\n---\n\n`config list`/`config ls` duplicated `config show`, so this removes both\nparser aliases and makes `config show` the sole command for displaying\neffective config values and their sources. Drops `list_mode`, the\n`config list` JSON label/catalog special-casing, backward-compat\ncomments, and now-dead paths; `config show --json` keeps effective-only\nfields (catalog folded in only with `--verbose`) and always labels the\npayload `\"config show\"`. User-facing suggestions now point at `config\nshow`/`config show --verbose`. Backward compatibility is intentionally\nnot preserved.\n\n### Breaking change\n\n`config list --json` was the machine-readable catalog endpoint (its JSON\nenvelope `command` field was `\"config list\"` and it always folded in\ncatalog fields). It is gone: the command no longer parses, and the\ncatalog fields are now available via `config show --verbose --json`\n(payload labeled `\"config show\"`). Any machine consumer of `config list\n--json` must migrate.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7351f382-9468-b4dc-2df4-03eaf75ef12f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T19:48:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3f82114c374f71f740c37a990cd96b1578a318ac","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3f82114c374f71f740c37a990cd96b1578a318ac","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3f82114c374f71f740c37a990cd96b1578a318ac/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"66048202355ab758c72fdaeb57c1ab9168305129","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/66048202355ab758c72fdaeb57c1ab9168305129","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/66048202355ab758c72fdaeb57c1ab9168305129"}]},{"sha":"66048202355ab758c72fdaeb57c1ab9168305129","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY2MDQ4MjAyMzU1YWI3NThjNzJmZGFlYjU3YzFhYjkxNjgzMDUxMjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T19:28:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T19:28:07Z"},"message":"fix(infra): preserve merge base in Dependabot lockfile fixer (#4829)\n\nRelated #4827\n\nThe Dependabot lockfile fixer now keeps enough Git history to inspect\ndependency PRs that have fallen behind `main`.\n\n---\n\nThe preflight checkout already retrieves complete history, but its\nexplicit fetch of the event-time base used `--depth=1`. That marked the\nbase commit as a shallow boundary, so the three-dot diff could not walk\nback to the common ancestor when `main` had advanced after Dependabot\ncreated its branch.\n\nFetch the exact base SHA without limiting its depth. This retains the\nevent snapshot while preserving the ancestry needed by the path-scope\nguard. The fix was validated against the base and head SHAs from #4827,\nwhere the diff now resolves to the two expected `libs/talon` files.","tree":{"sha":"129410f4426d654c5337c57ae0576cf18952b8cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/129410f4426d654c5337c57ae0576cf18952b8cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/66048202355ab758c72fdaeb57c1ab9168305129","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWoJHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8YEQABscTnEkAZCJbWX2qRqiRylS\nj59S5xKWHtM25l5qjTmaaGWYmIJzGu3eXvYdTybv+72+meF+A5HfMFe+nOKffBfo\nSKjZz06Py8ovhlNuinu943t7D7SHSwuGLBETJpwx5xcuXgsvBcYm5fT02fvSPclc\ntF8jGiTo3+pqzu6H+U1E9IEDi7xoulDznm6Uq5Qvuco/l2Ca0omPBHxFjibDYj3i\nHGiLdialPFGTXF4dH53bVWM4FRtEp+6NmsT3upmpbL/SHE1ugwpu7uhcDAf0cV1i\nToMxQPlKSmy23UwvYvYgCULB4GGrLvwcWET3D5vqiIWl6exRk9hnS9iCO9705Ccu\nZeceOY0T6aT31ehy3ViZH7jXFhAdGm+oDxkLkX5TWyqCjMeKq84135c4CxPLNXSs\nAHSR6LUJAzrAK1DSHkOysJIZFdK8KiGlVE8vHTpJlNFp/mJjn3MdZ2CHjpxvBFjt\nkhlaQSn1FH1rS700fWc+wuvFJakyANm6I9AkXzQsIpw3KjbooLeB1JikVxCshmyv\niBFAPyzMqIemmNKH3TqcuYnXkdHIkeSdyqcaOqrlEj55pN9xC2ChA/dqb1CID+eq\nep/x8z8ktNmhRDHRhZkErW4wsns/wg9kharTCgLO7LA6LrT3LoNAKUFLLpR5YWa7\nzA5MEOyXPW39lo5z95eL\n=yfzJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 129410f4426d654c5337c57ae0576cf18952b8cd\nparent 68adab563caab129baa9c87a4800c37a6110aea2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784316487 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784316487 -0400\n\nfix(infra): preserve merge base in Dependabot lockfile fixer (#4829)\n\nRelated #4827\n\nThe Dependabot lockfile fixer now keeps enough Git history to inspect\ndependency PRs that have fallen behind `main`.\n\n---\n\nThe preflight checkout already retrieves complete history, but its\nexplicit fetch of the event-time base used `--depth=1`. That marked the\nbase commit as a shallow boundary, so the three-dot diff could not walk\nback to the common ancestor when `main` had advanced after Dependabot\ncreated its branch.\n\nFetch the exact base SHA without limiting its depth. This retains the\nevent snapshot while preserving the ancestry needed by the path-scope\nguard. The fix was validated against the base and head SHAs from #4827,\nwhere the diff now resolves to the two expected `libs/talon` files.","verified_at":"2026-07-17T19:28:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/66048202355ab758c72fdaeb57c1ab9168305129","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/66048202355ab758c72fdaeb57c1ab9168305129","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/66048202355ab758c72fdaeb57c1ab9168305129/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"68adab563caab129baa9c87a4800c37a6110aea2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/68adab563caab129baa9c87a4800c37a6110aea2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/68adab563caab129baa9c87a4800c37a6110aea2"}]},{"sha":"68adab563caab129baa9c87a4800c37a6110aea2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY4YWRhYjU2M2NhYWIxMjliYWE5Yzg3YTQ4MDBjMzdhNjExMGFlYTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-17T19:17:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T19:17:41Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump torch from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0 in /libs/talon (#4827)\n\nBumps [torch](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch) from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/releases\">torch's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>PyTorch 2.13.0 Release Notes</h1>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#highlights\">Highlights</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#backwards-incompatible-changes\">Backwards\nIncompatible Changes</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#deprecations\">Deprecations</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#new-features\">New\nFeatures</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#improvements\">Improvements</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#bug-fixes\">Bug\nfixes</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#performance\">Performance</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#documentation\">Documentation</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#developers\">Developers</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h1>Highlights</h1>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<p>For more details about these highlighted features, you can look at\nthe release blogpost. Below are the full release notes for this\nrelease.</p>\n<h1>Tracked Regressions</h1>\n<h3>ROCm wheels break <code>torch.compile</code> on CPU in environments\nwithout a GPU</h3>\n<p>Running a <code>torch==2.13.0+rocm7.2</code> wheel in an environment\nwhere no GPU is available (<code>torch.cuda.is_available()</code> is\n<code>False</code>) breaks <code>torch.compile</code> on the CPU path:\nthe first compile raises <code>RuntimeError: Can't detect vectorized ISA\nfor CPU</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/189194\">#189194</a>).\nThis is a regression from <code>torch==2.12.1+rocm7.2</code>, which\ncompiles CPU code fine (detecting e.g. <code>VecAVX2</code>) in the same\nsetup. The 2.13 ROCm wheel appears to rely on something present in the\nROCm builder image to detect the CPU vectorized ISA, so it works when\nrun on a ROCm image but fails on a plain CPU-only image.</p>\n<p>Workaround: run the <code>+rocm</code> wheel on a ROCm image, or\ninstall a standard CPU/CUDA build for GPU-less environments.</p>\n<h1>Backwards Incompatible Changes</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Stop building CPython 3.13t (free-threaded) binaries (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/182951\">#182951</a>)</p>\n<p>Upstream <code>pypa/manylinux</code> removed CPython 3.13t\n(free-threaded) on 2026-05-07, because 3.13t\nwas experimental and has been superseded by the now-non-experimental\nCPython 3.14t. As a result,\nPyTorch 2.13 no longer ships <code>cp313t</code> wheels (Linux, Triton,\nand related artifacts). Users on the\nfree-threaded interpreter should move to Python 3.14t.</p>\n<p>PyTorch 2.12:</p>\n<pre lang=\"bash\"><code># cp313t (free-threaded 3.13) wheels were\navailable\npython3.13t -m pip install torch\n</code></pre>\n<p>PyTorch 2.13:</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/cf30153c4c131c8164ee7798e5022d810682e2cb\"><code>cf30153</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Strip +PTX from CUDA arch list on release/RC builds (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/188914\">#188914</a>)\n...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/3e3e24bd95b010f8f74915f0c30476906e60d4fc\"><code>3e3e24b</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Restrict cuda-bindings to Python &lt; 3.15 for CUDA 12.9\nbuilds (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/7986b068032abf5e22ea51fe7fea63ef5bcaf3b1\"><code>7986b06</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Bump binary build timeout 280 -&gt; 400 minutes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/188551\">#188551</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/0bdbc268e08fba9debac8f35a8a12e9c008ec0fd\"><code>0bdbc26</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Add CUDA 12.9 to TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST tables (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/188443\">#188443</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/9cabb45ca6e6ed3bb4645c929bcfd07691651f74\"><code>9cabb45</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Update manywheel docker image pin to 78e737ad (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/188409\">#188409</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/78e737ad29420ffc4800e677c51e2a852caf8359\"><code>78e737a</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Revert &quot;Tighten generalized scatter graph target (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/184075\">#184075</a>)&quot;\n(#...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/0bb9b5bc24bed3278488372d62d9f2235e9e77e3\"><code>0bb9b5b</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Revert &quot;dynamo: round-trip torch.cuda.stream ctx mgr\nacross gr...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/aaac2bfe460c04a4d41e83e03452d2347f7142b9\"><code>aaac2bf</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Revert &quot;[Reland] Port D104346887/PR 182675 for\nindex_add fast ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/933081368c3ab64fa2e953217e413b3ba52844e3\"><code>9330813</code></a>\nFix build_with_debinfo.py broken by CONFIGURE_DEPENDS globbing (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/188192\">#188192</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/4e077a7dcf29167db9e97d86cc62f431905e09f7\"><code>4e077a7</code></a>\nRemove setuptools upper bound (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/188190\">#188190</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/compare/v2.12.1...v2.13.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=torch&package-manager=uv&previous-version=2.12.1&new-version=2.13.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cdf445ea5d85bd8c65fe1ca4a7db731e51cbc839","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/cdf445ea5d85bd8c65fe1ca4a7db731e51cbc839"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/68adab563caab129baa9c87a4800c37a6110aea2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWn/VCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlO0QAI0OOkF+iFB86AuW0bFrrIQL\nmxbHpXnD1SmjqzJrU/SpUZP5Hg0BuYouoZJ0mSc/kTAnqkag1fdclecEH19+EvkW\naGfhgc8tpW/2NNHGXng8g8j3AWwSSgJ4WYM8QjHSShBBjwPHKAxZuJj0eQfnWQk6\nZcQhv+FvVQiXhe8UQSCjn44Ml61XuP5/lxkdw5yO31dYiDA0ME0vXEE2lfuvbP+I\nm4Xpg6GVBLF2uOwXiCY45pCp4MkYaULBjQp4Z/Jr4utCfv3Kz5qRYC4H3cGZrJmv\nbG5n9noa3pcG/0g91QEfE9+FmaTE8cJ4Dnkm5HgtCxMnWSrtx/Cvjekgm5b/isI8\nT8kKyz7ukSUIesga3TkRXGjtp2fcQDdoEBactH9LVltuN24mIMl5oN6pqPTTctW1\n58hXKS3mfeGLhaK2fk7WVm/2r2ltyCSTEPMRfM7nUnWzTrNJNOsx7zVMzJr0J3GG\nqYWk5/86sJxMBhDWq0qu5UA2iJKBc1pLxY9AKyZ85358V0QPuSzi7y9PbSKL+1T9\nnhwcd+JW95+lnj2RYjKTr0CTZcsLYynZ2o9DZb/yYKKRdv1hkU3JAOvYlyy7purL\ntGcV+TKf8ZobiFdpS9l2heuLWOTdzZ+h/CDV+diyzSj+XWLXlIRjDr+xqmE+b3s7\nic5H3r6r5bDCV/qtbvaF\n=AFuN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cdf445ea5d85bd8c65fe1ca4a7db731e51cbc839\nparent a915c590dfb7c50d9bf697953ce724bad8dd4149\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784315861 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784315861 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump torch from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0 in /libs/talon (#4827)\n\nBumps [torch](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch) from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/releases\">torch's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>PyTorch 2.13.0 Release Notes</h1>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#highlights\">Highlights</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#backwards-incompatible-changes\">Backwards\nIncompatible Changes</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#deprecations\">Deprecations</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#new-features\">New\nFeatures</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#improvements\">Improvements</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#bug-fixes\">Bug\nfixes</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#performance\">Performance</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#documentation\">Documentation</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/HEAD/#developers\">Developers</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h1>Highlights</h1>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<p>For more details about these highlighted features, you can look at\nthe release blogpost. Below are the full release notes for this\nrelease.</p>\n<h1>Tracked Regressions</h1>\n<h3>ROCm wheels break <code>torch.compile</code> on CPU in environments\nwithout a GPU</h3>\n<p>Running a <code>torch==2.13.0+rocm7.2</code> wheel in an environment\nwhere no GPU is available (<code>torch.cuda.is_available()</code> is\n<code>False</code>) breaks <code>torch.compile</code> on the CPU path:\nthe first compile raises <code>RuntimeError: Can't detect vectorized ISA\nfor CPU</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/189194\">#189194</a>).\nThis is a regression from <code>torch==2.12.1+rocm7.2</code>, which\ncompiles CPU code fine (detecting e.g. <code>VecAVX2</code>) in the same\nsetup. The 2.13 ROCm wheel appears to rely on something present in the\nROCm builder image to detect the CPU vectorized ISA, so it works when\nrun on a ROCm image but fails on a plain CPU-only image.</p>\n<p>Workaround: run the <code>+rocm</code> wheel on a ROCm image, or\ninstall a standard CPU/CUDA build for GPU-less environments.</p>\n<h1>Backwards Incompatible Changes</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Stop building CPython 3.13t (free-threaded) binaries (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/182951\">#182951</a>)</p>\n<p>Upstream <code>pypa/manylinux</code> removed CPython 3.13t\n(free-threaded) on 2026-05-07, because 3.13t\nwas experimental and has been superseded by the now-non-experimental\nCPython 3.14t. As a result,\nPyTorch 2.13 no longer ships <code>cp313t</code> wheels (Linux, Triton,\nand related artifacts). Users on the\nfree-threaded interpreter should move to Python 3.14t.</p>\n<p>PyTorch 2.12:</p>\n<pre lang=\"bash\"><code># cp313t (free-threaded 3.13) wheels were\navailable\npython3.13t -m pip install torch\n</code></pre>\n<p>PyTorch 2.13:</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/cf30153c4c131c8164ee7798e5022d810682e2cb\"><code>cf30153</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Strip +PTX from CUDA arch list on release/RC builds (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/188914\">#188914</a>)\n...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/3e3e24bd95b010f8f74915f0c30476906e60d4fc\"><code>3e3e24b</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Restrict cuda-bindings to Python &lt; 3.15 for CUDA 12.9\nbuilds (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/7986b068032abf5e22ea51fe7fea63ef5bcaf3b1\"><code>7986b06</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Bump binary build timeout 280 -&gt; 400 minutes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/188551\">#188551</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/0bdbc268e08fba9debac8f35a8a12e9c008ec0fd\"><code>0bdbc26</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Add CUDA 12.9 to TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST tables (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/188443\">#188443</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/9cabb45ca6e6ed3bb4645c929bcfd07691651f74\"><code>9cabb45</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Update manywheel docker image pin to 78e737ad (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/188409\">#188409</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/78e737ad29420ffc4800e677c51e2a852caf8359\"><code>78e737a</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Revert &quot;Tighten generalized scatter graph target (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/184075\">#184075</a>)&quot;\n(#...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/0bb9b5bc24bed3278488372d62d9f2235e9e77e3\"><code>0bb9b5b</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Revert &quot;dynamo: round-trip torch.cuda.stream ctx mgr\nacross gr...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/aaac2bfe460c04a4d41e83e03452d2347f7142b9\"><code>aaac2bf</code></a>\n[release/2.13] Revert &quot;[Reland] Port D104346887/PR 182675 for\nindex_add fast ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/933081368c3ab64fa2e953217e413b3ba52844e3\"><code>9330813</code></a>\nFix build_with_debinfo.py broken by CONFIGURE_DEPENDS globbing (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/188192\">#188192</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/4e077a7dcf29167db9e97d86cc62f431905e09f7\"><code>4e077a7</code></a>\nRemove setuptools upper bound (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/188190\">#188190</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/compare/v2.12.1...v2.13.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=torch&package-manager=uv&previous-version=2.12.1&new-version=2.13.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T19:17:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/68adab563caab129baa9c87a4800c37a6110aea2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/68adab563caab129baa9c87a4800c37a6110aea2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/68adab563caab129baa9c87a4800c37a6110aea2/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a915c590dfb7c50d9bf697953ce724bad8dd4149","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a915c590dfb7c50d9bf697953ce724bad8dd4149","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a915c590dfb7c50d9bf697953ce724bad8dd4149"}]},{"sha":"a915c590dfb7c50d9bf697953ce724bad8dd4149","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE5MTVjNTkwZGZiN2M1MGQ5YmY2OTc5NTNjZTcyNGJhZDhkZDQxNDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T19:11:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T19:11:09Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep chat input responsive during `/restart` (#4808)\n\nTyping in the chat input is no longer blocked while the `/restart`\ncommand respawns the server.\n\n---\n\nRunning `/restart` froze the chat input until the server finished\nrespawning. `_handle_restart_command` awaited the multi-second\n`_restart_server_manual` (`server_proc.restart()`) directly on the\nTextual message pump, so key events stopped being forwarded and the chat\ninput was \"blocked\". This is the same class of bug fixed for the MCP\nviewer `Ctrl+R` reconnect path in #4753 — the fix runs the respawn as a\ndetached `asyncio.create_task` (mirroring the MCP viewer/force-reconnect\npaths), keeping the pump free so keystrokes stay live and queued\nmessages drain once `ServerReady` fires.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a27e2ef4-b392-c236-f410-c1b9ebc533aa)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9bcab34fa347fc48c94d4bd8af418f9c22817d22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9bcab34fa347fc48c94d4bd8af418f9c22817d22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a915c590dfb7c50d9bf697953ce724bad8dd4149","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWn5NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAr6gQAGmwdEtFIP57peWpH6t71Kq5\n/VX3djvuzMxIWTym0c4nCl8o0zXoGAiTNXr6pzwGRLS28utWvTRFv2yPLhHcKKxH\n3QfHRw4FBLzmUJFS8G11RmuYAYVAzOYebNlketTxnf7ev5s91eEqpbXY3a37MLKg\nZ0lzOhaUCsYa8xXsRwfSSlv7Nj9l6xMqO3EFmyAxZTUsKJRKT5oNwVnuvUbL2p1i\no6Y/GRSQASoxY6s5p8NY2/9hwaHRUKpP3CLJpqZn4BHDX6agGyQTA0ON+t4qbBTo\nFi/1YJtF90UuWk7996h+lYNkM63a/pjgyvQmCSvEmq1fZx4eLi+wOmTItOuBAi/w\nW8gtWtAoLq28nByY2UJIWBTFHPECIHZTqskkkMxTqwSYASy1OXJFKJ8euUc14hsb\nnLn4RDPwaVGOHttTkLeVuiEhwDdvXfko67r2C9ISEwqfZ1W7mdF35NeonpsycY6h\nA5iimfcvdNcGUMNR9fX9s00eNRmG62UvaRVshU6yltFFYauiXraqXcyrIpQArgrf\nIFj/OaPBXCRJrBuKJYS31y3Re7EUQiqPiV8x2/7YV7Ys6JO7hwoxXAtDDKZZgsk2\nPZVqJ3QauHb96lGu5vvyS6nI5IQr0cNHLCwG3VmelJuJE5TIH38morub6S/20auf\nnnhnb5vMGNFOZ/0Kawdc\n=jlSg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9bcab34fa347fc48c94d4bd8af418f9c22817d22\nparent 7408378896344e4db7dbc45a35ae6b02cc746d31\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784315469 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784315469 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep chat input responsive during `/restart` (#4808)\n\nTyping in the chat input is no longer blocked while the `/restart`\ncommand respawns the server.\n\n---\n\nRunning `/restart` froze the chat input until the server finished\nrespawning. `_handle_restart_command` awaited the multi-second\n`_restart_server_manual` (`server_proc.restart()`) directly on the\nTextual message pump, so key events stopped being forwarded and the chat\ninput was \"blocked\". This is the same class of bug fixed for the MCP\nviewer `Ctrl+R` reconnect path in #4753 — the fix runs the respawn as a\ndetached `asyncio.create_task` (mirroring the MCP viewer/force-reconnect\npaths), keeping the pump free so keystrokes stay live and queued\nmessages drain once `ServerReady` fires.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a27e2ef4-b392-c236-f410-c1b9ebc533aa)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T19:11:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a915c590dfb7c50d9bf697953ce724bad8dd4149","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a915c590dfb7c50d9bf697953ce724bad8dd4149","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a915c590dfb7c50d9bf697953ce724bad8dd4149/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7408378896344e4db7dbc45a35ae6b02cc746d31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7408378896344e4db7dbc45a35ae6b02cc746d31","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7408378896344e4db7dbc45a35ae6b02cc746d31"}]},{"sha":"7408378896344e4db7dbc45a35ae6b02cc746d31","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc0MDgzNzg4OTYzNDRlNGRiN2RiYzQ1YTM1YWU2YjAyY2M3NDZkMzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T19:09:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T19:09:44Z"},"message":"fix(code): disentangle version diagnostics for editable installs (#4816)\n\nEditable installs conflated three distinct version facts, so `/version`,\n`--version`, and `doctor` could silently report a single number that hid\nstale metadata or a broken SDK dependency pin. Version diagnostics now\nseparate the live source version, the installed distribution metadata\nversion, and the `deepagents` requirement that `deepagents-code`\ndeclares — reporting the source version as primary for editable\ninstalls, showing the installed metadata alongside it when they drift,\nand flagging an actionable mismatch when the installed SDK metadata does\nnot satisfy the declared requirement.\n\n---\n\nA new structured `DistributionVersion`/`VersionReport` representation in\n`extras_info` is the single source of truth these surfaces render.\n`resolve_sdk_version()` is preserved as a thin compatibility wrapper so\nexisting callers are untouched.\n\n- `/version`, `--version`, and `doctor` render the same facts: an\neditable SDK is now clearly identified (not just editable\n`deepagents-code`), source/metadata drift shows both versions, and an\nunsatisfied requirement (compared via `packaging.Requirement`) is\nsurfaced as `required by deepagents-code: <version> — mismatch`.\n- `doctor` marks a dependency-requirement mismatch unhealthy, while\ntreating source/metadata drift as informational since it is normal while\nediting SDK source.\n- Normal non-editable output is unchanged when all versions agree, and\nversion collection stays fully offline and best-effort (no\n`uv`/`pip`/PyPI, no subprocess).\n- No package versions or dependency pins were changed.\n\nTwo existing `doctor` integration tests now isolate the SDK requirement\ncheck so they stay deterministic regardless of the workspace's\nintentional prerelease pin; the mismatch and drift paths have dedicated\nnew coverage.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1145d1a5-ba8a-abbb-e5b7-039e9c2a5b04)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"69115d23fea19b137d4ef6459f593f07f97b800c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/69115d23fea19b137d4ef6459f593f07f97b800c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7408378896344e4db7dbc45a35ae6b02cc746d31","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWn34CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAONwQABwoGrUy+Z/F/+OVkjF36NEL\nnHTYpQlgG3RhukyrLUG8thpAN+mK+qVLKNeXN7jrj4YvduKB7iX+wQC4moXEqCfc\njJ+Qu+hZYPSXsFDEQl0RnUxWgpZnDqXCRK/IKXmRtYzCI1XT32WvQPArrpum8xIA\nxC3urNuo37AUUYYWIhD9HOXt0zGOEPzHC8xE8WntlEOkm6vVstC5FDiL20Dx/18C\nF7euQr8ylJh+0CZtGQTVfQZZ6MmOHrQjalfoWnvcmqyYY/5IdsO556yiLvn9HSsT\nfyznIlU6VgWT7WvaHkimmz55Xq1IuRcKrxpzS21yjKdXc4fZobgHjgrFae4Uo+fu\nPadt6jL6/Gzvm9SilJQOdxwC536dGo+F9bCM9sSoKjSQU9dt4tdWp8ob+jLkXIrq\nDXb6opcK8+himJT+kIg1ia8N74lYm0EF4BuZqudwMibwRJe96mpRM/pj5aKkGaB8\n4XitNKtSPk4v6DUHUoqsu6WYTYkBBIMPY5OyjLxG5ewpGxf4cac4kvNiSiFsFFJO\nTR+XQbIRYu341hlOAEkIo2E+Yh6bofbo84g+mNus07sx5e84GNcIFXMTqrBOtpRs\n4zmU4gT47ldFCdv7qtPqga4D55yLw5C2O3qo9BxKOIrPVKeWpzA4XSQ2T+vMtTVQ\nHJNB7Odaj2OPsvG5x7bM\n=BX3p\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 69115d23fea19b137d4ef6459f593f07f97b800c\nparent 69520118a7f96866a5e92e7b31894d8ba3312938\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784315384 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784315384 -0400\n\nfix(code): disentangle version diagnostics for editable installs (#4816)\n\nEditable installs conflated three distinct version facts, so `/version`,\n`--version`, and `doctor` could silently report a single number that hid\nstale metadata or a broken SDK dependency pin. Version diagnostics now\nseparate the live source version, the installed distribution metadata\nversion, and the `deepagents` requirement that `deepagents-code`\ndeclares — reporting the source version as primary for editable\ninstalls, showing the installed metadata alongside it when they drift,\nand flagging an actionable mismatch when the installed SDK metadata does\nnot satisfy the declared requirement.\n\n---\n\nA new structured `DistributionVersion`/`VersionReport` representation in\n`extras_info` is the single source of truth these surfaces render.\n`resolve_sdk_version()` is preserved as a thin compatibility wrapper so\nexisting callers are untouched.\n\n- `/version`, `--version`, and `doctor` render the same facts: an\neditable SDK is now clearly identified (not just editable\n`deepagents-code`), source/metadata drift shows both versions, and an\nunsatisfied requirement (compared via `packaging.Requirement`) is\nsurfaced as `required by deepagents-code: <version> — mismatch`.\n- `doctor` marks a dependency-requirement mismatch unhealthy, while\ntreating source/metadata drift as informational since it is normal while\nediting SDK source.\n- Normal non-editable output is unchanged when all versions agree, and\nversion collection stays fully offline and best-effort (no\n`uv`/`pip`/PyPI, no subprocess).\n- No package versions or dependency pins were changed.\n\nTwo existing `doctor` integration tests now isolate the SDK requirement\ncheck so they stay deterministic regardless of the workspace's\nintentional prerelease pin; the mismatch and drift paths have dedicated\nnew coverage.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1145d1a5-ba8a-abbb-e5b7-039e9c2a5b04)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T19:09:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7408378896344e4db7dbc45a35ae6b02cc746d31","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7408378896344e4db7dbc45a35ae6b02cc746d31","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7408378896344e4db7dbc45a35ae6b02cc746d31/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"69520118a7f96866a5e92e7b31894d8ba3312938","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/69520118a7f96866a5e92e7b31894d8ba3312938","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/69520118a7f96866a5e92e7b31894d8ba3312938"}]},{"sha":"69520118a7f96866a5e92e7b31894d8ba3312938","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY5NTIwMTE4YTdmOTY4NjZhNWU5MmU3YjMxODk0ZDhiYTMzMTI5Mzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T19:02:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T19:02:28Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep `task` timers monotonic across nested subagent HITL (#4771)\n\nFixed dcode TUI `task` elapsed timers resetting when a nested subagent\nreached a human-in-the-loop approval checkpoint.\n\n---\n\nA long-running `task [general-purpose]` row's elapsed timer reset to\nzero whenever a nested subagent hit a HITL approval checkpoint. The\ninterrupt handler paused/resumed *every* tracked tool row, and\n`ToolCallMessage.pause_running()`/`set_running()` clear and reassign\n`_start_time` — so an unrelated nested child's (or sibling subagent's)\napproval restarted the outer `task` timers. This scopes pause/resume to\nonly the rows an interrupt actually owns (matched by tool name + args\nvia the new `_interrupt_owned_tool_rows` helper). Untracked nested-child\ninterrupts now own no outer row, so outer and sibling `task` timers stay\nmonotonic and completed `Took …` durations reflect full execution time.\nA tool awaiting its own initial approval still pauses then resumes as\nbefore.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/5c0ae962-c16b-6e04-ada4-d4d76826adb9)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c31f8244756f501bc9e4146b2075a168f41bc5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1c31f8244756f501bc9e4146b2075a168f41bc5b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/69520118a7f96866a5e92e7b31894d8ba3312938","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnxECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/RcQAHq3DuwAUQ5Oq95G/7mYoXB5\nyynUvRfmG8GdrAQ88/QBwsD63EEPMsVHDF+wiNdH6NbQ6zIQuqkBbTdvBhsysdSh\n33bLjDHZ/rBfUGK9u2/3CxWRESdridcoR/yEDws0wDxQPyCNQg3EePzKFqjO9JBR\nLBob7ASu2RQMIjt13Js/GVpoY9qTCQahSC4ARkjZkeoTOc8Knal2Y6xRI/xZYjHE\n9Z8scYlXL2MzxkHGVRX7xjDKoAYsP7CxF56hTKhbUVBjrgA8D2rbIrLZ4SjpX27y\nNRmPN6WriuPueHQGNA1aEMCBW3FI5K/bn82+tr/6DxyEEmq3BVM13n/0nmIMRWBZ\nyZdvwOrtWoLhhd8KGI2YUz60RJE9m73j21FN8IjhSljuAvJV/B9MeW3b+XN28yIE\ngcvBrOht8L4Dq2Ry6GzECIo9h9J9NvwxNgz6Sv/pgFreirRgGE3qjooxz9RvDyFw\n34/i7jUp0ZYOWPvs7k+C41bN8VrD4NV7vkHNgv9GOkyLCmCGsnWnoH4KcyV5n9NV\n0fHgSm4kIkR/uVVGWNnOpqtbXGQXzcHQrVtotaJPZAEd2bGQXzpTMvAbxCnHA+B0\nrsGTXBGQQRUjWfhblKFgQvrMMP0Bz/y+OEGe7eVNu2lGNcrsA8GEYAmWBnbiRa9c\nDM6wVxsGT8E5mlQ3uWXl\n=07BU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1c31f8244756f501bc9e4146b2075a168f41bc5b\nparent 4e618f07b4b00f94133b4d1c105011c438cb35be\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784314948 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784314948 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep `task` timers monotonic across nested subagent HITL (#4771)\n\nFixed dcode TUI `task` elapsed timers resetting when a nested subagent\nreached a human-in-the-loop approval checkpoint.\n\n---\n\nA long-running `task [general-purpose]` row's elapsed timer reset to\nzero whenever a nested subagent hit a HITL approval checkpoint. The\ninterrupt handler paused/resumed *every* tracked tool row, and\n`ToolCallMessage.pause_running()`/`set_running()` clear and reassign\n`_start_time` — so an unrelated nested child's (or sibling subagent's)\napproval restarted the outer `task` timers. This scopes pause/resume to\nonly the rows an interrupt actually owns (matched by tool name + args\nvia the new `_interrupt_owned_tool_rows` helper). Untracked nested-child\ninterrupts now own no outer row, so outer and sibling `task` timers stay\nmonotonic and completed `Took …` durations reflect full execution time.\nA tool awaiting its own initial approval still pauses then resumes as\nbefore.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/5c0ae962-c16b-6e04-ada4-d4d76826adb9)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T19:02:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/69520118a7f96866a5e92e7b31894d8ba3312938","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/69520118a7f96866a5e92e7b31894d8ba3312938","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/69520118a7f96866a5e92e7b31894d8ba3312938/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4e618f07b4b00f94133b4d1c105011c438cb35be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4e618f07b4b00f94133b4d1c105011c438cb35be","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4e618f07b4b00f94133b4d1c105011c438cb35be"}]},{"sha":"4e618f07b4b00f94133b4d1c105011c438cb35be","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRlNjE4ZjA3YjRiMDBmOTQxMzNiNGQxYzEwNTAxMWM0MzhjYjM1YmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:57:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:57:06Z"},"message":"fix(code): drop `uv install` tip from `/version` update hint (#4822)\n\nThe `/version` command's update-available line hard-coded `uv tool\ninstall -U deepagents-code`, which is stale guidance now that dcode\nauto-updates on relaunch and offers `/update` and `dcode update`. It now\npoints at the relaunch/auto-update path when auto-update is enabled, and\nat `/update` or `dcode update` otherwise.\n\n---\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a8b54b7c-cc2f-e6cc-a034-61a8578b8a04)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"12f6354b696f3ab577ef6d33c2798d70ec039c20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/12f6354b696f3ab577ef6d33c2798d70ec039c20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4e618f07b4b00f94133b4d1c105011c438cb35be","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnsCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmLYQAD1ewoal7sakX9eFaTcszdhF\nRT6YUhq3N1EGnKoVdfdjMjSGNcJ6f0t/y4LdhaFRdeWK53dBF+SmLjyiETq0pJi2\nBgpjBpObK2v3r19JH1okCiqHl5eiTQEX/P9ZQqKxN31wQ0aVDHfACBVvhN0ED4xc\nBv3f5o+j77CAPt5iyx/dE/rNcOuspJUIvhWZgJXkxQiPO60syvNEJbV9k85eTt9T\nWNabGKExK3r2tSKExVlhjGsaWSzW2LRIgXKrnHoEGFdyPsDHmzJZvhjyRpH3hvvj\n2SiuXjk2EwmgJMMZ9X95U7DIFDssWdZ+ZjQrgrykXOyk6bFsDboBBKVXs1+3PgUp\nz0PIAs1ChlsmmDAVm4CgJa66gETSBz4dTbcYK79IPsrxOnJF1xiMzn+cQ48Y0sU9\nCANKmTOxYk0M7tA9hUAGmdTtRADUDgisYQtqZ4p8DCKj1isLiJBcb2BF+1tAY39u\n/QK3iFVfjRFAnPV3Rbr9v6VmVIbBSadojfui+wXbH0sTXdT69ClSJ0OQx+GxGH+F\nmJynkt9FdPH/RIwy72S0hOM8N6q/53IZTXfMcpV4ht/OeIc3TRsukGJjBKRP2zeQ\nJshY39qzneR8qJCHN3Y42JVCig9ldP5rsGh9AOdCSG/bV4v6ByrzhIzrfoebMLrx\nVUuzgniBmQZyoZHwBZ7U\n=pCZT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 12f6354b696f3ab577ef6d33c2798d70ec039c20\nparent 487b25f885c74b43ad2df837c6c0f6c45626be2a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784314626 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784314626 -0400\n\nfix(code): drop `uv install` tip from `/version` update hint (#4822)\n\nThe `/version` command's update-available line hard-coded `uv tool\ninstall -U deepagents-code`, which is stale guidance now that dcode\nauto-updates on relaunch and offers `/update` and `dcode update`. It now\npoints at the relaunch/auto-update path when auto-update is enabled, and\nat `/update` or `dcode update` otherwise.\n\n---\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a8b54b7c-cc2f-e6cc-a034-61a8578b8a04)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:57:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4e618f07b4b00f94133b4d1c105011c438cb35be","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4e618f07b4b00f94133b4d1c105011c438cb35be","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4e618f07b4b00f94133b4d1c105011c438cb35be/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"487b25f885c74b43ad2df837c6c0f6c45626be2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/487b25f885c74b43ad2df837c6c0f6c45626be2a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/487b25f885c74b43ad2df837c6c0f6c45626be2a"}]},{"sha":"487b25f885c74b43ad2df837c6c0f6c45626be2a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ4N2IyNWY4ODVjNzRiNDNhZDJkZjgzN2M2YzBmNmM0NTYyNmJlMmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:49:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:49:28Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep goal criteria proposal when marker clear fails (#4785)\n\nFixed `/goal` criteria being discarded when clearing the completed\ncriteria request from the thread failed.\n\n---\n\nFollow-up to #4784. When a YOLO `/goal` criteria run succeeds, cleanup\nclears the `goal_criteria_request` marker before syncing but ignored a\nfailed clear (checkpoint write failure). A stale marker still naming the\njust-completed request then made the sync\n(`_sync_goal_rubric_state_from_thread`) and restore\n(`_restore_goal_rubric_state`) paths strip the freshly generated\n`_pending_goal_*` payload, so no review/YOLO acceptance mounted and the\ncriteria were silently lost. The marker now supersedes a proposal only\nwhen it names a *different* request than the pending proposal's request\nid.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6f2018c7-ffa3-ac12-4dab-8eed1142e4c4)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"57f0a61b64413dfed606d5b83d5cc9b4ddaa069f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/57f0a61b64413dfed606d5b83d5cc9b4ddaa069f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/487b25f885c74b43ad2df837c6c0f6c45626be2a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnk4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdzwQAK+yeBUJ/vpQRHr6+pmwsL5F\n6tymN6xTsxDgZyj/Hh4xWuO87cQp2dR/l7qUl6JUhdPgy9rNnKBktezZoGNUuaYB\nqe/OQ18j2CQclj51pbg/KcCr1E2p2p4Pf4FfhaMis5IL71J04R1COU7IHq6kKxkv\nVM4k24a3QvOoSRKOk0o9eWaP9N3KwLLVjgOnC7WPVEowiiwvLB89RD4JZewAqa+M\n7rl0YK7ukFSstpicaroi9S9NdsfDrN5hXG4R8V2xv89n77clT+hCdc6ZFsY0v+3b\nWa/6Vf6TBAyvrZFN9Z4wH+cs8b8yMm0dZrHKsUx5d8bJhnaEinPIuo1KAaSIAVbK\nHIv/E7glGlZnt5emvHEHT2DLFBJc1reUD/1zQ6D/iKrs5exi739gy80sctu9AjAn\nFjU6mCKiGBPdJyxXwAnfzzIVhGeyA+fYiaP8yQn5/uycoX6Qgo+nlTPTmkZtoNWM\nCr1pW21q9UpVVwDbg6Sl5gmVySV6eKWn6TUUywBN5wqSSpIzMMAyC3E+SuoUZ9Hf\ndMM8zno8VhuRdLkVsI1DS4t1ExfyvRUaQDg7WzeuwrYVHRmzbEcpJOnw0+1Zw3P0\nIDWC8dhjtT69Q3OF+wQnfNtpX5hVHCcfutx/IFv6/U3bHBQeYEMJW7oAesGJRnYl\nE7tRvT4oHq8k2RSK+slX\n=Cl5b\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 57f0a61b64413dfed606d5b83d5cc9b4ddaa069f\nparent c2c27d621b63d5af18870e034f99355dc410cbda\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784314168 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784314168 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep goal criteria proposal when marker clear fails (#4785)\n\nFixed `/goal` criteria being discarded when clearing the completed\ncriteria request from the thread failed.\n\n---\n\nFollow-up to #4784. When a YOLO `/goal` criteria run succeeds, cleanup\nclears the `goal_criteria_request` marker before syncing but ignored a\nfailed clear (checkpoint write failure). A stale marker still naming the\njust-completed request then made the sync\n(`_sync_goal_rubric_state_from_thread`) and restore\n(`_restore_goal_rubric_state`) paths strip the freshly generated\n`_pending_goal_*` payload, so no review/YOLO acceptance mounted and the\ncriteria were silently lost. The marker now supersedes a proposal only\nwhen it names a *different* request than the pending proposal's request\nid.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6f2018c7-ffa3-ac12-4dab-8eed1142e4c4)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:49:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/487b25f885c74b43ad2df837c6c0f6c45626be2a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/487b25f885c74b43ad2df837c6c0f6c45626be2a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/487b25f885c74b43ad2df837c6c0f6c45626be2a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c2c27d621b63d5af18870e034f99355dc410cbda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c2c27d621b63d5af18870e034f99355dc410cbda","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c2c27d621b63d5af18870e034f99355dc410cbda"}]},{"sha":"c2c27d621b63d5af18870e034f99355dc410cbda","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGMyYzI3ZDYyMWI2M2Q1YWYxODg3MGUwMzRmOTkzNTVkYzQxMGNiZGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:49:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:49:01Z"},"message":"fix(code): quiet MCP auth-skip debug logging for known patterns (#4805)\n\nReduce noisy full-traceback DEBUG logs when an MCP server is skipped\nbecause it requires authentication; the actionable warning and a concise\ndebug line remain.\n\n---\n\nWhen an MCP server is skipped during discovery because it needs\nauthentication — either a token-refresh (`reauth`) failure or an RFC\n9728 `401` OAuth challenge — `deepagents-code` logged the entire anyio\n`ExceptionGroup` / httpx traceback at DEBUG via `exc_info`, on top of\nthe actionable WARNING. For these already-classified, expected outcomes\nthe traceback adds no diagnostic value and just floods debug output.\n\nThese two recognized branches now emit a concise single-line DEBUG\nbreadcrumb (the exception class name only). The full traceback is still\nlogged for genuinely unknown discovery errors (the `else` branch) and\nfor classifier failures, so real anomalies stay debuggable. The\nuser-facing WARNING is unchanged apart from dropping the now-inaccurate\n\"the original error is in debug logs\" note from the reauth message.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a5ab799b-1747-0d65-16b6-ee0ccccee0c4)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c1bae5f94c8aa8d10c945bcb7e86be288a407ea4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c1bae5f94c8aa8d10c945bcb7e86be288a407ea4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c2c27d621b63d5af18870e034f99355dc410cbda","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnkdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC8oQAKxr1fyq3Hiza1CqnetkNweS\n+OA5KZbY//1q2izMQ3zehM8jjOkj33TwQMmC73ZWH9yybc+HDSBa3njS96AgcYz6\net7u1DrTy+06quK6zejSV/XWC2F4I/650R5KzBnsqt8D8ijC1PSuurXdFhxTpMq0\naGTHN36UZXj+BtLpgzd9BZ5SpfowmgrH5wOjfxwyC6g3QHDuhEpdKf4pxzkNYWIK\ndEpJ8Mk7Xhc2+boPQ4TLy8QmQOMXTCRsWBUPcn6QLeFcPev5iqzOij1EweSym2xw\nvabr2NvDOf1BP7rVY0t22TJuZXNhdHl4FTxAEKEE02B0fghI0nGf/OiH2eGRMUXY\nBVJbAhVK8gjYtRmGywoa3P549m7xIrJ/zf9L34L1bj9uoEakOsGepWN1yT9KLi3j\nTUtFfBE2/t9xYjwhlwFurCgKwGtYf8UjlMYSa4Jug/apC4LfZzAQagh2qrR6oAzc\nBB71bQR2uO6mfDxwHKAXXxoJnjUCF9yShrqq7MZ/vfrELIffP9R/O3tCyqd5k2/8\nXWXJzo/yOSQMSAOIBeMBgDdWE7AesFKTJsBjsXsxNHosUMUd377w5KwrP6D59aUg\nee4ULYY8D9ACW5KBBJ8GQ5sXAeabBLv6EKtKfDOaVGHPmUdfyt5ZQE3mXlOdQUVf\nbMIm02O8oAByez+NiPXO\n=GQ4+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c1bae5f94c8aa8d10c945bcb7e86be288a407ea4\nparent 2ddb551bd77d210d689f3a75037259ade4fbf54a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784314141 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784314141 -0400\n\nfix(code): quiet MCP auth-skip debug logging for known patterns (#4805)\n\nReduce noisy full-traceback DEBUG logs when an MCP server is skipped\nbecause it requires authentication; the actionable warning and a concise\ndebug line remain.\n\n---\n\nWhen an MCP server is skipped during discovery because it needs\nauthentication — either a token-refresh (`reauth`) failure or an RFC\n9728 `401` OAuth challenge — `deepagents-code` logged the entire anyio\n`ExceptionGroup` / httpx traceback at DEBUG via `exc_info`, on top of\nthe actionable WARNING. For these already-classified, expected outcomes\nthe traceback adds no diagnostic value and just floods debug output.\n\nThese two recognized branches now emit a concise single-line DEBUG\nbreadcrumb (the exception class name only). The full traceback is still\nlogged for genuinely unknown discovery errors (the `else` branch) and\nfor classifier failures, so real anomalies stay debuggable. The\nuser-facing WARNING is unchanged apart from dropping the now-inaccurate\n\"the original error is in debug logs\" note from the reauth message.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a5ab799b-1747-0d65-16b6-ee0ccccee0c4)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:49:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c2c27d621b63d5af18870e034f99355dc410cbda","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c2c27d621b63d5af18870e034f99355dc410cbda","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c2c27d621b63d5af18870e034f99355dc410cbda/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2ddb551bd77d210d689f3a75037259ade4fbf54a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2ddb551bd77d210d689f3a75037259ade4fbf54a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2ddb551bd77d210d689f3a75037259ade4fbf54a"}]},{"sha":"2ddb551bd77d210d689f3a75037259ade4fbf54a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJkZGI1NTFiZDc3ZDIxMGQ2ODlmM2E3NTAzNzI1OWFkZTRmYmY1NGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:48:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:48:01Z"},"message":"feat(code): expand truncated `task` descriptions on click or `Ctrl+O` (#4811)\n\nA long `task` tool description is rendered on a dim line truncated at\n120 characters, but the full text was previously unreachable. This makes\nthe truncated preview expandable: clicking the description region or\npressing Ctrl+O toggles between the truncated and full description,\nmirroring the collapsible command/code affordance on `execute`/`js_eval`\nrows.\n\n---\n\nThe `task` description now owns Ctrl+O when it is truncated (like an\nexpandable command/code block), while any expandable tool output stays\nreachable by clicking its own region. A \"click or Ctrl+O to\nexpand/collapse\" hint is shown beside a truncated description.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Added `TestToolCallMessageTaskDescription` covering expandability\ndetection, the toggle swap, and click routing.\n- Added an app-level Ctrl+O routing test that prefers a truncated `task`\ndescription over expandable output.\n- Updated existing Ctrl+O routing tests to account for the new\nhigher-priority branch.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f5d64d3e-e6e2-d1cf-f52c-0ecbd8829ef4)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"84a5cd88ad1a5533d6401507573b1df22b302efe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/84a5cd88ad1a5533d6401507573b1df22b302efe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2ddb551bd77d210d689f3a75037259ade4fbf54a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnjhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOEMQAKKHZR4J71P1mupLLvjnxUP/\nBJc4mH0TM0hF1JJbKo2XizI4HtE3JP6nIP5V5B7iFa2kxJ6ex2Wy5i2DC2JsqsrJ\nyVNI8fXB402D7nxv+u8AgimBXmQ/q1klAYupisRSjexPg9j4ui6I3a44Py9uKVMy\nLxadRQjvksVoyoPGNJRmaBEPjjm9PSQXhwEY+dtOh9ZPmqas490Cqt1Two5HVba8\nPe9bDL0KC96QXEPhK/O7htmtJVAL4sk72BvOExMV+fOP244czcnkleBeAN/nUzVB\n2KJ+2Yx9IfMqNpotoVVgsHE6HZ1ZxwSm1SvsKRyjvcXs9t7a66yI5aELvyvV93/D\nple+uAg9Bi1drU8pWAlxaTNSTsPV1YcaQfq38Xuwos/NzwTyuipwL+vYx63ibm8a\njliqlQD9eDhMa+kMF3I9ItPHYlrL9OAsoUycwLlOzMI9aXS4cbzFL+uXwfL4wVjI\nh1hRTEZ/6Jr905Ds0+goMMbQL0ToJxCnpNtG25VdwH/KG9iwUvxzfSOWfZhJuy8/\nG4iJUBepxiX35YTgJiT6kQprTNfCDFthOymYeRvMVGuO8N2Cl0o5aQQFJBErf4oL\naEmB4jBqcMvhcJ1qYMFLow7E4twf6qB6OZDUtb7zqnY7NunCN7adCaiJT2cBPJpa\np8JrgP6YzuXaxftHsFM/\n=2qiZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 84a5cd88ad1a5533d6401507573b1df22b302efe\nparent bd07d9628db4a7171d603674dde4e1c484622ee9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784314081 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784314081 -0400\n\nfeat(code): expand truncated `task` descriptions on click or `Ctrl+O` (#4811)\n\nA long `task` tool description is rendered on a dim line truncated at\n120 characters, but the full text was previously unreachable. This makes\nthe truncated preview expandable: clicking the description region or\npressing Ctrl+O toggles between the truncated and full description,\nmirroring the collapsible command/code affordance on `execute`/`js_eval`\nrows.\n\n---\n\nThe `task` description now owns Ctrl+O when it is truncated (like an\nexpandable command/code block), while any expandable tool output stays\nreachable by clicking its own region. A \"click or Ctrl+O to\nexpand/collapse\" hint is shown beside a truncated description.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Added `TestToolCallMessageTaskDescription` covering expandability\ndetection, the toggle swap, and click routing.\n- Added an app-level Ctrl+O routing test that prefers a truncated `task`\ndescription over expandable output.\n- Updated existing Ctrl+O routing tests to account for the new\nhigher-priority branch.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f5d64d3e-e6e2-d1cf-f52c-0ecbd8829ef4)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:48:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2ddb551bd77d210d689f3a75037259ade4fbf54a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2ddb551bd77d210d689f3a75037259ade4fbf54a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2ddb551bd77d210d689f3a75037259ade4fbf54a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bd07d9628db4a7171d603674dde4e1c484622ee9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bd07d9628db4a7171d603674dde4e1c484622ee9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bd07d9628db4a7171d603674dde4e1c484622ee9"}]},{"sha":"bd07d9628db4a7171d603674dde4e1c484622ee9","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJkMDdkOTYyOGRiNGE3MTcxZDYwMzY3NGRkZTRlMWM0ODQ2MjJlZTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:47:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:47:22Z"},"message":"ci(infra): link release runs from merged release PRs (#4817)\n\nAfter a release PR merges and dispatches `release.yml`, the merged PR\nnow gets a comment linking directly to the package release workflow run.\n\n---\n\n`workflow_dispatch` does not return the new run's ID, while the\n`trigger-releases` job already resolves it for the job summary. This\nreuses that resolved URL and the existing merge-commit-to-PR lookup.\nComment failures remain warnings and cannot turn a successful release\ndispatch into a failed job.","tree":{"sha":"b27c03dd4c4ee6b880894aacde087957ce1510a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b27c03dd4c4ee6b880894aacde087957ce1510a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/bd07d9628db4a7171d603674dde4e1c484622ee9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWni6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAevIQALESetMwbBljuIDB1vBfI01V\nCFy6ovFw3YCmyzmSGH3yM05I3Z+LcdJGzTofcMldQfgq8JPRop34iNw/CzzzFHQQ\nySwOWs71mCAAg7x9Qrf2iTMe/iFYGYTUg9XtbBIns7abWWl6uw3Z7MbHpLVlbpYu\nWl3JCRiHSBjoK9m0DZjYHxF2bxIqGbPxuExFgWJh0WAQaJ//Rc13qTuzVkCLvEvM\ne+ZinhHxs9sEBZGD5VOiNQy3HWsZ/tonmUNqOhMnLyXFhziS3m+ft8N9jrRmOxR2\neG0uHE3JuTXV3d8K+r+GrxJb0PMNMbEwWdosw2ixyd0jpNFkNpeBvulDWzHxoVu3\n0SmAFRa9exV24CTFdLDxWUHFBV84Q24jfostxvFVpYtzknMcLf0b8Da11OZQ7FwB\nPoERTkd57Cq8x9d/pDzmjns/3uaEeCGS4ORcHSu44XcYaP2h8razslT1lWYsfBnS\n43l3PaM9bL5qrsuCCJSEQtLY7RNNFMVcBNXXWldqMZSdXh9fGSU7dufdvXyp3Fl/\nVMdZTwuxJyvvHDQggIM7ZCYPNFMUOACKI1UR5jdIIRX9G0tIue87rqrwXoPIj3fZ\n2xNuAFFbUrch/pX34m/xRvvEdUajoyX4U73S+sOn+WMmvBX3GziWTwXdquvos00U\nejH/n8FHkH6H9Nh+2qjK\n=zkk3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b27c03dd4c4ee6b880894aacde087957ce1510a2\nparent f5c32592461a990143445067e22083adea7c1107\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784314042 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784314042 -0400\n\nci(infra): link release runs from merged release PRs (#4817)\n\nAfter a release PR merges and dispatches `release.yml`, the merged PR\nnow gets a comment linking directly to the package release workflow run.\n\n---\n\n`workflow_dispatch` does not return the new run's ID, while the\n`trigger-releases` job already resolves it for the job summary. This\nreuses that resolved URL and the existing merge-commit-to-PR lookup.\nComment failures remain warnings and cannot turn a successful release\ndispatch into a failed job.","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:47:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bd07d9628db4a7171d603674dde4e1c484622ee9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bd07d9628db4a7171d603674dde4e1c484622ee9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bd07d9628db4a7171d603674dde4e1c484622ee9/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f5c32592461a990143445067e22083adea7c1107","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f5c32592461a990143445067e22083adea7c1107","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f5c32592461a990143445067e22083adea7c1107"}]},{"sha":"f5c32592461a990143445067e22083adea7c1107","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY1YzMyNTkyNDYxYTk5MDE0MzQ0NTA2N2UyMjA4M2FkZWE3YzExMDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:47:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:47:00Z"},"message":"style(code): show enabled plugin status in green (#4821)\n\nIn the installed plugin details view, the `Status: ✓ Enabled` line was\nrendered `dim` like every other status line. This styles it with the\n`$success` theme color so a successful load reads as green, matching the\nsemantic coloring used elsewhere in the TUI. Other status lines\n(error/disabled/pending, and the secondary MCP restart note) stay `dim`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d3174852-cfc9-43f5-f431-56993468deaf)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5b4fd3711f248a77a25417c81474fbb64eb43ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a5b4fd3711f248a77a25417c81474fbb64eb43ff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f5c32592461a990143445067e22083adea7c1107","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnikCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAV24QACeBOm+C3MiwJ39B9nBsdpUq\ng29eG4f0S3fTypTNrZfTdiwE2Lp5epJkZiR2zdFfCow4mgv0fm7gGwCrr6aCYzuc\njp3kj3ajqmEJnvAFTTSnBVq/FsY+PtSaX1xRvfKAKNQUpb+khu5r7EhqQVflwPmg\nEAPH6FLp55mflFSn1JbToIv83Z9Ne4OuU/8vgEo08kISIC38o4sD08Fy6TCmdcuV\nnaqdBRoAVnBDrBdsIx/uYQssu2Z7P/vHeuy4r7ZsF0xMU4YMzJapgMudkQ48AiUT\ngjdHApQnViD3lTNMdEDbfITdsjjMYrmCk6Vm3a7LDDds8eaUifI0NCSVu/HsD5DV\ngYbfZ/1KBtjlbseqcJAAPARXRQ6wF59QyyosmhjaZEc5XSdmyTtS9ykRF4Oc4oHc\nMvEM4Sp3jmLvGTkU+8uKAoZTVdb+xkDP9HTuwC79jalKV7ToeSuxXs2nHVFtKwkU\nc2IECWBkf3P6T4sylCp7dP0fzmHSLwbyzyBvkeOZqWxa1DlYPW7ib/+H+VcoF7Z/\nUaGpkaEuuxiKQsRBAXl1oOCk0zmvklWYMxAA8Rr7jDjX6paTQPQzbiZUq8ZXkklW\n5AhtYuTZhapY11lE76R5Z8jzvrXqZrBinmqVTdRzrXHIMMAaYbzxHqKNckTNZ9k5\nvCHP3iKfxpNIWs+/a9Wt\n=B712\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a5b4fd3711f248a77a25417c81474fbb64eb43ff\nparent f328753ea2daf2eaad5498abbf0a990d4edea01d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784314020 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784314020 -0400\n\nstyle(code): show enabled plugin status in green (#4821)\n\nIn the installed plugin details view, the `Status: ✓ Enabled` line was\nrendered `dim` like every other status line. This styles it with the\n`$success` theme color so a successful load reads as green, matching the\nsemantic coloring used elsewhere in the TUI. Other status lines\n(error/disabled/pending, and the secondary MCP restart note) stay `dim`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d3174852-cfc9-43f5-f431-56993468deaf)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:47:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f5c32592461a990143445067e22083adea7c1107","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f5c32592461a990143445067e22083adea7c1107","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f5c32592461a990143445067e22083adea7c1107/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f328753ea2daf2eaad5498abbf0a990d4edea01d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f328753ea2daf2eaad5498abbf0a990d4edea01d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f328753ea2daf2eaad5498abbf0a990d4edea01d"}]},{"sha":"f328753ea2daf2eaad5498abbf0a990d4edea01d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGYzMjg3NTNlYTJkYWYyZWFhZDU0OThhYmJmMGE5OTBkNGVkZWEwMWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:45:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:45:55Z"},"message":"ci(infra): flag stale dependency minimums on release PRs (#4823)\n\nRelease PRs currently verify that dependencies resolve against PyPI, but\nthey do not show when a declared minimum has fallen behind the newest\npublished version. That makes dependency reconciliation easy to miss at\nthe point maintainers are preparing a release.\n\nThis adds an advisory release-PR check for the changed package\nmanifests. It compares required and optional dependency minimums with\nPyPI, reports whether the newest version still fits the current ceiling,\nand maintains one non-blocking PR comment. The existing `release-deps:\nacknowledged` label records that maintainers reviewed the result without\nrequiring a metadata change.\n\nStable releases are compared by default. Pre-releases participate only\nwhen the declared minimum is itself a pre-release, while an environment\nsetting keeps that policy explicit and adjustable. Local path and\nworkspace sources are excluded, so sibling development installs do not\ncreate noise while external LangChain dependencies remain covered.\n\nPyPI requests use bounded concurrency, timeouts, and retries. Query\nfailures remain advisory and preserve any previous finding rather than\nincorrectly declaring the dependency set current. Unit coverage\nexercises requirement parsing, release selection, upper bounds, source\nexclusions, retries, output formatting, and canonical-name request\ndeduplication.","tree":{"sha":"1117ce769d1af5e1c7cde0217c1aa7bf25ad9668","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1117ce769d1af5e1c7cde0217c1aa7bf25ad9668"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f328753ea2daf2eaad5498abbf0a990d4edea01d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnhjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9UcQAEvXR8u6Kvcjhmlpq6WwLW4X\n0Bdz7DFin6Bm7iYcDlrwxCOy81F8xtznbPEPL6wI/tkSS0WZti3yIC8X9YykMekN\nPXZbp6pvS+sdKMZO8X3Rqzglh9F0gT2KCzK42eLMo0+SpR/8/EIitFQJFHoOg2zO\nNwgvbDOmwzyg7ZD0U+NKPjIq1j52lkPKlZ6hk7N5iNVUkcA7p6OpLUQDhp4Ia9Gb\n+6rWUmK2huV6ZmF/iH+qRl4xVoWCFmCq7e8+5ItbDZuEF8KHtYMeyqrOdflpgE6Y\nouFJl3zkLhwqfpK9th/cChaPpkk8e2uHv4gITpSg/rIDbhjg1tIXcSnCLfHWbUWr\nL9gszIR4e51jAyFB5TPoKjkfFtySazk0FHwP+JtPTNGjjQN7SAGw86ZxXYjgso0L\nVsmbyPzb1ApsPp3LIpTWi4aKHfx3yIsbzw19dYuK9YYDeCMfWpgRa0JlwTjL707a\naW0fej9YwuH+iW0N1qL9HU9MQI0sXYZHAPu8F6MW4BiIq2Zm3sOWznaI0aXn+tdu\nKi6kio77HAXL7c0XBse9Z4DAEyhjAhZGzVPQKDnlwACnoy7JbMrvDrM2s8miMUNg\nSk1adLxHhndtSMMj1EfPY34Xiuq/Ox6SisaqKtiqvensxJW+9g2qAFtvMNlMrF+s\n+HlNjHfj9LqWd3YhxA07\n=7x2B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1117ce769d1af5e1c7cde0217c1aa7bf25ad9668\nparent ea825386b3c817f8461ea9e92c71de3411991e2a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784313955 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784313955 -0400\n\nci(infra): flag stale dependency minimums on release PRs (#4823)\n\nRelease PRs currently verify that dependencies resolve against PyPI, but\nthey do not show when a declared minimum has fallen behind the newest\npublished version. That makes dependency reconciliation easy to miss at\nthe point maintainers are preparing a release.\n\nThis adds an advisory release-PR check for the changed package\nmanifests. It compares required and optional dependency minimums with\nPyPI, reports whether the newest version still fits the current ceiling,\nand maintains one non-blocking PR comment. The existing `release-deps:\nacknowledged` label records that maintainers reviewed the result without\nrequiring a metadata change.\n\nStable releases are compared by default. Pre-releases participate only\nwhen the declared minimum is itself a pre-release, while an environment\nsetting keeps that policy explicit and adjustable. Local path and\nworkspace sources are excluded, so sibling development installs do not\ncreate noise while external LangChain dependencies remain covered.\n\nPyPI requests use bounded concurrency, timeouts, and retries. Query\nfailures remain advisory and preserve any previous finding rather than\nincorrectly declaring the dependency set current. Unit coverage\nexercises requirement parsing, release selection, upper bounds, source\nexclusions, retries, output formatting, and canonical-name request\ndeduplication.","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:45:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f328753ea2daf2eaad5498abbf0a990d4edea01d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f328753ea2daf2eaad5498abbf0a990d4edea01d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f328753ea2daf2eaad5498abbf0a990d4edea01d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ea825386b3c817f8461ea9e92c71de3411991e2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ea825386b3c817f8461ea9e92c71de3411991e2a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ea825386b3c817f8461ea9e92c71de3411991e2a"}]},{"sha":"ea825386b3c817f8461ea9e92c71de3411991e2a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGVhODI1Mzg2YjNjODE3Zjg0NjFlYTllOTJjNzFkZTM0MTE5OTFlMmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:45:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:45:04Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep paste placeholder when backspacing newline below it (#4757)\n\nFixed the `dcode` chat input deleting a collapsed `[Pasted text #N]` (or\n`[image N]`) placeholder when backspacing the line break on the line\nbelow it; the line break is now removed while the placeholder is\npreserved.\n\n---\n\nIn the `dcode` chat input, pasting large text collapses it into a\n`[Pasted text #N]` placeholder. Pressing Enter to add a newline and then\nbackspacing from the start of that new line deleted the entire\nplaceholder instead of just rejoining the lines.\n\nThe cause is in `_find_placeholder_span`: its backwards-delete branch\ntreats any whitespace immediately after a placeholder as an\nauto-inserted trailing separator and swallows the whole token with it.\nSince `str.isspace()` also matches a newline, backspacing a line break\nbelow a placeholder removed the placeholder. Restricting that branch to\na literal space (the separator actually auto-inserted after media\nplaceholders) lets a newline fall through to the default backspace,\nwhich removes only the line break and leaves the cursor at the end of\nthe placeholder line. The same fix is applied to the shared base text\narea used by the inline prompts.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/79b11ee1-f326-668a-e659-c990811f4e29)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"52ccbd1d51eaae8bbb83e8b8968117d4a8a8e174","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/52ccbd1d51eaae8bbb83e8b8968117d4a8a8e174"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ea825386b3c817f8461ea9e92c71de3411991e2a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWngwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArVkQAAhKhaxo94HQdCYTZsEaAWaX\nc5Kb5vxPonf/pWuquS+5AeFCTtkf32doJGjUe66++/c2gT94vQfxqWmn7V1bDqB5\nxkTIW2HH+zv67r/VCSPOaQC78f62PJ2EAF4rIdXkzCS6FYQ9k4SX4LRrH6bBKeV2\nPv+Br7k5SUK3CqpMgwpfMLDOLf38+bTNOfBR8F9ezxxJar5MBnaHKln5hYKMKS0Y\njuHu00UfA8YhNzlr0no6GXNRQEG/krrEPdX+GTa69+Ip1pLUsQJJouguGDaH9KZP\nfj5gGbJHanqUbx+xcbPxPXj3ZaCK4G4JAYRLHxhRzbgDu/5O6uMbakWali/0CMfY\nGWGqi+ug9aY0Wu0wV6GOosi/cWlqLfVoO+lc6g2ST7LubnN3J4KCCoAX5f3B4IOm\nr9wLQw4ydn8HBWrI7WEqyCsObY76cJRjQpbs379Dwy8PpH5YnmXvtDaU09hmoMr+\nkUGZLcifAHkcrPbWMNdyBzzszHUgS8H8uYhpSrthvtSzJUJGkmJgP6mXnbPqImcm\nRMFionIAzfYmRlH4sdz20p2qRKHysF4qsYuvnLu4f6fcurqVmoTKj2ABVlBUq/OI\nSoiGowXwtrYntph01DdOkQmBiASlWKIJRNGzWyZSinLJTT6EjAvZUPGrEiJSrwvM\nICokXGv7Dc3b4FbqDk85\n=9JMt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 52ccbd1d51eaae8bbb83e8b8968117d4a8a8e174\nparent be8e5214a06225acce6c0363eb14ed4c14db2f59\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784313904 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784313904 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep paste placeholder when backspacing newline below it (#4757)\n\nFixed the `dcode` chat input deleting a collapsed `[Pasted text #N]` (or\n`[image N]`) placeholder when backspacing the line break on the line\nbelow it; the line break is now removed while the placeholder is\npreserved.\n\n---\n\nIn the `dcode` chat input, pasting large text collapses it into a\n`[Pasted text #N]` placeholder. Pressing Enter to add a newline and then\nbackspacing from the start of that new line deleted the entire\nplaceholder instead of just rejoining the lines.\n\nThe cause is in `_find_placeholder_span`: its backwards-delete branch\ntreats any whitespace immediately after a placeholder as an\nauto-inserted trailing separator and swallows the whole token with it.\nSince `str.isspace()` also matches a newline, backspacing a line break\nbelow a placeholder removed the placeholder. Restricting that branch to\na literal space (the separator actually auto-inserted after media\nplaceholders) lets a newline fall through to the default backspace,\nwhich removes only the line break and leaves the cursor at the end of\nthe placeholder line. The same fix is applied to the shared base text\narea used by the inline prompts.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/79b11ee1-f326-668a-e659-c990811f4e29)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:45:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ea825386b3c817f8461ea9e92c71de3411991e2a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ea825386b3c817f8461ea9e92c71de3411991e2a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ea825386b3c817f8461ea9e92c71de3411991e2a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"be8e5214a06225acce6c0363eb14ed4c14db2f59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/be8e5214a06225acce6c0363eb14ed4c14db2f59","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/be8e5214a06225acce6c0363eb14ed4c14db2f59"}]},{"sha":"be8e5214a06225acce6c0363eb14ed4c14db2f59","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJlOGU1MjE0YTA2MjI1YWNjZTZjMDM2M2ViMTRlZDRjMTRkYjJmNTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:44:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:44:39Z"},"message":"style(code): drop hardcoded indent from `ls` and `write_todos` output (#4762)\n\n`ls` and `write_todos` results in the `deepagents-code` TUI now align\nflush under the output-gutter glyph, matching other tools, instead of\nbeing indented an extra four spaces.\n\n---\n\nThe `ls` and `write_todos` renderers in the terminal UI prefixed every\nrow with four hardcoded spaces, so their entries rendered at a 4-space\nhanging indent under the `⎿` output-gutter glyph. Every other tool\nformatter (`grep`, `glob`, `read_file`, `execute`) sits flush after that\ngutter, and the gutter layout already owns alignment for soft-wrapped\nlines — so the extra pad just produced an inconsistent gap between the\nglyph and the first item. This emits bare rows for both formatters and\nalso drops the matching indent from the todo stats header and\nempty-state, so the whole block stays flush and consistent. The todo\ncontinuation-line hang-indent auto-adjusts since it derives from the\nstatus-label width.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/c5dec078-214f-79a6-2417-4b0014e0944e)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"61927776d2324eff4377b682b94735c5b17862fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/61927776d2324eff4377b682b94735c5b17862fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/be8e5214a06225acce6c0363eb14ed4c14db2f59","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWngXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbw0QAFhO6RMYEd7PNEPxzyi+XQJv\nPT77SJ0L0hkS6w9MVj/117iRFkgcCQwhoEsegbSj3OHTef9GHLDxvndYvZlmX7ha\ntRaxfRB/6NE5qIIccfVs4cuTXkl29qt0b3ve6e5J6kuui06L9uWTo2rieJ7/e7h+\nRiplcBKK8Phe5whgGm0Sk6GJIqF1BFTo+ghFrNevKXbsLAjOQ62YYIqlnlBQpYyl\n6am1SmS8aZpozsApofXLZ1A3fmtN0OO3bWXLHSNuFOae2mNmhITTJSRAc2IiqEro\n3G/IgK3j5TbAIci2FakccpNM0ySkf7epwO4QAgGb1IhCZQvIT7mosdbQyyc1ak4P\n93aGh9mQUR4eD6JAQkN2Wno0SbyKVbAzxm1j5+YDxRWL5cGru/IaKVOIfhLuwY5L\nhTieKsCoPuVwIi953tEDVF8Hnq5YL9gpGgvivbBt8OYHwSWmqv5l7qESLUz0WBHv\nKerhCA1jCnvluNkFCWjgqboTXhXW/Et707Weig/sv3As20VX3JT1K2j4xg7Scq75\nAJg/XlisABGegSWx14ag4i3Lgs/ac/w2s3NE+ogqwtW8NPejbDTokGLzCbeA79MH\nY9WyWq7PY51qixSEAtQcMf162pRDuFlFFpJdCMsTgx/SB6AMleWOiU494TqJFL27\no9ZHHoJl/XHoqu0AVwLW\n=Jt7I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 61927776d2324eff4377b682b94735c5b17862fb\nparent 77603c69e2eeededf6f1df68b384da27f7d2843f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784313879 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784313879 -0400\n\nstyle(code): drop hardcoded indent from `ls` and `write_todos` output (#4762)\n\n`ls` and `write_todos` results in the `deepagents-code` TUI now align\nflush under the output-gutter glyph, matching other tools, instead of\nbeing indented an extra four spaces.\n\n---\n\nThe `ls` and `write_todos` renderers in the terminal UI prefixed every\nrow with four hardcoded spaces, so their entries rendered at a 4-space\nhanging indent under the `⎿` output-gutter glyph. Every other tool\nformatter (`grep`, `glob`, `read_file`, `execute`) sits flush after that\ngutter, and the gutter layout already owns alignment for soft-wrapped\nlines — so the extra pad just produced an inconsistent gap between the\nglyph and the first item. This emits bare rows for both formatters and\nalso drops the matching indent from the todo stats header and\nempty-state, so the whole block stays flush and consistent. The todo\ncontinuation-line hang-indent auto-adjusts since it derives from the\nstatus-label width.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/c5dec078-214f-79a6-2417-4b0014e0944e)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:44:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/be8e5214a06225acce6c0363eb14ed4c14db2f59","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/be8e5214a06225acce6c0363eb14ed4c14db2f59","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/be8e5214a06225acce6c0363eb14ed4c14db2f59/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"77603c69e2eeededf6f1df68b384da27f7d2843f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/77603c69e2eeededf6f1df68b384da27f7d2843f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/77603c69e2eeededf6f1df68b384da27f7d2843f"}]},{"sha":"77603c69e2eeededf6f1df68b384da27f7d2843f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc3NjAzYzY5ZTJlZWVkZWRmNmYxZGY2OGIzODRkYTI3ZjdkMjg0M2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:43:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:43:17Z"},"message":"feat(code): debug-log skill-name override collisions (#4772)\n\nDeep Agents Code now emits a `DEBUG` log when a higher-precedence skill\noverrides another skill with the same name, aiding skill-resolution\ndebugging.\n\n---\n\nSkill sources (built-in, plugin, global, project) are merged by\nprecedence and a higher-precedence skill silently replaces a\nlower-precedence one with the same name. This override is intentional\nand unchanged; this PR makes it diagnosable by routing both\nskill-discovery merge points — the CLI `skills list` loader\n(`skills/load.py`) and the runtime `PluginSkillsMiddleware` — through a\nshared `merge_skill` helper that emits a `DEBUG` log on each effective\nreplacement, recording the skill name plus the previous and replacement\nsource paths and labels.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/5f97f80c-bed1-0fa5-d0b1-ce67060df37c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4c88f8b35c683e3341fe7ee825863e16824a30e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4c88f8b35c683e3341fe7ee825863e16824a30e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/77603c69e2eeededf6f1df68b384da27f7d2843f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnfFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvS0QABsdcAGYvCiSlf4o/eVsNKdd\nxfxSCHJHgtVEhJzAShRZJTldPfS8yQSXZ/3h6xdIP7FmA0ZPAasZPGoZiHDuJV40\nB02NyeclA+VPOj9B7Clj3MOnkahN+a+1E7Jzo5eR8E2QtUIx5HxKFiUD4oZGChK6\nCDlnC6ChChfJh6QOVpcbLnQxHyxrH3vc/rwcxAKhy23rR5zF/4TBkbmqBPpYXcgj\nP6qZjTJui15t8v5o42rTJ2s2lCJSLReZ7hpTgKFvL9tV5HtMFZ7d5JQ2iEUEbirF\ntg7MIbc1mZjNVBkTfE0wdVbuOUKdcYKcO0hm7LT3kOfffwEkTBexSkIumr4f/JIF\nnriCF/eXr+vferNSYa1ukf8lasVE2UzO9pTKj52BlfqrbC6NgLwEiwLXQisq3kfU\nFLciq7LBAfekYgNGSMr3PhdzIBqSvHQFDA7p+p9oEZ8cwmqO1qLeIRVUbkvA5C/f\n562dieXm7y/6u0dRUsAtk7ar/CczGtEgksn/AJ6Sv6HII63Qvkv6WEN2w5gHbkLD\nXD5NgTkFSVx+GrtfYnpYwHD1UMJefdzEW2hGZoO6iiHrGyI/B3/xjO6tIiiam56S\nVSpiFGxD5dtImxFVNtSYfer4O26x6sCFmhx2DxDXvOk3lfxeRF82wZRtLA3lmtF5\n16+6WjcQzmU1Ra62FFcg\n=FOK8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4c88f8b35c683e3341fe7ee825863e16824a30e2\nparent 45baf6c7a47e08e656ba56eb76beea30a9956403\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784313797 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784313797 -0400\n\nfeat(code): debug-log skill-name override collisions (#4772)\n\nDeep Agents Code now emits a `DEBUG` log when a higher-precedence skill\noverrides another skill with the same name, aiding skill-resolution\ndebugging.\n\n---\n\nSkill sources (built-in, plugin, global, project) are merged by\nprecedence and a higher-precedence skill silently replaces a\nlower-precedence one with the same name. This override is intentional\nand unchanged; this PR makes it diagnosable by routing both\nskill-discovery merge points — the CLI `skills list` loader\n(`skills/load.py`) and the runtime `PluginSkillsMiddleware` — through a\nshared `merge_skill` helper that emits a `DEBUG` log on each effective\nreplacement, recording the skill name plus the previous and replacement\nsource paths and labels.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/5f97f80c-bed1-0fa5-d0b1-ce67060df37c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:43:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/77603c69e2eeededf6f1df68b384da27f7d2843f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/77603c69e2eeededf6f1df68b384da27f7d2843f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/77603c69e2eeededf6f1df68b384da27f7d2843f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"45baf6c7a47e08e656ba56eb76beea30a9956403","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/45baf6c7a47e08e656ba56eb76beea30a9956403","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/45baf6c7a47e08e656ba56eb76beea30a9956403"}]},{"sha":"45baf6c7a47e08e656ba56eb76beea30a9956403","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ1YmFmNmM3YTQ3ZTA4ZTY1NmJhNTZlYjc2YmVlYTMwYTk5NTY0MDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:39:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:39:44Z"},"message":"fix(code): probe unreachable Ollama daemon once per reload (#4806)\n\nWhen an Ollama daemon is down, discovery no longer probes it twice or\nemits duplicate, out-of-order debug logs at startup — it probes and logs\n\"not detected\" once per reload.\n\n---\n\nOllama discovery runs from two startup callers — `get_available_models`\nand `get_model_profiles` — that both call\n`_get_ollama_installed_models`. Empty results were never cached, so an\nunreachable daemon was probed twice per reload and logged `Ollama daemon\nnot detected ...` twice. Because the second `not detected` (from\n`get_model_profiles`) landed right after the first pass's `discovery\nreturned no models` line, the two appeared out of order even though each\nindividual pass logs in the correct order.\n\nThis tracks endpoints that fail the TCP presence preflight in\n`_ollama_unreachable_endpoints` and negatively-caches their empty\nresult, so the probe and log happen once. A *reachable* daemon that\nsimply reports no models is still left uncached, preserving recovery of\na later `ollama pull` without `/reload` (covered by the existing\n`test_empty_installed_model_discovery_not_cached`).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7b64e449-2a7e-f258-17a1-5ffe933608a3)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"aaa3f87897fc00e5a1c237f56b8e93ab5eaa3245","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/aaa3f87897fc00e5a1c237f56b8e93ab5eaa3245"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/45baf6c7a47e08e656ba56eb76beea30a9956403","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnbwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY40QAISTNY7+OnxTP5Nr3Wl4k2tu\nLlylnMHBTpSvgfmFK0XtCGVfFKqQc4l14h7wrAVgdubsH+xfDUpIzLwZlCckQtRN\nIRBD1iOXychELGL6yQLm7SFLQBh7YNRYpgSAqT87CMamjVvSvwN0P76D6hkbSK8h\nPfcUptbu49sWyQsARKcZOL+IwSe9v0R9V2Xbdwh1xryv8KfsppRZqSDiiD7dkxyp\nubJ7FxQx0YYKIBN08Ut5ZOQV7NlADuAFh99yYo4PxHBGbItutEdgWTG3msj62CBS\nnGqQ0+JAbq1rSBg92XoWohGlc7fn4zPw9BYqMQ8IU+6OC5d7kTi+gM6zv0xvRzm8\nX6RuE/dNe/vpMGrfgaSPWEOu4xy7NYkYr1HKOaKQwWHj6ScRuBIxqrB5xqyqzuCy\nfMnY4PhBldVhNanOrazudvw3ZEJSJzsc3Jnj1CtypTnSDycQ6q7QPlaL+nfmx5f9\nowJ7WpOlwv4GzdxlC3N4VtL/a6h1H0XOMhiZtNA4Z8cN6BOJwc019BiEFW1f1NBP\nVqBAxcR3eEihtSlAIuAzsePV7IiQE9CG51DNLX1vOegDUrqH5D04Fs75+avkQj2N\naVmvJF2Z+cL7KAs7Vq9tSdp243dZWule6e67tilUxTDUlTgR7JlBHVutB7Ak53dQ\nJwdRJlO5scMNeFn7TFI7\n=ZZHc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree aaa3f87897fc00e5a1c237f56b8e93ab5eaa3245\nparent 4d483fdf39b6d7c691322041a4fc58be06ecfd6b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784313584 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784313584 -0400\n\nfix(code): probe unreachable Ollama daemon once per reload (#4806)\n\nWhen an Ollama daemon is down, discovery no longer probes it twice or\nemits duplicate, out-of-order debug logs at startup — it probes and logs\n\"not detected\" once per reload.\n\n---\n\nOllama discovery runs from two startup callers — `get_available_models`\nand `get_model_profiles` — that both call\n`_get_ollama_installed_models`. Empty results were never cached, so an\nunreachable daemon was probed twice per reload and logged `Ollama daemon\nnot detected ...` twice. Because the second `not detected` (from\n`get_model_profiles`) landed right after the first pass's `discovery\nreturned no models` line, the two appeared out of order even though each\nindividual pass logs in the correct order.\n\nThis tracks endpoints that fail the TCP presence preflight in\n`_ollama_unreachable_endpoints` and negatively-caches their empty\nresult, so the probe and log happen once. A *reachable* daemon that\nsimply reports no models is still left uncached, preserving recovery of\na later `ollama pull` without `/reload` (covered by the existing\n`test_empty_installed_model_discovery_not_cached`).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7b64e449-2a7e-f258-17a1-5ffe933608a3)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:39:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/45baf6c7a47e08e656ba56eb76beea30a9956403","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/45baf6c7a47e08e656ba56eb76beea30a9956403","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/45baf6c7a47e08e656ba56eb76beea30a9956403/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4d483fdf39b6d7c691322041a4fc58be06ecfd6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4d483fdf39b6d7c691322041a4fc58be06ecfd6b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4d483fdf39b6d7c691322041a4fc58be06ecfd6b"}]},{"sha":"4d483fdf39b6d7c691322041a4fc58be06ecfd6b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRkNDgzZmRmMzliNmQ3YzY5MTMyMjA0MWE0ZmM1OGJlMDZlY2ZkNmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:35:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:35:09Z"},"message":"fix(code): count only running tools in live tool-group line (#4809)\n\nFix the live tool-group progress line in `dcode` so it counts only the\ntools still running instead of every tool in the step.\n\n---\n\nThe collapsed tool-group summary's live progress line summarizes the\nwhole assistant step instead of what is actually still running. Because\nit aggregates every tool in the group, finished calls keep being\nreported as in progress — e.g. it shows `Running 1 shell command,\nrunning 2 agents…` even after the shell command and one of the agents\nhave completed.\n\nThis builds the present-tense line from only the still-pending members,\nso finished calls drop out as they complete. The past-tense line (shown\nonce everything finishes) continues to summarize every tool that ran.\nThe cached present phrasing now rebuilds whenever the set of running\nmembers changes, not just when the group grows.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/25ed04be-b8ed-97c9-a600-d24d80c02162)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae606fe810f6a485211e616c808c3818488d44bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ae606fe810f6a485211e616c808c3818488d44bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4d483fdf39b6d7c691322041a4fc58be06ecfd6b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnXdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQawQAGYbsQFlJZ8Hu18n9JL1eNJy\nElFE197ndy94zw+9oJnX86muzyEVB3o08k0nJTISIIQsHefjlnfwuBIWYJKvvNGE\n1zlMcrMrwkbLV7V9zd0G01GYzH2WjSs5cwAK36XifRluKidlf8Hqtx5t58mz8Oet\n9g6vaBr1RIaQDljvMFYgLxdZeAk0EOi2V6lwmGSx2cptUubUzBORd25+TG1KQntw\n9uVxorVIrNCtsWpFwFEc1KUaYrW1nUUB7azd5AHiYEqLpvt0xUEiov/i2zQxIN2M\nRwe/XW7mepsSGsSfQEEZlxpg0bPKKGxsaSd4F2zRd1JqRq8TiEh+L1Pq/6xKtK7C\nRQgddFwGpbaBBoRrg9fMNgTpb416MCDRg9+GCjic5xbhwiucUjAN8V3mp8Zs1VFi\nh3ZPpnHPkQMrvWApbgUmZtK5x6ouffkKGcE5oFJtrXa9JyDrYRrVlYhdtsFRSrlI\njzHKaACrr4fKdGi8Eg4MIUEN730xSRU9LKLTXvxpQlVIiH5DJSWL7UKlpVY2nem9\ndOLpaoSDYspn9ShG7poER4ZlDUk2Qpmne9Gyp1wHAxoWuhGnzj/CgGM+WyOXKgCe\nLgh6kZv3E0ffFdC9wMCi8Ei3e6Zf6oBaPSQzCgCZGxbeCqHKQDY6JvtU3wGleZxk\nsgmp8r1JfB/aUwkJx6Ci\n=ymbq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ae606fe810f6a485211e616c808c3818488d44bc\nparent 20089a53703b031726fdc898831bb09f434527b7\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784313309 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784313309 -0400\n\nfix(code): count only running tools in live tool-group line (#4809)\n\nFix the live tool-group progress line in `dcode` so it counts only the\ntools still running instead of every tool in the step.\n\n---\n\nThe collapsed tool-group summary's live progress line summarizes the\nwhole assistant step instead of what is actually still running. Because\nit aggregates every tool in the group, finished calls keep being\nreported as in progress — e.g. it shows `Running 1 shell command,\nrunning 2 agents…` even after the shell command and one of the agents\nhave completed.\n\nThis builds the present-tense line from only the still-pending members,\nso finished calls drop out as they complete. The past-tense line (shown\nonce everything finishes) continues to summarize every tool that ran.\nThe cached present phrasing now rebuilds whenever the set of running\nmembers changes, not just when the group grows.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/25ed04be-b8ed-97c9-a600-d24d80c02162)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:35:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4d483fdf39b6d7c691322041a4fc58be06ecfd6b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4d483fdf39b6d7c691322041a4fc58be06ecfd6b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4d483fdf39b6d7c691322041a4fc58be06ecfd6b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"20089a53703b031726fdc898831bb09f434527b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/20089a53703b031726fdc898831bb09f434527b7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/20089a53703b031726fdc898831bb09f434527b7"}]},{"sha":"20089a53703b031726fdc898831bb09f434527b7","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDIwMDg5YTUzNzAzYjAzMTcyNmZkYzg5ODgzMWJiMDlmNDM0NTI3Yjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:28:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:28:41Z"},"message":"feat(code): persist Debug Console `Ctrl+L` clear across reopen (#4812)\n\nClearing the Debug Console (`Ctrl+\\`) traceback/log tail with `Ctrl+L`\nnow persists across closing and reopening the console for the process\nlifetime, instead of re-populating from the in-memory buffer on the next\nopen.\n\n---\n\nThe console modal is recreated fresh on every open and, on mount,\nreplays everything still retained in the always-on in-memory ring\nbuffer. `Ctrl+L` (`action_clear_view`) was deliberately a view-only\nclear that advanced only the current instance's render cursor, so\nclosing and reopening replayed the buffer and the \"cleared\" records came\nback.\n\nThis adds a process-lifetime \"cleared upto\" cursor owned by the app.\n`DebugConsoleScreen` gains keyword-only `cleared_upto` (seeds its render\ncursor so a prior clear is honored on open) and `on_clear` (reports the\nnew cursor when `Ctrl+L` fires). `DeepAgentsApp` stores the cursor in\n`_debug_console_cleared_upto`, seeds each new console from it, and\npersists updates via the callback.\n\nThe change stays strictly view-only: the shared ring buffer is never\nmutated, other diagnostics are unaffected, and records logged *after* a\nclear still appear. Clearing is by emission time, matching the existing\nin-session semantics.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/58c9cc66-afbe-b468-729d-375b731bbf71)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3400de60849c3fba6ccfc75dfd21767edb2df1b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3400de60849c3fba6ccfc75dfd21767edb2df1b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/20089a53703b031726fdc898831bb09f434527b7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnRZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnhEQAFjmNZjb9HzoJq+Tigspwe+0\nZQOOkhcUSTqh1iO8mswAYSkWQDJL7vAlXltjBpYwewtuDnzCJD+cWB01FaKoYlmc\nwovP0OsHNf0dbaRxY5BlspAlaY/+CgdLeAySqAaujT+3heSjSktkLTZ6nSI8xC5n\nfQgTN6lVttctdaJ32wYQ/7ie21F63XbkobyqoouqHsr0RSnxpr+W4pFEtPRvJpGW\nRdQRyjVdXa84PEqgjhsWKF9igNB8eS9eFqto0sKsxIimm6wj9edSitUsPao5hWNb\nvu+Q1OhpMVOW/Bv6QjCSJR6qf45moCuhpypz3CwgDh3fjQp+vSRV0E3nupHaamwq\n9ccbQQC2q1TUPvdBBdFrQ19ciejysv/z3S1PEcJwmzIzdslBWSCHBYkcDOmI50Iu\n50GDYfKgukMT7fPbzk8ZdLhIxdN59cdfrnz/KIqlTx3CrfMzSlOBQjVCAX9XdjIe\n7WeuYdZx06oA1xShUjuFRdOylqWhjkDZOkX0GE3L+Rbpo0KcNlk8mtwaLSSyHQOY\n5vFqvceJe7qXDHX8fRJKd4NkBNi2s6kMVKsv5Rh3HLOn+Xg/POpxC3RK4apP64eu\nHGNsoZMaIT54Uz06qLUMB/RjP/KDSmFZlVt11elny2UMv/711PK5zMFH5tCOBEKm\nSPvF9Le8Pu/pSZ27I7Ih\n=YdYe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3400de60849c3fba6ccfc75dfd21767edb2df1b3\nparent 2d6b2ceeda97f8c77d1b3ea70c674b076e7d713f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784312921 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784312921 -0400\n\nfeat(code): persist Debug Console `Ctrl+L` clear across reopen (#4812)\n\nClearing the Debug Console (`Ctrl+\\`) traceback/log tail with `Ctrl+L`\nnow persists across closing and reopening the console for the process\nlifetime, instead of re-populating from the in-memory buffer on the next\nopen.\n\n---\n\nThe console modal is recreated fresh on every open and, on mount,\nreplays everything still retained in the always-on in-memory ring\nbuffer. `Ctrl+L` (`action_clear_view`) was deliberately a view-only\nclear that advanced only the current instance's render cursor, so\nclosing and reopening replayed the buffer and the \"cleared\" records came\nback.\n\nThis adds a process-lifetime \"cleared upto\" cursor owned by the app.\n`DebugConsoleScreen` gains keyword-only `cleared_upto` (seeds its render\ncursor so a prior clear is honored on open) and `on_clear` (reports the\nnew cursor when `Ctrl+L` fires). `DeepAgentsApp` stores the cursor in\n`_debug_console_cleared_upto`, seeds each new console from it, and\npersists updates via the callback.\n\nThe change stays strictly view-only: the shared ring buffer is never\nmutated, other diagnostics are unaffected, and records logged *after* a\nclear still appear. Clearing is by emission time, matching the existing\nin-session semantics.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/58c9cc66-afbe-b468-729d-375b731bbf71)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:28:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/20089a53703b031726fdc898831bb09f434527b7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/20089a53703b031726fdc898831bb09f434527b7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/20089a53703b031726fdc898831bb09f434527b7/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2d6b2ceeda97f8c77d1b3ea70c674b076e7d713f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2d6b2ceeda97f8c77d1b3ea70c674b076e7d713f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2d6b2ceeda97f8c77d1b3ea70c674b076e7d713f"}]},{"sha":"2d6b2ceeda97f8c77d1b3ea70c674b076e7d713f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJkNmIyY2VlZGE5N2Y4Yzc3ZDFiM2VhNzBjNjc0YjA3NmU3ZDcxM2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T18:27:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T18:27:14Z"},"message":"fix(code): make markdown `AppMessage` output selectable (#4814)\n\n`/version` output (and incognito shell output) is now selectable and\ncopyable.\n\n---\n\nThe output from the `/version` command could not be selected or copied.\nThose tables — and incognito shell output — render through\n`AppMessage(markdown=True)`, which produced a raw Rich renderable.\nTextual only supports text selection over `Content`/`Text` visuals, so a\n`RichVisual` carries none of the per-cell offset metadata selection\nrelies on and its text is neither highlightable nor copyable.\n\nThis renders the muted markdown to segments and rebuilds it as\n`Content`, laid out to the widget's current width, so the\ntables/rules/emphasis look the same but the text is now selectable and\ncopyable. Trailing padding is trimmed per line so copies stay clean.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f705adb2-3ebb-25a2-7ebd-ddce94887917)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e66497c93a712b0812cf86e5927c7dbcea0d43f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3e66497c93a712b0812cf86e5927c7dbcea0d43f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2d6b2ceeda97f8c77d1b3ea70c674b076e7d713f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnQCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAupgQACoNWkGBEJb3f/ICb0ZVUtG8\nNb9ORHmlgwM3dY9sRZMvywjwkyyGDDOnSE+RNM4CLoBvqb1HibRqCrhCwCpPCJwN\nTpyQW+mSUVHaYdJrlBb8XhCKaHpIjsfuRlrNAcLnVY6japc3sRcgn0QdRPefCiAL\nnhThFjOPVHhjuWLVWklxwZRjnbI0BUZ9J4aPLyXEtMFVr5xcbJon16ViFbqXcmzk\neJCnLtI20epLvYfH4OlmmrU77oVa2sfsH8kPZc279ZVnmx1d3+aj10Mh2nD0AVVq\nY0D6pKQJfs4IRFyj45iFaxSbzTpypaiU1AA4OcYCWfJhUMbIIro5SHjSCyn9MtM0\nCRNxqJtOcPrvC6YfAdWIGz8iYO6sl1VUM6hzt1TrAGYELcLf4u8o7ERPZlwagdxO\nOZ5aNOLffOn8roNf/+4pBa74p8WvOIx9PCY5eqZzyy7QAlq4l5bnH8523tWumkBr\ntTJGBu3QZ03wyj+PLj0PD61Ab9NDT+V9I6W2zqqrUz803nEENs7r5D6hVofcgmy4\ndUyK0fQlDJslBGs6uUFXAtW92LHevOX6b1j8d9pt60gUf3/JTgqUTeYLP4vMiTiC\n1k4SlRTq52NnKDWjccp4YWc78kFYilrWvUhUMZ2w+Jwg/OtOU9CWjyF5iQgWPAR6\ndz+iMVewk7emv4ehy9cx\n=3Tm8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3e66497c93a712b0812cf86e5927c7dbcea0d43f\nparent 41123924da6f6aa0243b51f2374210bee86df089\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784312834 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784312834 -0400\n\nfix(code): make markdown `AppMessage` output selectable (#4814)\n\n`/version` output (and incognito shell output) is now selectable and\ncopyable.\n\n---\n\nThe output from the `/version` command could not be selected or copied.\nThose tables — and incognito shell output — render through\n`AppMessage(markdown=True)`, which produced a raw Rich renderable.\nTextual only supports text selection over `Content`/`Text` visuals, so a\n`RichVisual` carries none of the per-cell offset metadata selection\nrelies on and its text is neither highlightable nor copyable.\n\nThis renders the muted markdown to segments and rebuilds it as\n`Content`, laid out to the widget's current width, so the\ntables/rules/emphasis look the same but the text is now selectable and\ncopyable. Trailing padding is trimmed per line so copies stay clean.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f705adb2-3ebb-25a2-7ebd-ddce94887917)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:27:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2d6b2ceeda97f8c77d1b3ea70c674b076e7d713f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2d6b2ceeda97f8c77d1b3ea70c674b076e7d713f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2d6b2ceeda97f8c77d1b3ea70c674b076e7d713f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"41123924da6f6aa0243b51f2374210bee86df089","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/41123924da6f6aa0243b51f2374210bee86df089","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/41123924da6f6aa0243b51f2374210bee86df089"}]},{"sha":"41123924da6f6aa0243b51f2374210bee86df089","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQxMTIzOTI0ZGE2ZjZhYTAyNDNiNTFmMjM3NDIxMGJlZTg2ZGYwODk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-17T17:06:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T17:06:14Z"},"message":"fix(code): surface `langchain-quickjs` in `/version` core deps (#4813)\n\n`/version` now lists `langchain-quickjs` under its \"Core dependencies\"\nsection for editable installs.\n\n---\n\n`langchain-quickjs` powers the built-in interpreter and is a core\nruntime dependency (declared directly in `dependencies`, not as an\noptional extra). It was previously invisible in `/version`: the\n\"Installed optional dependencies\" table only reads packages gated by\n`extra == \"...\"` markers (and the `quickjs` extra is intentionally\nempty), while the curated `CORE_DEPENDENCIES` list that drives the \"Core\ndependencies\" section did not include it.\n\nAdding it to `CORE_DEPENDENCIES` surfaces its resolved version alongside\nthe other LangChain-ecosystem packages, which helps diagnose editable\nenvironments where a local checkout of the partner package may be\noverriding the released one. The section is only rendered for editable\ninstalls, matching existing behavior.\n\nThe `CORE_DEPENDENCIES`-driven tests iterate the tuple generically, so\nthey cover the new entry without modification.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e258f95b-7cc4-33f3-52f0-32d4aa4c13fd)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"93ed6e8133fe8e8ba768ee4bc06af2a605e36e44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/93ed6e8133fe8e8ba768ee4bc06af2a605e36e44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/41123924da6f6aa0243b51f2374210bee86df089","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWmEGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7lsQAIilbfiVqBnwrEq7ve6bod8g\nWmPGB52aNMyCdp2+kO4OHcM40Lvgrp4MLqQJYZmenCnEteOwXUb2k2ehvqiowo+5\nYCjs2t2LT4vTq8WkZe5wn1qyh4F6YlMCWYTvMtRJzxduMKvDRuHLbVWRbTa172ef\nOVPTOqQDjy6TNk1txDbqhyl9AU/8PDH54AMF/mb/sMS73gpzCB1FH3XHwBVFLDWz\nnKMYNusc6q1cHofJs1ZxrTGe3ZQE9a970LvPg1c4d8boxZX2a3PuE1V9iX12YDm5\n2UKSRLbH5KsPCRfPfI+v5QnWoZDpoi5Dfj/KaB3Cal8HKdR5m1ToX/HaQ7988Cw0\nYcMyDmrDptrzGChLzybTELzmkbMg/v4MOeNSV3fhOOjG8md4NSinoFfOWbh8+cId\nUARCN0Mrmkz7S8IT+xP7lzX8KoL5MVUv5lEbZJiL+P71eZ1QUFFs1Pt7UWZgcJYn\nt5BYDUvyk47tf+5erWkDrw118Trc1CEslb2W8patbmzePiJPMm2u0YJVq25Z1tYT\nnai0VOFOuYj5cNllnkAhI+BvmzNq3XIRN91Yc9LLDF9rvoFAPZ7NhdZWP0Wz+s13\naHLcx8ZAW5GGn2s64DEIkKy8ZhzKSvKlX/pOpo4LR/LnAmpoJjoOI3Vg9bJBbRwL\nmu7rkMixh/Szkw5SNUqi\n=1XnW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 93ed6e8133fe8e8ba768ee4bc06af2a605e36e44\nparent 18679a1a88a3f10777bf2f45593cb104e822d49f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784307974 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784307974 -0400\n\nfix(code): surface `langchain-quickjs` in `/version` core deps (#4813)\n\n`/version` now lists `langchain-quickjs` under its \"Core dependencies\"\nsection for editable installs.\n\n---\n\n`langchain-quickjs` powers the built-in interpreter and is a core\nruntime dependency (declared directly in `dependencies`, not as an\noptional extra). It was previously invisible in `/version`: the\n\"Installed optional dependencies\" table only reads packages gated by\n`extra == \"...\"` markers (and the `quickjs` extra is intentionally\nempty), while the curated `CORE_DEPENDENCIES` list that drives the \"Core\ndependencies\" section did not include it.\n\nAdding it to `CORE_DEPENDENCIES` surfaces its resolved version alongside\nthe other LangChain-ecosystem packages, which helps diagnose editable\nenvironments where a local checkout of the partner package may be\noverriding the released one. The section is only rendered for editable\ninstalls, matching existing behavior.\n\nThe `CORE_DEPENDENCIES`-driven tests iterate the tuple generically, so\nthey cover the new entry without modification.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e258f95b-7cc4-33f3-52f0-32d4aa4c13fd)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T17:06:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/41123924da6f6aa0243b51f2374210bee86df089","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/41123924da6f6aa0243b51f2374210bee86df089","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/41123924da6f6aa0243b51f2374210bee86df089/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"18679a1a88a3f10777bf2f45593cb104e822d49f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/18679a1a88a3f10777bf2f45593cb104e822d49f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/18679a1a88a3f10777bf2f45593cb104e822d49f"}]},{"sha":"18679a1a88a3f10777bf2f45593cb104e822d49f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE4Njc5YTFhODhhM2YxMDc3N2JmMmY0NTU5M2NiMTA0ZTgyMmQ0OWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-17T03:24:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-17T03:24:16Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.42 (#4793)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. The published GitHub release body is extracted from the\nmerged `CHANGELOG.md` by `release.yml`, not from this PR description._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.42](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.41...deepagents-code==0.1.42)\n(2026-07-17)\n\n### Features\n\n- Plugins are now generally available.\n([#4797](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4797))\n- Added search to the plugin list and now summarize plugin changes after\nreloads.\n([#4765](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4765),\n[#4767](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4767))\n- Added Kimi K3 to the OpenRouter model selector.\n([#4803](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4803))\n- Added hidden `connect` and `reconnect` keywords for `/restart`.\n([#4807](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4807))\n- Debug Console thread IDs can now be clicked to copy, with an added\nLangSmith link.\n([#4760](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4760))\n- Added auto-approve (YOLO) mode to trace metadata.\n([#4764](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4764))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Improved plugin marketplace loading and onboarding, including\nasynchronous marketplace additions and polish for empty marketplace\nstates.\n([#4766](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4766),\n[#4759](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4759))\n- Clarified plugin component discovery and reload status.\n([#4774](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4774))\n- Avoided blocking MCP OAuth token refresh.\n([#4770](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4770))\n- Restored keyboard focus for marketplace details.\n([#4763](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4763))\n- Dismissed the startup tip when submitting an initial prompt with `-m`.\n([#4779](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4779))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"eede6fe1e1a4248ff82fa60ad6fc94f2cd59a298","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/eede6fe1e1a4248ff82fa60ad6fc94f2cd59a298"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/18679a1a88a3f10777bf2f45593cb104e822d49f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWaBhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa9UQAEkHKV+XsOFh8w8oa2H7MLlx\n4XiTK5UsaNdYA4DpkxyvLXrbmABV1EzfJTOC1ljmQZFLthYccEK9EKl5suRsxS06\n2iO0OMEXfPNLiqKFYoClZd/oQlcTZ1VAcnumY9zw7T2X/zDTE6Kz16lf+1obvTJu\nJoK9n236QuC8aBlqs2uSuqbAPE1aT0aQ/NbDaDsn4aL6oUvWIiBgTRsfTMN15TR4\ncMhKQO1e9p7Gl2WkX2ljf1LRQOr6eci0GXO2G2Rwy2REFz0GNira+qFagosKf5b+\nGYvnR19lsxOl/ZlSxF7S0TTiwfCEuMBEC24ecP0plbm9DUaoPPXHx0q0wd2q6TsY\nEKAsALzdDa7/LUAWtYivN/myV0MAn4pqNYQ/jrQwhgdaj/dryJwA5Lv/b8V3Q18V\nCdaGzg4I3+ckoKi3Z7WBnBAE/hY+SwBEgoqrQFUlABfxEInEB089vhSHZZtiT1nC\nN0hRlB2+8bsaY7OqfVNXDWog24/8h3xwcxkaM5AC5uUfjKKYD3rCBPmeITgMkqcL\nlRFVAM8qhLx9Ye0fPhuztAaxqzzNKwPuoLFv4jlf0PCbiMgff8zXm105kjFyYA+a\nyHtaBYFEzFS5IY3D85//z0y2jOBqVfOI7pKaPxkPpYHxhs6gSv3zKVj+iE7NI3et\nP85jYg9XPEh254jR1L9E\n=PqeP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree eede6fe1e1a4248ff82fa60ad6fc94f2cd59a298\nparent 3da6e471c26f1da4cddeb12a435bab92bd7866c6\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784258656 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784258656 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.42 (#4793)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. The published GitHub release body is extracted from the\nmerged `CHANGELOG.md` by `release.yml`, not from this PR description._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.42](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.41...deepagents-code==0.1.42)\n(2026-07-17)\n\n### Features\n\n- Plugins are now generally available.\n([#4797](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4797))\n- Added search to the plugin list and now summarize plugin changes after\nreloads.\n([#4765](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4765),\n[#4767](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4767))\n- Added Kimi K3 to the OpenRouter model selector.\n([#4803](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4803))\n- Added hidden `connect` and `reconnect` keywords for `/restart`.\n([#4807](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4807))\n- Debug Console thread IDs can now be clicked to copy, with an added\nLangSmith link.\n([#4760](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4760))\n- Added auto-approve (YOLO) mode to trace metadata.\n([#4764](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4764))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Improved plugin marketplace loading and onboarding, including\nasynchronous marketplace additions and polish for empty marketplace\nstates.\n([#4766](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4766),\n[#4759](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4759))\n- Clarified plugin component discovery and reload status.\n([#4774](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4774))\n- Avoided blocking MCP OAuth token refresh.\n([#4770](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4770))\n- Restored keyboard focus for marketplace details.\n([#4763](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4763))\n- Dismissed the startup tip when submitting an initial prompt with `-m`.\n([#4779](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4779))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-17T03:24:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/18679a1a88a3f10777bf2f45593cb104e822d49f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/18679a1a88a3f10777bf2f45593cb104e822d49f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/18679a1a88a3f10777bf2f45593cb104e822d49f/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/r