se, consistent title and body\nconventions.\n\n---\n\nRoutine PRs should omit dedicated test plans; large or highly\nconsequential changes keep them in collapsed details. User-facing\nrelease-note text now appears as plain-English frontmatter, and\nLinear-style issue-closing markers belong in the body rather than the\ntitle.","tree":{"sha":"17ccd94fbf52344e5cefba8e7e4ac39cfd503861","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/17ccd94fbf52344e5cefba8e7e4ac39cfd503861"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7403cec8ed8969a9120a101d3c85a2c26fc68c15","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWTKgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm7MQAG4hdUJKPNnL63kCuLv9HBQI\nnxKWjjN3Fol3CJNBJ7aHHgMkqgZpXXl3gSe7A8BpM/X3vh63l7dCa8eCGNdGndGZ\nc3OBPVKt+kzTiHe4p1mLJ2+sNiTqbYaWQUbxE31wqOfvmEcHsyd6sblDLJIE+7Wt\nmLon8kCR87RvYQneBbZZih9JFTcHDPcApONmIhLvMTf6D2TfOPjQoHMHOyM4Zi6e\nKHZeoYnFlGmysCHbWrkbuVkSkwx7gaw4iKzIte7zYplgjW8HAU7dJYdpegwGmz1p\nXis/tC1AsnlGjg/KqSx4XSd2t/FZdDOBDu67231W+SmbIf2H0P+TkTNWC8TR3jxc\nj3J5CXUz9P7NG3RVIFgzpQOnFx79IqfqNnUH2tS4DmbkI8hGt1KEIlF67JIPc0DO\ncdXwxBzThkeySV3xTtdPmUs2bDTnWJcC9yzVqcfeP/6y9uUTRevUEfyC42IKgAJZ\nzS5t7iQFKI775T/rPYEZyofXQvWWT5muYokglf5S+6zKaD99t8EWTp2pm3FUUZHW\nwgTJgBQ9GbY8C49xjqqCvHYhrGkl4kJazz7uieUdYFtsuGC9rrXLGvDVQexOg988\nsm9B8jOcbJ7wbyHllyKu7Vw5MFbgxx9eDUEV95yOkSSOghqPYvFOC66zRYUpYj2b\nt1rRooB1PrfS2O7yiOvK\n=+z07\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 17ccd94fbf52344e5cefba8e7e4ac39cfd503861\nparent d88601ed582b89d4a5b517e842029d06370c0891\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784230560 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784230560 -0400\n\ndocs(repo): clarify PR title and body guidance (#4796)\n\nPR authors and agents now follow concise, consistent title and body\nconventions.\n\n---\n\nRoutine PRs should omit dedicated test plans; large or highly\nconsequential changes keep them in collapsed details. User-facing\nrelease-note text now appears as plain-English frontmatter, and\nLinear-style issue-closing markers belong in the body rather than the\ntitle.","verified_at":"2026-07-16T19:36:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7403cec8ed8969a9120a101d3c85a2c26fc68c15","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7403cec8ed8969a9120a101d3c85a2c26fc68c15","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7403cec8ed8969a9120a101d3c85a2c26fc68c15/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d88601ed582b89d4a5b517e842029d06370c0891","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d88601ed582b89d4a5b517e842029d06370c0891","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d88601ed582b89d4a5b517e842029d06370c0891"}]},{"sha":"d88601ed582b89d4a5b517e842029d06370c0891","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ4ODYwMWVkNTgyYjg5ZDRhNWI1MTdlODQyMDI5ZDA2MzcwYzA4OTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-16T19:01:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-16T19:01:58Z"},"message":"feat(code): trace auto-approve (YOLO) mode in trace metadata (#4764)\n\nAuto-approve (\"YOLO\") runs are now labeled with\n`dcode_auto_approve=True` in LangSmith trace metadata, making them\nfilterable.\n\n---\n\nAuto-approve (\"YOLO\") mode — the `Shift+Tab` toggle / `--auto-approve` —\nsets `interrupt_on = {}` so tools run with no HITL gate, but nothing\nrecorded that state in LangSmith traces, so YOLO runs weren't\nfilterable. The `coding-agent-v1` contract's `approval_policy` key can't\nhelp here: it's scoped to root/interrupted runs and would leak onto\nevery descendant run (and fail contract validation) if stamped\ntrace-wide.\n\nThis adds a non-contract diagnostic `dcode_auto_approve=True` metadata\nkey in `build_stream_config`, mirroring the existing\n`dcode_experimental` pattern (only stamped when active). Interactive\nturns pass `session_state.auto_approve`; headless turns pass the\nresolved `use_auto_approve` (which reflects \"tools run without HITL\nbecause shell is unrestricted or disabled\" — the same `auto_approve`\nflag the graph consumes). Metadata is sampled once at turn start, so a\nmid-turn toggle doesn't relabel that turn's trace.\n\nNew keyword-only `auto_approve` param defaults to `False`, so the change\nis additive and backward-compatible.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/31881cb9-2c33-7505-1b1a-fd453e84ea5a)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/31881cb9-2c33-7505-1b1a-fd453e84ea5a/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0ab4cd0aa4d2015a9da1524ec98c74d927b26048","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0ab4cd0aa4d2015a9da1524ec98c74d927b26048"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d88601ed582b89d4a5b517e842029d06370c0891","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWSqmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALqYQAFqTfegzSoMv3TBi9SOfTb+Z\ntAXH40rU3MhfMhGwnn4XDuR3owQ/WSYKIetn7yABr0JNTCOtVwU73BMenW6bEqH9\nHwd4D4rt7Fl3qAvTpLdXIJ2OrEx1tUl8eeBKHsN3nsP3b7bF02u03+9IYwbZkqSR\n0nIHQUugXxWNqqqM6FU+zpulZ1g0jzO4kIOuOa9FpFOKaRqFgqO/wvfuxc0BPJ7Z\nyUhjt/UKLUU0q13Vb8OH6fh2nfCpMqm/h12P/3iFpllQVj7PfVUnF/MRTrLu1w+A\n89Gf13V0ocYFxeVq1MKoPP5jxQoy9WNaXl9BjRfD6mS5mfWVvoN/luSzSYvFK/uh\niotkKbK1/sd78AvNNSFJ90QN79sPyryoWHlM5myPuRQ9ggw1ip2VD2EgxUyMUCce\nIA1KbcsgyPuGUfDqohqXOQZYrGv5IvrHUgbL7WT31+A4Ukh3yZw4EW2gO+ZIS18O\nzeFh/NXCAGg8uaEA1yKQuDRyM3D0q6SbubRSfNJ41QYuxiUIJWqnxRleoMY81nkR\nJKrDqVCZYVfgInoHpGOTEF+f5p2n+Xt4gDVvSIwCIJJ1lMXxBYhIcBjqoJdo6dAc\nCsyoKTqivzxWmWfB0q9uBxzcKuC8q6gAuHnuM2Df9Ajrci20IX0fkqUs3IMf+uEk\nuIqg93tr3YEdvE99gWZq\n=Uu/3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0ab4cd0aa4d2015a9da1524ec98c74d927b26048\nparent 78f9f5fcb38dcaec6f0d7552c061ec15844c839b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784228518 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784228518 -0400\n\nfeat(code): trace auto-approve (YOLO) mode in trace metadata (#4764)\n\nAuto-approve (\"YOLO\") runs are now labeled with\n`dcode_auto_approve=True` in LangSmith trace metadata, making them\nfilterable.\n\n---\n\nAuto-approve (\"YOLO\") mode — the `Shift+Tab` toggle / `--auto-approve` —\nsets `interrupt_on = {}` so tools run with no HITL gate, but nothing\nrecorded that state in LangSmith traces, so YOLO runs weren't\nfilterable. The `coding-agent-v1` contract's `approval_policy` key can't\nhelp here: it's scoped to root/interrupted runs and would leak onto\nevery descendant run (and fail contract validation) if stamped\ntrace-wide.\n\nThis adds a non-contract diagnostic `dcode_auto_approve=True` metadata\nkey in `build_stream_config`, mirroring the existing\n`dcode_experimental` pattern (only stamped when active). Interactive\nturns pass `session_state.auto_approve`; headless turns pass the\nresolved `use_auto_approve` (which reflects \"tools run without HITL\nbecause shell is unrestricted or disabled\" — the same `auto_approve`\nflag the graph consumes). Metadata is sampled once at turn start, so a\nmid-turn toggle doesn't relabel that turn's trace.\n\nNew keyword-only `auto_approve` param defaults to `False`, so the change\nis additive and backward-compatible.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/31881cb9-2c33-7505-1b1a-fd453e84ea5a)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/31881cb9-2c33-7505-1b1a-fd453e84ea5a/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-16T19:01:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d88601ed582b89d4a5b517e842029d06370c0891","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d88601ed582b89d4a5b517e842029d06370c0891","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d88601ed582b89d4a5b517e842029d06370c0891/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"78f9f5fcb38dcaec6f0d7552c061ec15844c839b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/78f9f5fcb38dcaec6f0d7552c061ec15844c839b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/78f9f5fcb38dcaec6f0d7552c061ec15844c839b"}]},{"sha":"78f9f5fcb38dcaec6f0d7552c061ec15844c839b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc4ZjlmNWZjYjM4ZGNhZWM2ZjBkNzU1MmMwNjFlYzE1ODQ0YzgzOWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-16T19:01:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-16T19:01:44Z"},"message":"test(code): isolate ambient env and global dotenv in unit tests (#4778)\n\nMake the Deep Agents Code unit tests hermetic so they no longer depend\non the developer's real environment, `~/.deepagents/.env`, or the\ncheckout-path length.\n\nAmbient MCP trust vars\n(`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DANGEROUSLY_ENABLE_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS` and friends),\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG_NOTIFICATIONS`, and\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL` can be loaded from the developer's global\ndotenv at `deepagents_code.config` import time — before fixtures run —\nand `/reload` rereads that global dotenv and restores them. The\ndangerous MCP allowlist intentionally replaces scoped TOML approvals\n(breaking trust-list/selective-project-trust assertions), the debug var\nchanges notification suppression, and a restored experimental flag\nbreaks the `/reload` plugin-summary test. Separately,\n`TestBranchDisplay::test_short_branch_name_not_truncated` let a long\nreal CWD consume the status bar, leaving the branch widget zero width.\n\nApproach (test-only; no production behavior changes):\n- New autouse fixture redirects `config._GLOBAL_DOTENV_PATH` to a\nnonexistent `tmp_path` file so dotenv rereads (e.g. `/reload`) are\ninert.\n- New autouse fixture clears `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG_NOTIFICATIONS`; the\nexisting MCP-trust fixture already removes the trust vars (docstring\nexpanded to explain why).\n- The short-branch test now hides the CWD via `HIDE_CWD`, consistent\nwith neighboring branch-display tests, so path length can't starve the\nwidget.\n\nTests that intentionally exercise dotenv loading already set\n`_GLOBAL_DOTENV_PATH` and their inputs explicitly in the test body\n(after the isolation fixtures), so they are unaffected.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/234e9ee9-f18a-e812-4187-aae8190e4711)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"51d5c9ebc2216a6bf5bba5f76f9cf16ed8049f8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/51d5c9ebc2216a6bf5bba5f76f9cf16ed8049f8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/78f9f5fcb38dcaec6f0d7552c061ec15844c839b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWSqYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2OQQAF5bcHBcyF6YjQ9uIw0pNwLw\n3auoklj5OM6zD4wkfAuy8iKKlq0q5hcHE61MqXe/kQu+N7glWyWNz64PUmwU5BLa\nA+wJM0smgsIHCFSd4eTJ9K+YbbljimjU/pbtroy3Wa4M2/YzLPtGa94+d9lCz5r1\nXyCBi743442QHpQjQZlspMlN4a7mf3Mp9i2MjuDsuJbVf/kA4M/RaxLX4iPpK2MX\nx+grOv0tj75DeSw3CGQ8kBalWlCq949yFucNHxSCTTsVv94PChMro4E3w5GDE6uO\npXLX8A8M5wzepeHDQ43wOv8Ls7x9BOPld9CUSorrDEqrvuyuIfBy20+SxO3/ox1q\nNgdMClHSvU1TKadTmjeg/N9TxNmtENBBN4u9f2NHnjKSEsoGnqsDvYFXF0lxHJSF\nuWw2rLCQql+04taDki8Js3ohkLKFvm+b1JNEyjOXbQdNeuo1lNgGuOM/0wT5GdOu\n5V9ZW6CXyhrsiZkCr34oCuL11R8z0D+TG533Fij30gl5rfU9mjwxOWioApegvpey\ni+2sSc50seWQl2NVBzMsTCFs8qfyc+Z6A32/oydjdAZGBoxkG+a7fgk3cMcrg6Zf\nYxkoxGWyJs9DD3EALu+lMk3fCRAO1SnOhE3wD06SP92wsQM04mzaT7wI7Uy4KXDv\noy/KjLIwB12i56fI4gIV\n=irUU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 51d5c9ebc2216a6bf5bba5f76f9cf16ed8049f8c\nparent 8acd414a2e712d8b8b1968e40bff40483196856b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784228504 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784228504 -0400\n\ntest(code): isolate ambient env and global dotenv in unit tests (#4778)\n\nMake the Deep Agents Code unit tests hermetic so they no longer depend\non the developer's real environment, `~/.deepagents/.env`, or the\ncheckout-path length.\n\nAmbient MCP trust vars\n(`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DANGEROUSLY_ENABLE_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS` and friends),\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG_NOTIFICATIONS`, and\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL` can be loaded from the developer's global\ndotenv at `deepagents_code.config` import time — before fixtures run —\nand `/reload` rereads that global dotenv and restores them. The\ndangerous MCP allowlist intentionally replaces scoped TOML approvals\n(breaking trust-list/selective-project-trust assertions), the debug var\nchanges notification suppression, and a restored experimental flag\nbreaks the `/reload` plugin-summary test. Separately,\n`TestBranchDisplay::test_short_branch_name_not_truncated` let a long\nreal CWD consume the status bar, leaving the branch widget zero width.\n\nApproach (test-only; no production behavior changes):\n- New autouse fixture redirects `config._GLOBAL_DOTENV_PATH` to a\nnonexistent `tmp_path` file so dotenv rereads (e.g. `/reload`) are\ninert.\n- New autouse fixture clears `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG_NOTIFICATIONS`; the\nexisting MCP-trust fixture already removes the trust vars (docstring\nexpanded to explain why).\n- The short-branch test now hides the CWD via `HIDE_CWD`, consistent\nwith neighboring branch-display tests, so path length can't starve the\nwidget.\n\nTests that intentionally exercise dotenv loading already set\n`_GLOBAL_DOTENV_PATH` and their inputs explicitly in the test body\n(after the isolation fixtures), so they are unaffected.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/234e9ee9-f18a-e812-4187-aae8190e4711)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-16T19:01:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/78f9f5fcb38dcaec6f0d7552c061ec15844c839b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/78f9f5fcb38dcaec6f0d7552c061ec15844c839b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/78f9f5fcb38dcaec6f0d7552c061ec15844c839b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8acd414a2e712d8b8b1968e40bff40483196856b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8acd414a2e712d8b8b1968e40bff40483196856b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8acd414a2e712d8b8b1968e40bff40483196856b"}]},{"sha":"8acd414a2e712d8b8b1968e40bff40483196856b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhhY2Q0MTRhMmU3MTJkOGI4YjE5NjhlNDBiZmY0MDQ4MzE5Njg1NmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-16T19:01:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-16T19:01:10Z"},"message":"fix(code): dismiss startup tip on `-m` initial submission (#4779)\n\nThe splash tip above the chat input is now dismissed when the TUI is\nlaunched with an initial prompt (`-m`), skill (`--skill`), or goal\n(`--goal`), matching interactive submissions.\n\n---\n\nWhen launching the TUI with `dcode -m \"msg\"`, the splash tip above the\nchat input stayed visible, unlike a normal interactive prompt which\nclears it.\n\nThe tip was only dismissed inside `_submit_input`, the shared path for\ninteractive and external prompts. Startup submissions from `-m` (as well\nas `--skill` and `--goal`) run through `_submit_initial_submission`\ninstead, which dispatches directly to `_handle_user_message` /\n`_invoke_skill` / `_handle_goal_command` and never dismissed the tip.\nThis adds a `_dismiss_startup_tip()` call at the top of\n`_submit_initial_submission` so all startup submission paths match\ninteractive behavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/2d2a8fdc-c71c-58c6-287a-6d4109d24bbb)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b0c2e8b14bdca569408c89cd981d5d4d9f3c775c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b0c2e8b14bdca569408c89cd981d5d4d9f3c775c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8acd414a2e712d8b8b1968e40bff40483196856b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWSp2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKO0QAJRWoKJqJYl3OPOh+EgKVMwG\nv6kpOe0KQ5OhmIKH3CtZVr6EGLjhqBRL28PEBc2/NkPuz9adCcb7xpGS5Il/5xYu\nmMqOb7EbJKoLibAvOjGe/AvaX1lYBsYYF1n6P2mlpJ0qajD0F5/PAhfdoLi23rMw\ng/zzJhFHCmo8hEmkC/ww3OkTnB8Ak0Zr9VUvg74AYaT5WNTTFgzC/NDe232oc5n9\nwcIBhP7nqNS8/69hHw5q/DE5ww/cgHMzYQoUQvdFiX3rHrBSfAW8Ps1i/Kt/LnOB\nfn8O7m//yMOrjgBTe5RliNUC5h7dH7R+C070TScWiv/OFT5cEtfTrYcVOBfsmGq7\n1/+R6AzwfdtO1gEkjFhUaQDoedZG/EXuQzq0GdYGzmNhViVjbiAcyEaS/00IA2uu\nbpd5hsTKyHB4LJkcPSdv+g8KRuxT+vf3nNPSxwKzBRf3t8CsNjwo5qxGpSu64uND\n0KRFPhnMxIVQk1erSCFDI/ZQRkWV3bfvcNjlxZ22k8KuVdnkgRc4VGPmxLBDZo+N\npvrwjSMbhknHcYahSuU0ofnSc02/B5yrHoaARiKw617cdc9j9reux8edY/EjAwLy\nm/SFhppKRU7COVmu+ThQE7xfnuazfFeo8nsugIRt15IFCcSPhWKwAljq0/iy8AO/\ni4TGrX0zfaaIDYQEsaU0\n=fcPY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b0c2e8b14bdca569408c89cd981d5d4d9f3c775c\nparent e821d3dd26e8cd0c6ada1a44ceaceddad9f5ee80\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784228470 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784228470 -0400\n\nfix(code): dismiss startup tip on `-m` initial submission (#4779)\n\nThe splash tip above the chat input is now dismissed when the TUI is\nlaunched with an initial prompt (`-m`), skill (`--skill`), or goal\n(`--goal`), matching interactive submissions.\n\n---\n\nWhen launching the TUI with `dcode -m \"msg\"`, the splash tip above the\nchat input stayed visible, unlike a normal interactive prompt which\nclears it.\n\nThe tip was only dismissed inside `_submit_input`, the shared path for\ninteractive and external prompts. Startup submissions from `-m` (as well\nas `--skill` and `--goal`) run through `_submit_initial_submission`\ninstead, which dispatches directly to `_handle_user_message` /\n`_invoke_skill` / `_handle_goal_command` and never dismissed the tip.\nThis adds a `_dismiss_startup_tip()` call at the top of\n`_submit_initial_submission` so all startup submission paths match\ninteractive behavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/2d2a8fdc-c71c-58c6-287a-6d4109d24bbb)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-16T19:01:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8acd414a2e712d8b8b1968e40bff40483196856b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8acd414a2e712d8b8b1968e40bff40483196856b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8acd414a2e712d8b8b1968e40bff40483196856b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e821d3dd26e8cd0c6ada1a44ceaceddad9f5ee80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e821d3dd26e8cd0c6ada1a44ceaceddad9f5ee80","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e821d3dd26e8cd0c6ada1a44ceaceddad9f5ee80"}]},{"sha":"e821d3dd26e8cd0c6ada1a44ceaceddad9f5ee80","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGU4MjFkM2RkMjZlOGNkMGM2YWRhMWE0NGNlYWNlZGRhZDlmNWVlODA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-16T18:28:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-16T18:28:44Z"},"message":"fix(code): restore marketplace details keyboard focus [closes DCD-50] (#4763)\n\n## Description\nMarketplace detail controls ignored Tab and Shift+Tab because those\nbindings only attempted to switch tabs. Cycle enabled detail options\nwith wraparound while preserving existing list-tab and Escape behavior.\n\n## Release Note\nMarketplace detail controls now support visible, predictable Tab and\nShift+Tab keyboard navigation.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] Navigate marketplace details forward, backward, and through\nwraparound with a Textual pilot test.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/019f6783-f3db-727b-ad05-65934c0a9505)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0d966fbe65d82fbf00ddfe0ded3bbf5e029f91b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0d966fbe65d82fbf00ddfe0ded3bbf5e029f91b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e821d3dd26e8cd0c6ada1a44ceaceddad9f5ee80","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWSLcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZCQQAIp6hQ1yQFk/mz5gOTSMrKu0\nYNmyWLU0rm4x1D6VEUbtqyT/RPqcXFG281HNPW50bhZQMQP+8OIXIcElt+i2NoP0\nSQtklh9sH+N6BDKXSq0nG75mHSQNNLAaeIScBFIsM4SVrDaodhcBYsHcwZKjfZvg\n85LOwO3Ok8Z3RoUsl2dAN+UUHsQJSYPaq4bOLGmnUPzsw1H0NXyF6lGBPBoTPbCt\nKg7P2OrieCIkpU+LGywTMpdTAXPdlYsQW3l800t3pRPVmzc+DMks+u5qlNMoCXCO\nCwMa/ZJEsisDnKE7qGB9GouyDZJHuiSj+p4gmC+m2LA1o3/koyIRyIkdBH764czW\n6a8lue25TW3ABnMhGZUnrnUeQU1smtYnfJm/ejoA5yvJEnJnh1bJ4yra8MjAA0ls\n/JUqaV7sxZdcIcHPNJMptUghpsbsk0RlB07/FWtvDuZvXuQ8v0Irzaqb9Cxpatn5\n9S9oBuF31D4GXnTZ9wby7jgnnYPnDjlu/xI8VLSGhImfmMqNM+DslIAEQpJXyJ7K\nLpPw3M7lrLS3IDEa1TJd/LrSjflCleuEx3GzJXMEthAKppNWlYr7nEsEyv40xPBy\nJXFhNm9dxaeQrjOMuYqrtY4bU+0jFpAUbpzA+ANlLXFIAFc03wA6+Bt583Ja3dBB\nCwZO6s0cc/rkHaOCiK/E\n=69/z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0d966fbe65d82fbf00ddfe0ded3bbf5e029f91b5\nparent 5bff73b94e70f0110ef3c72057666387b16a1d8b\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1784226524 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784226524 -0700\n\nfix(code): restore marketplace details keyboard focus [closes DCD-50] (#4763)\n\n## Description\nMarketplace detail controls ignored Tab and Shift+Tab because those\nbindings only attempted to switch tabs. Cycle enabled detail options\nwith wraparound while preserving existing list-tab and Escape behavior.\n\n## Release Note\nMarketplace detail controls now support visible, predictable Tab and\nShift+Tab keyboard navigation.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] Navigate marketplace details forward, backward, and through\nwraparound with a Textual pilot test.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/019f6783-f3db-727b-ad05-65934c0a9505)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-16T18:28:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e821d3dd26e8cd0c6ada1a44ceaceddad9f5ee80","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e821d3dd26e8cd0c6ada1a44ceaceddad9f5ee80","c