._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e591cb00b08eef3fcb3c6746d533343ccd3b66c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e591cb00b08eef3fcb3c6746d533343ccd3b66c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d46a2cb033b8195f440f68de744e75874b6f8e6f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWNBOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJAwQAA9QIXaqk5InXFg18GCr8/mV\nUkcieqCV/I0ufEHVUf360uzvDHoPjA/7bvcxUK/6Ka/nw23UuJuh4eURVuw2T3Id\nc9CJzbimcyQL5svuNu1TvuustpRzJiuVYTBefu6q7BYsJn/btVlqss8cpxahLln1\nHUATUXUMvycNPoH1mQ2mllcpMYix7Q9erBwL7cUEGTLKzz+8SLlC7gs2UqnmSkYt\nQSwchNWv6VdDgWpdSzB8SbFCdZ/INX8lk0Z+e0TXH1Xt6MsojHZGlJgNZcBWFoed\nbGOQZs5NzoP9VVRhqkKvHGiSHUMkTIG8RAAG9lB0I7LC5XlALHKUvaiNO9ClcN/a\n+Nv/RSOqR8hms+JYuS4bJiImmnfFm9Vsc8gpiM0hJYGzuRj6TkPqhDl6lI72/v3e\np6D8UwuqO0dzXp3lBChTXdGgR+pWqPZRMq0d0gC49f92NxiKiT6IgSExw01FFB0I\n1OUMoD4Cn09ETqU9jWayQyYWZRPZXFIVrgBjLbvZnjPOnMYlNdHRoMQD4tCpM6XE\n2ZUuCg65eOV7Ln1wJWRpoPmhN8TKfG2j+sOrFQdqOp4BQFZ63mI4Nv7FOxWWVPWZ\nwvIqZgM36R5zb7NQURlNI1VDsedyIsRllG1UwlEW9emlePms0RQ7HAd+UJGb5P5h\nXqecbdF/eIg7wr8D0GUT\n=flvE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e591cb00b08eef3fcb3c6746d533343ccd3b66c2\nparent f9b7d75f24301081ae8973cd59f00e609eb024c5\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784205390 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784205390 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.41 (#4790)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. The published GitHub release body is extracted from the\nmerged `CHANGELOG.md` by `release.yml`, not from this PR description._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.41](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.40...deepagents-code==0.1.41)\n(2026-07-16)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Pinned `filelock` below 3.30 to avoid blocking imports\n([#4786](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4786))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-16T12:36:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d46a2cb033b8195f440f68de744e75874b6f8e6f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d46a2cb033b8195f440f68de744e75874b6f8e6f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d46a2cb033b8195f440f68de744e75874b6f8e6f/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f9b7d75f24301081ae8973cd59f00e609eb024c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f9b7d75f24301081ae8973cd59f00e609eb024c5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f9b7d75f24301081ae8973cd59f00e609eb024c5"}]},{"sha":"f9b7d75f24301081ae8973cd59f00e609eb024c5","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY5YjdkNzVmMjQzMDEwODFhZTg5NzNjZDU5ZjAwZTYwOWViMDI0YzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-16T11:57:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-16T11:57:49Z"},"message":"fix(code): pin filelock below 3.30 to avoid blocking import (#4786)\n\n`filelock` 3.30.0 runs a blocking temp-directory probe\n(`_probe_link_follow_symlinks`) at import time. `deepagents-code`\nimports `filelock` (via `mcp_auth`) on the async server-graph startup\npath, so Blockbuster rejects the resulting `os.getcwd` call and the\ngraph fails its readiness check with `BlockingError: Blocking call to\nos.getcwd`, aborting startup entirely. The broad `>=3.12,<4.0.0` range\nlet a fresh install resolve the just-released 3.30.0, which is why even\ndowngrading `deepagents-code` reproduced it.\n\nCapping at `<3.30` keeps resolution on 3.29.x. A follow-up can make the\n`filelock` import loop-safe (e.g. warm it up off the event loop) and\nrelax the cap.\n\n## Release Note\nFix `deepagents-code` startup failure (`BlockingError: Blocking call to\nos.getcwd`) caused by `filelock` 3.30.0.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] `dcode` launches cleanly with `filelock` resolved to 3.29.x\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a27d2d36-4e59-b0b2-edbb-228bc6e557c9)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"fdeb34da3c4dc2272bad5abb835e3cef1ffbce26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/fdeb34da3c4dc2272bad5abb835e3cef1ffbce26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f9b7d75f24301081ae8973cd59f00e609eb024c5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWMc9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj2EQAAFDgomvh/Z+jzijm17NNsBw\nEsMGdbbFI0p9SthIPWYg8/M82NfR1O7KlKRsOVltB6xayiqoo49ga+ThUxG3sVEa\n7HLsz7nWO7qkrX2hpxFPSI4+lnzYW8y82t+ZFelzY82/ZNks+Tg8HitU/CdYyVA7\nhQKOd4TAqL4xWSsEzGMHQlrN//Y/RUBRSQYVLmrzjN2OmdMDqFjR2P390RA2xTvy\nkqoCTd90eeGWyK6Uk+j+G/YIU7VN0elZ8k9DsP3dPszdKLQwuXcBaVhcVVpyrYyz\nSdpC5yJ1KjwXFA8GBKWTS06wYq+nTTmb/SCvrGc7YwqBtgZ5JOx+sRuhVkxMtwmb\nwPPz9IiRYunqiZDwO6bLbCrRCXqCXk2RBi5fsr1aDnGJe+g+v2l0T459i/MfM/zm\nuj8FAMPVAJV5/rjMcJF090a2+nBnJbw7vE4LGCrrQvPU6ytQQF4gVkxpDfL/x7gK\nj4n6WQ31cITwn4uJc+gj7I7HuXKKyEV3JQJnu+lX+WXpWH9w2+9jQAA2+M7iEk9G\nO7Vd4iCEThXm39RtuGrJp6x9ONWACPvaawqFlpxdAcRKaJdc1uv31WvPFXKV1367\nAKAjCuHX2bLuYfV6A3rmN5+cJ7AxqO8J1QENyymyHlGtcpsjED5DRT26C3pSGZ9X\nzS8TIJ7ZnmKoiyf/02d3\n=ZlGf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fdeb34da3c4dc2272bad5abb835e3cef1ffbce26\nparent d13d299a0fc91369efdbc8376f09837c52f27969\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784203069 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784203069 -0400\n\nfix(code): pin filelock below 3.30 to avoid blocking import (#4786)\n\n`filelock` 3.30.0 runs a blocking temp-directory probe\n(`_probe_link_follow_symlinks`) at import time. `deepagents-code`\nimports `filelock` (via `mcp_auth`) on the async server-graph startup\npath, so Blockbuster rejects the resulting `os.getcwd` call and the\ngraph fails its readiness check with `BlockingError: Blocking call to\nos.getcwd`, aborting startup entirely. The broad `>=3.12,<4.0.0` range\nlet a fresh install resolve the just-released 3.30.0, which is why even\ndowngrading `deepagents-code` reproduced it.\n\nCapping at `<3.30` keeps resolution on 3.29.x. A follow-up can make the\n`filelock` import loop-safe (e.g. warm it up off the event loop) and\nrelax the cap.\n\n## Release Note\nFix `deepagents-code` startup failure (`BlockingError: Blocking call to\nos.getcwd`) caused by `filelock` 3.30.0.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] `dcode` launches cleanly with `filelock` resolved to 3.29.x\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a27d2d36-4e59-b0b2-edbb-228bc6e557c9)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-16T11:57:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f9b7d75f24301081ae8973cd59f00e609eb024c5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f9b7d75f24301081ae8973cd59f00e609eb024c5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f9b7d75f24301081ae8973cd59f00e609eb024c5/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d13d299a0fc91369efdbc8376f09837c52f27969","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d13d299a0fc91369efdbc8376f09837c52f27969","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d13d299a0fc91369efdbc8376f09837c52f27969"}]},{"sha":"d13d299a0fc91369efdbc8376f09837c52f27969","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQxM2QyOTlhMGZjOTEzNjllZmRiYzgzNzZmMDk4MzdjNTJmMjc5Njk","commit":{"author":{"name":"langsmith-fleet[bot]","email":"242644093+langsmith-fleet[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-16T06:21:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-16T06:21:37Z"},"message":"chore(deps): Bump nltk for CVE-2026-54293 (#4787)\n\n## Summary\n- bump `nltk` in `libs/evals` from 3.9.4 to 3.10.0\n- raise the minimum `nltk` dependency bound to 3.10.0\n- include the new `defusedxml` transitive dependency required by NLTK\n3.10.0\n\n## Security\nFixes Dependabot alert 576 / GHSA-p4gq-832x-fm9v / CVE-2026-54293. The\nadvisory marks `nltk<=3.9.4` vulnerable; 3.10.0 includes hardened\nresource loading against path traversal.\n\n## Validation\n- `uv lock --project libs/evals --locked --offline`\n\nNote: I attempted to install/use Socket Firewall for package-manager\nprotection, but the SFW binary download returned HTTP 502 in the\nsandbox. I avoided registry-resolving package-manager updates and used\nPyPI release metadata plus offline lock validation instead.\n\nCo-authored-by: Langster <security-agent@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"d072e2131014865e17639c335c6ca68c07c5a0c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d072e2131014865e17639c335c6ca68c07c5a0c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d13d299a0fc91369efdbc8376f09837c52f27969","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWHhxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyF0QAFhOlwA6UFaV2rYQ6pmtwXXK\nDc/iDku9fQg9BDEORoP4YpwvfaO7QC3O3QzRC/BFQ316UOwfeUsp6XO9DgV4uJn0\nrqSyPqrRjIuV9MiAw6vocVhLyi8v8yQ6THzoeBRJ2nUokFp2Q11HuTI5Pz+7Gjm8\nfWzOENmKe0zYoXG1RuLeBuOplycoQaJ3db3spLEgRbGspiaXaOA8eduB6/NnyW4O\nP+tDi0RtpsF97nFSrrvioSTSGQ6WhXsJR/GAKtqtfYXIUEv9WTkNZE9R77tL1Vnr\nJaFLgwJLRljY2fEhoHoiWE60UxpPbVFZhloaiubmULXE8NPAVZ1tQc8tiKAbzlew\ngtzaC7BmNYZ9FTK4mImd58XovIJvAn1bhnfIBKJJdL9kJFxYu1uEAytZrr/Mt83/\n/BPJd3yLRcmweAOq/ccy6qDd5W2ByXG0LoJmnjL7kXlk7nALotZdY/RvmyADsCpZ\nEWS6p/Sbam8dG8trUEt+zORFEnzjwKbDiiA0iB64IWQIBfXVOwDd42cZ4EBVJEQC\ntXhJ7k99bO2zCAUH2J4DCtuZjhSGW4c1DkqdOQJLVB8zr0hNWm2ekkVW4xrw1CTT\nz8OvHoe6py7QhcAhmA8lyNNgzqGwcTbKjBxSuOiB0VrhgWcfQTgN3Inm8Wp21Jdg\nVRClrDm0nb7vVMzBafBT\n=Xbv9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d072e2131014865e17639c335c6ca68c07c5a0c5\nparent 019489edb9c0d442a42ae6e5229f4ddf8ba56e08\nauthor langsmith-fleet[bot] <242644093+langsmith-fleet[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784182897 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784182897 -0700\n\nchore(deps): Bump nltk for CVE-2026-54293 (#4787)\n\n## Summary\n- bump `nltk` in `libs/evals` from 3.9.4 to 3.10.0\n- raise the minimum `nltk` dependency bound to 3.10.0\n- include the new `defusedxml` transitive dependency required by NLTK\n3.10.0\n\n## Security\nFixes Dependabot alert 576 / GHSA-p4gq-832x-fm9v / CVE-2026-54293. The\nadvisory marks `nltk<=3.9.4` vulnerable; 3.10.0 includes hardened\nresource loading against path traversal.\n\n## Validation\n- `uv lock --project libs/evals --locked --offline`\n\nNote: I attempted to install/use Socket Firewall for package-manager\nprotection, but the SFW binary download returned HTTP 502 in the\nsandbox. I avoided registry-resolving package-manager updates and used\nPyPI release metadata plus offline lock validation instead.\n\nCo-authored-by: Langster <security-agent@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-16T06:21:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d13d299a0fc91369efdbc8376f09837c52f27969","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d13d299a0fc91369efdbc8376f09837c52f27969","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d13d299a0fc91369efdbc8376f09837c52f27969/comments","author":{"login":"langsmith-fleet[bot]","id":242644093,"node_id":"BOT_kgDODnZ0fQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2251985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/langsmith-fleet%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/langsmith-fleet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langsmith-fleet%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langsmith-fleet%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langsmith-fleet%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langsmith-fleet%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langsmith-fleet%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langsmith-fleet%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langsmith-fleet%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langsmith-fleet%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langsmith-fleet%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"019489edb9c0d442a42ae6e5229f4ddf8ba56e08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/019489edb9c0d442a42ae6e5229f4ddf8ba56e08","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/019489edb9c0d442a42ae6e5229f4ddf8ba56e08"}]},{"sha":"019489edb9c0d442a42ae6e5229f4ddf8ba56e08","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDAxOTQ4OWVkYjljMGQ0NDJhNDJhZTZlNTIyOWY0ZGRmOGJhNTZlMDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-16T03:35:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-16T03:35:57Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.40 (#4734)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. The published GitHub release body is extracted from the\nmerged `CHANGELOG.md` by `release.yml`, not from this PR description._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.40](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.39...deepagents-code==0.1.40)\n(2026-07-16)\n\n### Features\n\n- Added plugin marketplace support\n([#4554](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4554)).\n- Added an “always allow” option to the project MCP approval prompt\n([#4562](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4562)).\n- Improved `/goal` workflows: criteria generation now runs server-side,\nYOLO mode auto-accepts criteria, goals complete after satisfied grading,\nand goal review editing now supports `Ctrl+X`\n([#4754](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4754),\n[#4784](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4784),\n[#4781](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4781),\n[#4780](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4780)).\n- Reasoning effort now persists across restarts\n([#4728](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4728)).\n- Added a toast prompting you to re-paste when a chat paste collapses\n([#4742](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4742)).\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Tool calls awaiting approval are now surfaced correctly\n([#4739](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4739)).\n- Fixed transcript tail hydration when scrolled to the bottom edge\n([#4733](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4733)).\n- Kept chat input responsive during MCP viewer `Ctrl+R` reconnects\n([#4753](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4753)).\n- Improved inline free-text prompts by sharing paste handling and\nmatching primary-input `Ctrl+D` behavior\n([#4736](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4736),\n[#4729](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4729)).\n- Fixed local offloaded tool results to use the real filesystem\n([#4740](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4740)).\n- Cleaned offloaded history when deleting a thread\n([#4751](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4751)).\n- Removed duplicated content from the system prompt by overwriting the\nbase prompt\n([#4516](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4516)).\n- Closed subprocess transport during install teardown\n([#4735](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4735)).\n- Added targeted `uv` constraints for prerelease dependencies\n([#4744](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4744)).\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e80046bcb23a1bc1c4959b24aee915e7e31a0768","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e80046bcb23a1bc1c4959b24aee915e7e31a0768"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/019489edb9c0d442a42ae6e5229f4ddf8ba56e08","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWFGdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYooQAAOj1efWky5/mYXDd1S74ceD\neytzCo6UGK1dtnsFRhwogPcqNK+R6AfBzMDEl6AXKdIxFKIkudzkEVl4rSYeoLEs\n4TlyHcqree47fTY6mS22Rop6Uu1WzfghC0KHsu8iziw3FIoINMWDfbS0KHxfJ89p\n/f74LeQp0RsBZNhDsJA4H9xaJqHmNikb5qfIdhs//cXHm57g+1nzwyFQUGk70Lo6\nLnc3r3K2ORTol7700cluePeYaeWV0f13BE/uJ/0ERSZKa5jR2fxvKx9K8WuFQ4r/\nTf6FEDfIjwi2NlNa/wHex2iBbgZm73cmy/tmKXADkgoKhaKGHRS4MtbJK4K0+PBE\nVXnO1pG3ZzpBweuxw0aKoDa0QqTLRI1TYPGBSZOjBgodMLOdPQjql1wWvcHRlw66\n9H1NfewC91T64/uaYAT9L6RzqqcvwfcJQ8Fb71rc1/DSPJnfqgo8R9AVr0aQWlxJ\n7ySdPa8Dq2X9xyPDEYbw+5G7aiRvedkGPFrRZ0S1ETccLbtln+tfmE16h6RkoY2K\n/DUXVcaM2Elx7xBP0e035pmuOzpDECV4z6/DU8bc+UYOh2MN3Q46oUI9VLAc3Ec1\nGTp2+wyI7v247Hsf4+owQvKaByrGuVaCQJA82H19/t+tEf8g3smbTVvMezDCIRXj\nzoyurjkdf2xSHw4FX7qu\n=74yh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e80046bcb23a1bc1c4959b24aee915e7e31a0768\nparent cc662f236dbf72303be5cbf2c4cfd00710a2d32c\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784172957 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784172957 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.40 (#4734)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. The published GitHub release body is extracted from the\nmerged `CHANGELOG.md` by `release.yml`, not from this PR description._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.40](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.39...deepagents-code==0.1.40)\n(2026-07-16)\n\n### Features\n\n- Added plugin marketplace support\n([#4554](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4554)).\n- Added an “always allow” option to the project MCP approval prompt\n([#4562](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4562)).\n- Improved `/goal` workflows: criteria generation now runs server-side,\nYOLO mode auto-accepts criteria, goals complete after satisfied grading,\nand goal review editing now supports `Ctrl+X`\n([#4754](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4754),\n[#4784](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4784),\n[#4781](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4781),\n[#4780](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4780)).\n- Reasoning effort now persists across restarts\n([#4728](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4728)).\n- Added a toast prompting you to re-paste when a chat paste collapses\n([#4742](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4742)).\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Tool calls awaiting approval are now surfaced correctly\n([#4739](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4739)).\n- Fixed transcript tail hydration when scrolled to the bottom edge\n([#4733](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4733)).\n- Kept chat input responsive during MCP viewer `Ctrl+R` reconnects\n([#4753](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4753)).\n- Improved inline free-text prompts by sharing paste handling and\nmatching primary-input `Ctrl+D` behavior\n([#4736](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4736),\n[#4729](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4729)).\n- Fixed local offloaded tool results to use the real filesystem\n([#4740](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4740)).\n- Cleaned offloaded history when deleting a thread\n([#4751](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4751)).\n- Removed duplicated content from the system prompt by overwriting the\nbase prompt\n([#4516](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4516)).\n- Closed subprocess transport during install teardown\n([#4735](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4735)).\n- Added targeted `uv` constraints for prerelease dependencies\n([#4744](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4744)).\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-16T03:35:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/019489edb9c0d442a42ae6e5229f4ddf8ba56e08","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/019489edb9c0d442a42ae6e5229f4ddf8ba56e08","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/019489edb9c0d442a42ae6e5229f4ddf8ba56e08/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cc662f236dbf72303be5cbf2c4cfd00710a2d32c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cc662f236dbf72303be5cbf2c4cfd00710a2d32c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cc662f236dbf72303be5cbf2c4cfd00710a2d32c"}]},{"sha":"cc662f236dbf72303be5cbf2c4cfd00710a2d32c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNjNjYyZjIzNmRiZjcyMzAzYmU1Y2JmMmM0Y2ZkMDA3MTBhMmQzMmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-16T03:24:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-16T03:24:29Z"},"message":"feat(code): auto-accept `/goal` criteria in YOLO mode (#4784)\n\nYOLO mode now automatically accepts successfully generated `/goal`\nacceptance criteria, including amendments, regenerated proposals, and\nproposals restored from a thread.\n\n---\n\nWhen someone creates, amends, or regenerates a `/goal` while YOLO mode\nis enabled, dcode still generates acceptance criteria but now accepts a\nsuccessful proposal without interrupting the workflow with an\ninteractive review.\n\nAutomatic acceptance reads the live per-thread approval mode and follows\nthe same persistence and continuation path as selecting “Accept proposed\ncriteria.” Turning YOLO on also resolves a proposal already awaiting\nreview, while turning it off before generation finishes preserves the\nmanual review. Failed, cancelled, rejected, stale, and superseded\nproposals remain fail-closed, and review widgets, futures, tasks, and\nfocus are cleaned up when automatic acceptance takes over.\n\nManual goal review and standalone `/rubric` behavior are unchanged. The\ntranscript explains when YOLO accepted criteria automatically, and\n`/goal show` continues to expose the accepted objective and criteria.","tree":{"sha":"c66fb454bb4e568c9e3b85db79c0235e638aea67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c66fb454bb4e568c9e3b85db79c0235e638aea67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/cc662f236dbf72303be5cbf2c4cfd00710a2d32c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWE7tCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnRoQACldKF1psKerNz+aJR2NFOib\nfTgMfHq5VbXIAACJ3YkYZfL8OFGvnjQKfZcMHlfUxH12iUUCG1ykug4t7c4YFR+A\nSeUc/Nql+lwyiu18qebavJZPlIbb6uDa3G1FHsdo7GCSlLFrZNkinR+cXtLfO3W/\nlPWhZJrgWKKijYSvna3eCwSxbCRuy8rEjun8EjAz4BGn1DSiMCctwQrgjeSDqj7P\nrggACgoGWOb8tI92TMOMCnORMwnZk7GuipKmOpYQcagTBxii+w20RrVnWGp1NGRE\nHiek23Ptvt9n27tTlhO5CkDncxIMgZeKl4uWEjF2OF3ZR4VmFtB3610VulvuJy/d\n/xOkisHi3dB+pLT7A72X8pWNbC8Z/t6vEaS8nuDgbn8F6rkKbIj2WW5cTikQ+lVc\n6qYTv9auVfesSo9hlPb8xX/onhHP1My9PyyimBZKZ6l9iJi2xaWoxz6gGKUmuK2b\nPQoj3SehPjXL2fj4vfDWEWPF/QnqR1D+qY9+M+EQk8nRaXHWVVcdAKuwaqaVfsTf\nkIlj4CMI2s05kcgINMhtq6S26mhdluCoolj17UNs7JyxkIjflpbTFg48QvIBMDAZ\noTcbxEguKImrb/HEIcjaCefCct0CRe6BiwozPPXcS4Vh3CygDWXUILykJyF3+61R\nqBL6pYuketKHRSxwAi8O\n=1fjP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c66fb454bb4e568c9e3b85db79c0235e638aea67\nparent 682ce0fc760e96cf546ea9c97050293548aebc45\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784172269 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784172269 -0400\n\nfeat(code): auto-accept `/goal` criteria in YOLO mode (#4784)\n\nYOLO mode now automatically accepts successfully generated `/goal`\nacceptance criteria, including amendments, regenerated proposals, and\nproposals restored from a thread.\n\n---\n\nWhen someone creates, amends, or regenerates a `/goal` while YOLO mode\nis enabled, dcode still generates acceptance criteria but now accepts a\nsuccessful proposal without interrupting the workflow with an\ninteractive review.\n\nAutomatic acceptance reads the live per-thread approval mode and follows\nthe same persistence and continuation path as selecting “Accept proposed\ncriteria.” Turning YOLO on also resolves a proposal already awaiting\nreview, while turning it off before generation finishes preserves the\nmanual review. Failed, cancelled, rejected, stale, and superseded\nproposals remain fail-closed, and review widgets, futures, tasks, and\nfocus are cleaned up when automatic acceptance takes over.\n\nManual goal review and standalone `/rubric` behavior are unchanged. The\ntranscript explains when YOLO accepted criteria automatically, and\n`/goal show` continues to expose the accepted objective and criteria.","verified_at":"2026-07-16T03:24:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cc662f236dbf72303be5cbf2c4cfd00710a2d32c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cc662f236dbf72303be5cbf2c4cfd00710a2d32c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cc662f236dbf72303be5cbf2c4cfd00710a2d32c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"682ce0fc760e96cf546ea9c97050293548aebc45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/682ce0fc760e96cf546ea9c97050293548aebc45","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/682ce0fc760e96cf546ea9c97050293548aebc45"}]},{"sha":"682ce0fc760e96cf546ea9c97050293548aebc45","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY4MmNlMGZjNzYwZTk2Y2Y1NDZlYTljOTcwNTAyOTM1NDhhZWJjNDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-16T01:30:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-16T01:30:00Z"},"message":"fix(code): complete goals after satisfied grading (#4781)\n\nAccepted `/goal` objectives now automatically transition to `complete`\nwhen their current goal-backed work turn finishes with a satisfied\nacceptance-criteria grade. Completed goals remain visible through `/goal\nshow` but no longer affect later ordinary turns.\n\n---\n\nAn accepted `/goal` should finish when its own final rubric grade says\nevery criterion is satisfied. Previously the agent also had to call\n`update_goal(status=\"complete\", ...)`, manual mode requested another\napproval, and successful completion removed the goal record entirely.\nThat made completion depend on approval mode and left `/goal show` with\nnothing to report.\n\nCompletion now requires a validated grading event observed live during\nthe current goal-backed work turn, a matching grading-run identifier in\nthe checkpoint, and a turn that finishes without aborting. Criteria\ngeneration, thread restoration, standalone `/rubric` grading, unrelated\nor ungraded turns, stale persisted grader state, and unknown grader\nverdicts cannot complete a goal. If a satisfied grade arrives before an\ninterrupted turn, the goal remains active and the UI explains that it\nwill be checked again on the next turn.\n\nCompletion is persisted transactionally; if that write fails, the active\ngoal and any agent-provided note remain available for a later retry.\nCompleted goals retain their objective, acceptance criteria, status, and\ncompletion note while no longer driving subsequent work or grading.\nAgents may still call `update_goal(status=\"complete\", ...)` to provide a\ncompletion note, but the call is optional. Manual and YOLO modes use the\nsame completion path without a completion approval prompt.","tree":{"sha":"2201a62d4ac6db4da5cb112204a7291873eaa91b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2201a62d4ac6db4da5cb112204a7291873eaa91b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/682ce0fc760e96cf546ea9c97050293548aebc45","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWDQYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3dAQACJ+K1FL2wRcqQUKehBxz0Pz\nv8RFRK+rdsG4Zx+QYKlTK4EEmqadU1ByuBWTVB+wJCXk1EY766oGWaO45bFaDTqW\nM61PCfQnakXHTWWXT5Mf+cCwge6BN3XuSan4v/noX7th8gZY7cNsg+ikFct8mtqp\nAlOW2KP/d7oCkZIh1sCmcJ/27mXvXGWZsBXWkY2qnsQ4MszLAiSEok0zcfOtBwbB\ncXoKsy1Fc7clhi6+yCFhN+WCNT5ImH/jsYczTQ625FbNm4+T4YFlLd0IY00YCTfw\nfy0Bayeuclc+egfXL+otSbkevlLtVKwN/2Ocu8rxYo+8FefpQcO34FEc2h5WXWkH\nZ13ZIvtSz5BBwdL65Tn4psrncY1Csqv1jdq4RYBPCC27nySXqRZE3o0oyX5TWuUL\ncvCIl4nDto9IfdWafNP7u+E5BS8WwXFVEs4iX40sz+ABQ3r3lFzLTkKhRsqdptAu\n6u33T4jfLeY0Uhoy7bxnjT8I4E5nUU7IfYCxdqcicxdlhLA5FYbjpy+vgQv8uTtA\n9H45fSJKKGG+/2BQpP3bSYDdX3g3toDTQGkF4ZTE8Np0gONYjqTLg1OICB8zE7mv\nsGtvmk9fhSr3sPVcBpVwzM0opx3ZBKo+/7lBF3VF/02WMvuu6wJQir+Q64Vi9NTd\nVjc/3U1FjTJU0lTq65GX\n=76wf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2201a62d4ac6db4da5cb112204a7291873eaa91b\nparent 641b906157db2c6ae476805f0714ae8f51040492\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784165400 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784165400 -0400\n\nfix(code): complete goals after satisfied grading (#4781)\n\nAccepted `/goal` objectives now automatically transition to `complete`\nwhen their current goal-backed work turn finishes with a satisfied\nacceptance-criteria grade. Completed goals remain visible through `/goal\nshow` but no longer affect later ordinary turns.\n\n---\n\nAn accepted `/goal` should finish when its own final rubric grade says\nevery criterion is satisfied. Previously the agent also had to call\n`update_goal(status=\"complete\", ...)`, manual mode requested another\napproval, and successful completion removed the goal record entirely.\nThat made completion depend on approval mode and left `/goal show` with\nnothing to report.\n\nCompletion now requires a validated grading event observed live during\nthe current goal-backed work turn, a matching grading-run identifier in\nthe checkpoint, and a turn that finishes without aborting. Criteria\ngeneration, thread restoration, standalone `/rubric` grading, unrelated\nor ungraded turns, stale persisted grader state, and unknown grader\nverdicts cannot complete a goal. If a satisfied grade arrives before an\ninterrupted turn, the goal remains active and the UI explains that it\nwill be checked again on the next turn.\n\nCompletion is persisted transactionally; if that write fails, the active\ngoal and any agent-provided note remain available for a later retry.\nCompleted goals retain their objective, acceptance criteria, status, and\ncompletion note while no longer driving subsequent work or grading.\nAgents may still call `update_goal(status=\"complete\", ...)` to provide a\ncompletion note, but the call is optional. Manual and YOLO modes use the\nsame completion path without a completion approval prompt.","verified_at":"2026-07-16T01:30:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/682ce0fc760e96cf546ea9c97050293548aebc45","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/682ce0fc760e96cf546ea9c97050293548aebc45","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/682ce0fc760e96cf546ea9c97050293548aebc45/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"641b906157db2c6ae476805f0714ae8f51040492","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/641b906157db2c6ae476805f0714ae8f51040492","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/641b906157db2c6ae476805f0714ae8f51040492"}]},{"sha":"641b906157db2c6ae476805f0714ae8f51040492","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY0MWI5MDYxNTdkYjJjNmFlNDc2ODA1ZjA3MTRhZThmNTEwNDA0OTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-16T00:36:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-16T00:36:40Z"},"message":"feat(code): add `Ctrl+X` to goal review editing (#4780)\n\n`Ctrl+X` now opens the active `/goal` criteria or rejection-feedback\nfield in the configured external editor.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user was editing proposed goal criteria or entering regeneration\nfeedback, `Ctrl+X` still opened the unrelated chat draft because the\npriority app binding always targeted the composer. This moved focus out\nof the review and made external-editor composition unusable in both\ngoal-review modes.\n\n`Ctrl+X` now detects the active goal-review field and opens its complete\nlogical value, including expanded collapsed-paste content, in `$VISUAL`\nor `$EDITOR`. Saved text returns to the same field without submitting;\ncancellation or failure preserves the existing value and focus. Hidden,\nstale, detached, or unfocused goal editors fall through to the unchanged\nchat-input behavior.","tree":{"sha":"447b1a5b620b83fa1da9612c3030649c1ace05c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/447b1a5b620b83fa1da9612c3030649c1ace05c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/641b906157db2c6ae476805f0714ae8f51040492","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWCeYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAObgQAIwNJda4A1vBLMT7qxj4GOJk\n0XbxtFCndOzvb1IoFW+5gXORAmDWEO3HBwAmweT+zA7swP9S0H3IusfszRz+olzx\nvTjqrKVlsODaSMnAyY4eKuDg9x601EY3ycZ5jMZuIc7xHYRPsSKfRy2FIpXI1dE+\n+1GFru0t+vRmtQwIyexH2RoD/JhDsKmOpI2frwfWO/VVB3EFuTS4UCi5CmEqvBDq\n7tEJHOaxt5xiJacCeLju/vcSv9f7uwwLt/NM7YqR8mZrnb6Xj/EuBDhI1yBChbbQ\nxu4J3zwuncvbTPZrTlo8jfTak+bTYpOGTa9WpzvxukR1Bu9fmBQGDzaUP/la1Zp9\n1V6Dd3hN4L7tREjb0cnzn1O0CNPjkXtWdEk5ECFr25LOrwrhmFZvu8H6vSp9svU6\nJMXAKNAo33XY51DQtfVBxZGrSR9eiof41nn3PucQg7JuPuHrsYihnN7jtvEIzN7E\nBJbyZ2oU9o/VnK17hJ3qLNYNezIXrFuc9uYOWUoMRL0SfZsxTfODmz4HcHtCqocK\n2Bvx4PHDDCGHW2m5EW43K84GjFYzcOHhsbr3vJVZD8a+Cxoca+0btEnhew8l9GP/\nSGmG+AkebtatRuExn/etfYi1yUDuZ8xWyE9Y1xtBRizGLdpM29f1jw9qMODh+LaF\nXFR6thsR6353PN3ZvIMs\n=bzLl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 447b1a5b620b83fa1da9612c3030649c1ace05c0\nparent 9fdd498937842e2ac490ae0e0ca74eef47abd0bb\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784162200 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784162200 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add `Ctrl+X` to goal review editing (#4780)\n\n`Ctrl+X` now opens the active `/goal` criteria or rejection-feedback\nfield in the configured external editor.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user was editing proposed goal criteria or entering regeneration\nfeedback, `Ctrl+X` still opened the unrelated chat draft because the\npriority app binding always targeted the composer. This moved focus out\nof the review and made external-editor composition unusable in both\ngoal-review modes.\n\n`Ctrl+X` now detects the active goal-review field and opens its complete\nlogical value, including expanded collapsed-paste content, in `$VISUAL`\nor `$EDITOR`. Saved text returns to the same field without submitting;\ncancellation or failure preserves the existing value and focus. Hidden,\nstale, detached, or unfocused goal editors fall through to the unchanged\nchat-input behavior.","verified_at":"2026-07-16T00:36:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/641b906157db2c6ae476805f0714ae8f51040492","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/641b906157db2c6ae476805f0714ae8f51040492","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/641b906157db2c6ae476805f0714ae8f51040492/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9fdd498937842e2ac490ae0e0ca74eef47abd0bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9fdd498937842e2ac490ae0e0ca74eef47abd0bb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9fdd498937842e2ac490ae0e0ca74eef47abd0bb"}]},{"sha":"9fdd498937842e2ac490ae0e0ca74eef47abd0bb","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDlmZGQ0OTg5Mzc4NDJlMmFjNDkwYWUwZTBjYTc0ZWVmNDdhYmQwYmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-15T21:17:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T21:17:41Z"},"message":"feat(code): move `/goal` criteria generation server-side (#4754)\n\n`/goal` acceptance-criteria drafting now runs on the agent server and\ncan use conversation, repository, web, and explicitly read-only\nconfigured MCP context while preserving resumable review state.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, `/goal` proposals were drafted in the client process from\nthe explicit objective, so remote or sandbox repository context and\nreferences to the current conversation were unavailable. This moves\nproposal and amendment drafting into a nested agent in the main server\ngraph, where it can use recent conversation context, bounded read-only\nrepository search, `fetch_url`, optional web search, and configured MCP\ntools explicitly annotated as read-only.\n\nRepository context remains read-only and repository-rooted across\nbackends: local reads use a virtual project root, while sandbox reads\nare constrained to the provider's declared working directory, including\ncanonical-path checks that reject symlink escapes.\n\nProposals are stored as pending checkpoint state rather than chat\nmessages, so review survives remote interrupts and resumes without\npolluting the coding conversation. Each proposal is correlated with its\noriginating request, and criteria requests are cleared after success,\nfailure, or cancellation without clearing newer requests. Cancelling\ncriteria generation stops the server run without adding normal\nchat-interruption messages. The client refreshes checkpoint state after\ngeneration and reuses the existing accept, edit, and reject flow; model\nprofile overrides now cross the client/server boundary consistently.","tree":{"sha":"ff3050a1746a05dfd657de4c1f3ddfdafde7abab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ff3050a1746a05dfd657de4c1f3ddfdafde7abab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9fdd498937842e2ac490ae0e0ca74eef47abd0bb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV/j1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMekQAFtMHIrkWgwJYPmUDnXLO7Y4\n4Io+C69+VLa2vff2rphIFFVQg2NqDmhXuFNNqD8G66iMLhBg/LC8kR3M3ZT5aRjn\nik3iYxrGTc+dHL7GO3MOc0jR+mde8mrYs1EIHfDoyadjH7WMZTLaczP0J4bkVGIj\nDsAJ5d5oGIqL5eFYUDsumfjFTPFXmallUnUJ20gR7gx+DsDmqDw+xD4U2bsaxTBo\n09KiTn42E9QAn59TYgBFVGIElq26tAwliId5QnrEsLo1e1+/slgU6CR4zg6OXXCO\n10BhN/cqRL+M3/iL8xebhjmJkBHhn8gxS8bZ6BOKLNd1s4MeVX+22kTzjHVKb3Lt\n4FTptkQh9Z8JBtqnEF4D9M7Fl7NDbbkVrJZX3UpLmPLytzSHWB82iK0wm3eEySvW\n9tnyHmgR1DpSG2x++LjO1CY3Fji6xwPuWE5JKK4Hu22hPQ8UGMnebDoWNo0HCL1Z\nAsO5ROfNC8KvRLmESdTt5DKDRBRcL3bF+97V3/eElnkxUdEbuAKi0p0xNEnDsf4F\nUwcQUoSkB89joPHQm4nJVEp/HRM8DNEYTXvD50MbTaO4Qgp8Ais/Bjq/iCcugJ/I\nbtj0LdjW48xqZ8ZKz/y648e+4XRjRfN3Hiovkw7ifyDW1eVqXna1+K+5sg2ImsKZ\nF1vL6kQBjdJ4g36DH2Rd\n=Je4t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ff3050a1746a05dfd657de4c1f3ddfdafde7abab\nparent a08a0fa1f4a4b1506a42eef794d7933423053ca6\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784150261 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784150261 -0400\n\nfeat(code): move `/goal` criteria generation server-side (#4754)\n\n`/goal` acceptance-criteria drafting now runs on the agent server and\ncan use conversation, repository, web, and explicitly read-only\nconfigured MCP context while preserving resumable review state.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, `/goal` proposals were drafted in the client process from\nthe explicit objective, so remote or sandbox repository context and\nreferences to the current conversation were unavailable. This moves\nproposal and amendment drafting into a nested agent in the main server\ngraph, where it can use recent conversation context, bounded read-only\nrepository search, `fetch_url`, optional web search, and configured MCP\ntools explicitly annotated as read-only.\n\nRepository context remains read-only and repository-rooted across\nbackends: local reads use a virtual project root, while sandbox reads\nare constrained to the provider's declared working directory, including\ncanonical-path checks that reject symlink escapes.\n\nProposals are stored as pending checkpoint state rather than chat\nmessages, so review survives remote interrupts and resumes without\npolluting the coding conversation. Each proposal is correlated with its\noriginating request, and criteria requests are cleared after success,\nfailure, or cancellation without clearing newer requests. Cancelling\ncriteria generation stops the server run without adding normal\nchat-interruption messages. The client refreshes checkpoint state after\ngeneration and reuses the existing accept, edit, and reject flow; model\nprofile overrides now cross the client/server boundary consistently.","verified_at":"2026-07-15T21:17:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9fdd498937842e2ac490ae0e0ca74eef47abd0bb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9fdd498937842e2ac490ae0e0ca74eef47abd0bb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9fdd498937842e2ac490ae0e0ca74eef47abd0bb/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a08a0fa1f4a4b1506a42eef794d7933423053ca6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a08a0fa1f4a4b1506a42eef794d7933423053ca6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a08a0fa1f4a4b1506a42eef794d7933423053ca6"}]},{"sha":"a08a0fa1f4a4b1506a42eef794d7933423053ca6","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGEwOGEwZmExZjRhNGIxNTA2YTQyZWVmNzk0ZDc5MzM0MjMwNTNjYTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-15T19:53:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T19:53:16Z"},"message":"feat(evals): unified evals lite profile, harness fixes, and luna scorecard (#4723)\n\n## Summary\n\nHardens the unified multi-model Harbor evals workflow\n(`unified_evals.yml`) and adds a model scorecard. Validated end-to-end\non `openai:gpt-5.6-luna` (docker sandbox, bare harness).\n\n### Workflow / harness\n\n- **`profile=lite`**: a frozen high-signal task subset (`lite_tasks.py`,\ndifficulty-frontier tasks; full rollouts, fewer tasks) selectable via\nthe `profile` input. Sharded one task per shard so GitHub's matrix\ndrains a dynamic queue (long pole is the slowest single task, and heavy\ntask images never concentrate on one runner). Roughly 8x faster and 6x\ncheaper than the full run.\n- **`agent_impl` input** (`dcode` | `bare`) to pick the harness for the\ncode categories; conversation stays on tau3.\n- **Multi-spec `harbor_package_override`** (one pip spec per line) so\n`harbor` and `harbor-langsmith` can be pinned to the same commit.\n- **LangSmith sandbox credential isolation**: the sandbox authenticates\nwith a dedicated `LANGSMITH_SANDBOX_API_KEY`, passed via harbor's\n`--environment-kwarg` (resolved from the host env at construction, so it\nnever lands on argv or in the serialized job/trial config), while\ntracing/datasets/results stay on `LANGSMITH_API_KEY`. Requires a harbor\nbuild with `--environment-kwarg ${VAR}` support\n(harbor-framework/harbor#2344); langsmith-sandbox runs must therefore\nset `harbor_package_override` until that releases.\n- Experiments land on the **canonical shared datasets** (one dataset per\ncategory, model-as-experiment) instead of per-model datasets.\n\n### Fixes\n\n- Use the **OpenAI Responses API** in the harbor langgraph agent, fixing\nthe `reasoning_effort` + tools 400 on Responses-only models.\n- Supply **`JUDGE_*` config + `OPENAI_API_KEY`** to the harbor-index\nverifier env for LLM-judge tasks, fixing `RewardFileNotFoundError`.\n- Fix **`resolve_langsmith_api_key`** preferring\n`LANGSMITH_SANDBOX_API_KEY` for tracing/dataset/results calls (which\nrouted them to the wrong tenant); those now use `LANGSMITH_API_KEY`.\n\n### Docs\n\n- `libs/evals/UNIFIED_SCORECARD.md`: GH aggregate pass@k / avg@k for\nluna, with **Full (default)** and **Lite** tables plus per-run\nconditions.","tree":{"sha":"77b521dba8940f067cdb01d0215860a3d70c0a69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/77b521dba8940f067cdb01d0215860a3d70c0a69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a08a0fa1f4a4b1506a42eef794d7933423053ca6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV+UsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR9EQAKKzxntI05JpzaklLOxhjNBt\njeZK0T8maoMDc/JrWPSg7+2nJDkQXcrNqu51Fzb7Kta8W26BRIctziJh9jCD6wWK\n42IRUPC/aMTxBianfdXs+B/WeXUy/hqQO/s3XkKaZDQTQLCNe0s45iCXpASZZTdn\nTHvucxA9JI1kGREpTL9QK9eeSuSZ89g3K9eR07cUdxD3EmberNWUYX2Zo5NfiSfe\n9gztwZ3zZfNxqLPg4LJUSTKV/YVpQh4DfbfCSa3GhoX8rhkCr9TJ2SKzQ3cblSzl\ntq5Eve1Wvyemz7V2IpdJd9LcS49oZzSUZR5elqD3s9TZ7Wu3B4AWSD5FLkvfb/aY\nuuEnvkq3uxr5ISZ/Afmm98HgOEwW60Q4ZRxQW1oLq8gjcb442y75bkZtwncFnOg9\nJHwBXeKW4dqIFEm6R9rzHLzVxYnOmzDketjTwiUwJ050rBfejEoT9nZHEmPcMeGq\nURIKfXJphaOPyZqd3nQOyWNHy/CsGzTDqoBhGnAgWQwnRrKPHZC2gFGNAfE9K/x0\n0WzLMhASfZ9b6IUZEzjZjkvu32aTiNYPmgAN+9pHWvnN1hFHpBETONqX6krU4YM6\nzwqpal/nb4e2KPPH/3dyXaWzP530vg2Sr7k0qJq5QyHUTQIWVDCsgTFM07LpPSf0\nkiB1GY9jQh6UaSpS1P5v\n=Z9VM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 77b521dba8940f067cdb01d0215860a3d70c0a69\nparent 47788ededafd44f74b4368ec6793bf4685ad3a3a\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1784145196 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784145196 -0400\n\nfeat(evals): unified evals lite profile, harness fixes, and luna scorecard (#4723)\n\n## Summary\n\nHardens the unified multi-model Harbor evals workflow\n(`unified_evals.yml`) and adds a model scorecard. Validated end-to-end\non `openai:gpt-5.6-luna` (docker sandbox, bare harness).\n\n### Workflow / harness\n\n- **`profile=lite`**: a frozen high-signal task subset (`lite_tasks.py`,\ndifficulty-frontier tasks; full rollouts, fewer tasks) selectable via\nthe `profile` input. Sharded one task per shard so GitHub's matrix\ndrains a dynamic queue (long pole is the slowest single task, and heavy\ntask images never concentrate on one runner). Roughly 8x faster and 6x\ncheaper than the full run.\n- **`agent_impl` input** (`dcode` | `bare`) to pick the harness for the\ncode categories; conversation stays on tau3.\n- **Multi-spec `harbor_package_override`** (one pip spec per line) so\n`harbor` and `harbor-langsmith` can be pinned to the same commit.\n- **LangSmith sandbox credential isolation**: the sandbox authenticates\nwith a dedicated `LANGSMITH_SANDBOX_API_KEY`, passed via harbor's\n`--environment-kwarg` (resolved from the host env at construction, so it\nnever lands on argv or in the serialized job/trial config), while\ntracing/datasets/results stay on `LANGSMITH_API_KEY`. Requires a harbor\nbuild with `--environment-kwarg ${VAR}` support\n(harbor-framework/harbor#2344); langsmith-sandbox runs must therefore\nset `harbor_package_override` until that releases.\n- Experiments land on the **canonical shared datasets** (one dataset per\ncategory, model-as-experiment) instead of per-model datasets.\n\n### Fixes\n\n- Use the **OpenAI Responses API** in the harbor langgraph agent, fixing\nthe `reasoning_effort` + tools 400 on Responses-only models.\n- Supply **`JUDGE_*` config + `OPENAI_API_KEY`** to the harbor-index\nverifier env for LLM-judge tasks, fixing `RewardFileNotFoundError`.\n- Fix **`resolve_langsmith_api_key`** preferring\n`LANGSMITH_SANDBOX_API_KEY` for tracing/dataset/results calls (which\nrouted them to the wrong tenant); those now use `LANGSMITH_API_KEY`.\n\n### Docs\n\n- `libs/evals/UNIFIED_SCORECARD.md`: GH aggregate pass@k / avg@k for\nluna, with **Full (default)** and **Lite** tables plus per-run\nconditions.","verified_at":"2026-07-15T19:53:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a08a0fa1f4a4b1506a42eef794d7933423053ca6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a08a0fa1f4a4b1506a42eef794d7933423053ca6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a08a0fa1f4a4b1506a42eef794d7933423053ca6/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"47788ededafd44f74b4368ec6793bf4685ad3a3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/47788ededafd44f74b4368ec6793bf4685ad3a3a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/47788ededafd44f74b4368ec6793bf4685ad3a3a"}]},{"sha":"47788ededafd44f74b4368ec6793bf4685ad3a3a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ3Nzg4ZWRlZGFmZDQ0Zjc0YjQzNjhlYzY3OTNiZjQ2ODVhZDNhM2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-15T18:43:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T18:43:32Z"},"message":"fix(code): clean offloaded history when deleting a thread (#4751)\n\nDeleting a thread now also removes its offloaded conversation history\nfrom `~/.deepagents`.\n\n---\n\nDeleting a thread through the `/threads` switcher (and the `threads\ndelete` CLI) only removed the thread's SQLite checkpoints, leaving its\noffloaded conversation-history archive orphaned under\n`~/.deepagents/conversation_history/{thread_id}.md`. Over time these\nfiles accumulate for threads the user believes are gone.\n\n`delete_thread` now also removes the per-thread archive via a new\n`delete_offloaded_history` helper in `offload.py`, which resolves the\nsame offload root used when writing history. The helper guards against a\ncrafted `thread_id` escaping the archive directory and is a no-op when\nno archive exists (e.g. server/sandbox mode, where history lives on the\nsandbox backend).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1ca83aca-3d44-5887-c9c2-3ea96c440136)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a43091c079172a2f720df12fbd5708e145805a5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a43091c079172a2f720df12fbd5708e145805a5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/47788ededafd44f74b4368ec6793bf4685ad3a3a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV9TUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe7wQAG+rRV5NRygv6cUZAyfjPfQx\n/i3fXhpTGbsM6KdjPzdzVvL8eQvnQHUkX9pp4RK9gOyHswytbgNQlVDwDPoxc28D\nZC8yd7Mb63Y5oYhov2+9bVOFV6N+ea5suaigh0CD73wmVdJ1xAqWlKiGBCxNxCCp\n68bPrgOwJhaXUv5athD31/NEEFoMzus3tLbK5sdp62VQ/7HUcYl+vq2/8iT1KonK\nuEedAAJ7GEwh5TApmmJzGh2DlBALieQwU/z96J42LhwbPt36Ch8vyZ85oI+aMtXJ\nzU02pqLfHxjarZJEeXs1LwSKFU1oYfg1upCbkAwQFeknDMLK6hNsZI4AOM7HDYky\n4Z6sfUkV0KsXm6e/2ldikp627hKM2ZXay0f1DWzi/34nY7vEDAtg6PwaSclUD/T1\n/dC9f36IsKs1YW+LPFugoYdB5TNRYICwp2EfyZkSAspninz1gW7Lke6fODmLNsLo\n10iwTd1CTlweI28Ov1RACpPfUcoevkf1Xjz4BVXX+zZnIMG7w4gWE6W3vWpvxc8Z\n2CWaQAunY1fyq1IWfCg8VyKke3rpy0gw7EqO7MD7RxoeITcUgiPcvjj+1KGbNMTp\nrRF3OGmJdWcLf22vZe0a/S/2B15/XAMkk+zL37w/JAPjYC3xkBHvSbIdg5aqxwXd\n3LzOJbocgna27nqrq8Vd\n=yDV5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a43091c079172a2f720df12fbd5708e145805a5f\nparent 28dc96d08bc057f2e435b557062a819db4191310\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784141012 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784141012 -0400\n\nfix(code): clean offloaded history when deleting a thread (#4751)\n\nDeleting a thread now also removes its offloaded conversation history\nfrom `~/.deepagents`.\n\n---\n\nDeleting a thread through the `/threads` switcher (and the `threads\ndelete` CLI) only removed the thread's SQLite checkpoints, leaving its\noffloaded conversation-history archive orphaned under\n`~/.deepagents/conversation_history/{thread_id}.md`. Over time these\nfiles accumulate for threads the user believes are gone.\n\n`delete_thread` now also removes the per-thread archive via a new\n`delete_offloaded_history` helper in `offload.py`, which resolves the\nsame offload root used when writing history. The helper guards against a\ncrafted `thread_id` escaping the archive directory and is a no-op when\nno archive exists (e.g. server/sandbox mode, where history lives on the\nsandbox backend).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1ca83aca-3d44-5887-c9c2-3ea96c440136)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-15T18:43:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/47788ededafd44f74b4368ec6793bf4685ad3a3a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/47788ededafd44f74b4368ec6793bf4685ad3a3a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/47788ededafd44f74b4368ec6793bf4685ad3a3a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"28dc96d08bc057f2e435b557062a819db4191310","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/28dc96d08bc057f2e435b557062a819db4191310","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/28dc96d08bc057f2e435b557062a819db4191310"}]},{"sha":"28dc96d08bc057f2e435b557062a819db4191310","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI4ZGM5NmQwOGJjMDU3ZjJlNDM1YjU1NzA2MmE4MTlkYjQxOTEzMTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-15T18:21:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T18:21:35Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep chat input responsive during MCP viewer `Ctrl+R` reconnect (#4753)\n\nFixed the `/mcp` viewer Ctrl+R reconnect blocking keyboard input until\nthe server finished reconnecting.\n\n---\n\nPressing Ctrl+R inside the `/mcp` viewer to reconnect froze the chat\ninput until the reconnect finished. The handler scheduled\n`_reconnect_from_viewer_safe` with `call_later`, which awaits the\ncoroutine inside the Textual app message pump; the multi-second\n`server_proc.restart()` then stalled the pump so key events were no\nlonger forwarded. Running the reconnect as a detached\n`asyncio.create_task` (mirroring the force-reconnect confirm path) keeps\nthe pump free, so input stays responsive and typed messages queue and\ndrain once the server is ready.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b1d98f23-e279-dc41-4f4f-ce0818900274)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"32a562b5513ff77d8e41245640604121a2fffaaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/32a562b5513ff77d8e41245640604121a2fffaaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/28dc96d08bc057f2e435b557062a819db4191310","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV8+vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiG0QAHgpvFVnIzqIjdztYnKflky+\nBcAk6g9OQ2LndE/dU8KQvw0fERJHD62TAx5IGVpLpxyFc6MKlm2y6PfGThqeQSIc\ngyC+FEQ0F8TX+MxDSIflxvDwIn39b6gVa+fvDQQ7qaE0JzIB5iN4scuLFmZsWiRU\n3tTvFG5+R6KMT28Py+132jDXicJKbETAZhlLlSikIj81ZMAz555kTcn1eqs2x98i\nSGYhHITMWyhcYSHudvYQEHqjRpj+jPRQsZtT0ORMjO8OVPC8sRL4WcBljhf5P3++\nMa2Q4tPbfBNv+PDbDcT401GGzmeCCuA6yt0IUftDEGe74r2TnsjFCJQa8oFxLvuh\nT2AWPWje/dkgXsdwluex+JxGOATU1TUOVpaek5MgClRNpfdoxu1jNnAXARwquXZk\nks4vd/hvA4EMOOUHlrP27y3MnQnoeu3G4ombh013Do1QQoRrEbdM5NL+Qq37kRd2\nx3KztIYS5cKuAJtJjzMuRIEuteeb61izl6UUa68XV4LWGDIBnyAmOtG9BRDXTeEG\nKScJXSBX/d3AYICivzeWZNQcLTEZuAGd3vaLY7pw1g9aBg7VbhO3SDJM543zLfWu\nvo5uBmuTetLCyyXRVr5391gSJwA9y1YS2lW3L0knpP4dQdNgoS35WCFG2wf0PrnH\nSHJw6MHjfOGGyPjJV9lk\n=z472\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 32a562b5513ff77d8e41245640604121a2fffaaf\nparent dacc8b0eadb504a6ddb0d61f84d598a06b45e3a1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784139695 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784139695 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep chat input responsive during MCP viewer `Ctrl+R` reconnect (#4753)\n\nFixed the `/mcp` viewer Ctrl+R reconnect blocking keyboard input until\nthe server finished reconnecting.\n\n---\n\nPressing Ctrl+R inside the `/mcp` viewer to reconnect froze the chat\ninput until the reconnect finished. The handler scheduled\n`_reconnect_from_viewer_safe` with `call_later`, which awaits the\ncoroutine inside the Textual app message pump; the multi-second\n`server_proc.restart()` then stalled the pump so key events were no\nlonger forwarded. Running the reconnect as a detached\n`asyncio.create_task` (mirroring the force-reconnect confirm path) keeps\nthe pump free, so input stays responsive and typed messages queue and\ndrain once the server is ready.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b1d98f23-e279-dc41-4f4f-ce0818900274)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-15T18:21:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/28dc96d08bc057f2e435b557062a819db4191310","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/28dc96d08bc057f2e435b557062a819db4191310","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/28dc96d08bc057f2e435b557062a819db4191310/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dacc8b0eadb504a6ddb0d61f84d598a06b45e3a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dacc8b0eadb504a6ddb0d61f84d598a06b45e3a1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/dacc8b0eadb504a6ddb0d61f84d598a06b45e3a1"}]},{"sha":"dacc8b0eadb504a6ddb0d61f84d598a06b45e3a1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRhY2M4YjBlYWRiNTA0YTZkZGIwZDYxZjg0ZDU5OGEwNmI0NWUzYTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-15T14:42:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T14:42:33Z"},"message":"test(code): isolate conversation history artifacts (#4750)\n\n`test_cli_agent_summarizes` exercises the production local\nconversation-history backend, whose fallback location is the user's\n`~/.deepagents` directory. The test's generated 720 KB payload therefore\nsurvived each run and polluted real user state.\n\nPatch the test helper's offload root to a directory under `tmp_path` and\nassert that the archive is created there. Pytest now removes the\nartifact with the rest of the test directory without changing production\npersistence behavior.\n\nVerified with the full `test_end_to_end.py` unit test file, Ruff, and a\nbefore/after comparison confirming the real conversation-history\ndirectory remains unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"c50084cb179b12e85490aaec1183f5f668d9cc58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c50084cb179b12e85490aaec1183f5f668d9cc58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/dacc8b0eadb504a6ddb0d61f84d598a06b45e3a1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV5xZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO2cQAAQN+6VzxgAyePg4YyWFEyBY\nVjCY3xzOzg5MknZGGri6b/Dj0ngKZUmFr8/VUgn7G2HXhO4SzrtDhcNyos1rS6u/\nCQDbC7OeoyXKEUBwD8UWhbQXxXDCJAeEmf3eXqWQdCrxPzxcAKd5IH8NTHgWoFlW\nOGthc0+Ac1FdhtLXgRYp/Fwks6XWVXCskBENU2Y3DAM47RBIFvTMFuqxUpwBZhef\n9tw3XIGa/WoNlPNQy3BoKj6/zI/ByHFR4wi9Uwu6JIKNh4YSuJM6/ANCF1+mWnqm\nLoFkkjMkVrs+ZRwT/oXdyAxnTHEI1cKUfgU+ymLxwfOESfTm0tv18Uqjj7ivseLM\ng4/DXZidSlnGSHf6k3ocb8c243RrgMiENisCvt7RoZqxDyAKvSj5lUOX6V0ZXLW/\nowvYcPkJ4g22r0V5FoeN3iUuAAJ/3LhVCojXO8lGPDw/FjD/MOoKIVCaSZw5cbHp\nY2hIqP6cklLvWoYm3A3ctENyM+Yfs2ENjIySsN1CNArx1UD5BQA2lDAfwtj/6E+Z\n0WYoDCEn7adbcDTEmn/L03ecNSw3sGv3T8ThLrfbZpqtWe2OS9m3kcm9E0yb8X0R\n99YvgC6/RAIagxHkJxjOR2VVpJzga0XBGT2fdRQKjwlJBrK9ZJWLVJVH0+5+iaPb\n6kHRDj9A1j3+qLBQEyd8\n=ClAP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c50084cb179b12e85490aaec1183f5f668d9cc58\nparent b0beef1fd19367995b16bccf383badbf4fe20be5\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784126553 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784126553 -0400\n\ntest(code): isolate conversation history artifacts (#4750)\n\n`test_cli_agent_summarizes` exercises the production local\nconversation-history backend, whose fallback location is the user's\n`~/.deepagents` directory. The test's generated 720 KB payload therefore\nsurvived each run and polluted real user state.\n\nPatch the test helper's offload root to a directory under `tmp_path` and\nassert that the archive is created there. Pytest now removes the\nartifact with the rest of the test directory without changing production\npersistence behavior.\n\nVerified with the full `test_end_to_end.py` unit test file, Ruff, and a\nbefore/after comparison confirming the real conversation-history\ndirectory remains unchanged.","verified_at":"2026-07-15T14:42:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dacc8b0eadb504a6ddb0d61f84d598a06b45e3a1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/dacc8b0eadb504a6ddb0d61f84d598a06b45e3a1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dacc8b0eadb504a6ddb0d61f84d598a06b45e3a1/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b0beef1fd19367995b16bccf383badbf4fe20be5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b0beef1fd19367995b16bccf383badbf4fe20be5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b0beef1fd19367995b16bccf383badbf4fe20be5"}]},{"sha":"b0beef1fd19367995b16bccf383badbf4fe20be5","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGIwYmVlZjFmZDE5MzY3OTk1YjE2YmNjZjM4M2JhZGJmNGZlMjBiZTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hunter Lovell","email":"40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-15T14:13:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T14:13:52Z"},"message":"test(code): update sandbox overwrite expectation (#4737)\n\nUpdates the deepagents-code sandbox integration suite to match the\ncurrent `write()` contract: writing to an existing file replaces its\ncontents rather than returning an error. This keeps the Python test\nexpectation aligned with the overwrite behavior covered by the\ncorresponding deepagentsjs standard tests.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Rename the existing-file write test to describe overwrite behavior.\n- Assert that the second write succeeds and that the replacement content\nis persisted.\n- Update the sandbox operations module overview to include overwriting\nexisting files.","tree":{"sha":"bbb95a01eb0d1e10df1c8d05554903a766d5d465","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/bbb95a01eb0d1e10df1c8d05554903a766d5d465"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b0beef1fd19367995b16bccf383badbf4fe20be5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV5WgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1K0QADMsQkLiFFP1v9ogIeLMIZrj\nfHrsniXYR0XW4VFly7sewHP31i6C7ynflSGC+TgF2fYkB04JVeyxHLJNYAIcmPrQ\nsIfXmqvtbLu2EqitEOKPPQzvge+IHXCsFNIdiQXUp0KfCG6/ty/ezILyPqJR2LMV\nVYUuv5sAvL/3Kppl2GScOtVG1AJkxiVlHo9l0tu3ppFccgVOynTWD07DSy6ix9+2\nDmFPjHxu7Hq7V1Qu4Vr+tXuViuhqVItaOIOnbl04Vo/h/wSyllyyYmXD9Bfpisja\niiVV4InlHZr4AtTasLcaZj2sKDqtUeCkYrFVa5k/dBjc7FedgJvpMtFUnQa4vJqq\nu+fOOEaMC++y/pz9y2YJgP3BCfqDku08TmYmm2oFe3TH+1lttXXo07Rb7DSZ8Zgf\nfhbmJS70oBIRThc7wYBWybrMK/UlJ3I7efZwKwip23LPqwAL/ZLwyLTz0cA7MPBZ\n6qz5Igo9IYKWcB+MENDLWcZ9OgKaJihabnL8/KTgnxeByoalssPKfxdGDLadCaAC\n7dW4tHjTKQikn6g9h/We3PPcVCkB8xBK/cFwYXwm00ihLcm6qFSiBdGQHjNykIRg\nhdpSG1KkI8ekqZc0BybcADzvJABg25J9tUZtzyt5z1EqXHsX/MbVrPmbQ9WV8cKk\n4PY5vE0KrCMhopeSlFxN\n=XFp7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bbb95a01eb0d1e10df1c8d05554903a766d5d465\nparent 814872492eb2bed4d5c382c6c1fe985ad4354b68\nauthor Hunter Lovell <40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com> 1784124832 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784124832 -0400\n\ntest(code): update sandbox overwrite expectation (#4737)\n\nUpdates the deepagents-code sandbox integration suite to match the\ncurrent `write()` contract: writing to an existing file replaces its\ncontents rather than returning an error. This keeps the Python test\nexpectation aligned with the overwrite behavior covered by the\ncorresponding deepagentsjs standard tests.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Rename the existing-file write test to describe overwrite behavior.\n- Assert that the second write succeeds and that the replacement content\nis persisted.\n- Update the sandbox operations module overview to include overwriting\nexisting files.","verified_at":"2026-07-15T14:13:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b0beef1fd19367995b16bccf383badbf4fe20be5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b0beef1fd19367995b16bccf383badbf4fe20be5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b0beef1fd19367995b16bccf383badbf4fe20be5/comments","author":{"login":"hntrl","id":40191806,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTkxODA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40191806?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl","html_url":"https://github.com/hntrl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"814872492eb2bed4d5c382c6c1fe985ad4354b68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/814872492eb2bed4d5c382c6c1fe985ad4354b68","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/814872492eb2bed4d5c382c6c1fe985ad4354b68"}]},{"sha":"814872492eb2bed4d5c382c6c1fe985ad4354b68","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgxNDg3MjQ5MmViMmJlZDRkNWMzODJjNmMxZmU5ODVhZDQzNTRiNjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-15T14:13:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T14:13:11Z"},"message":"fix(code): surface tool calls awaiting approval (#4739)\n\n`dcode` now surfaces the tool calls that require approval instead of\nhiding them in a collapsed group.\n\n---\n\nApproval-blocked tool calls could remain hidden inside the collapsed\nlive group, leaving only a generic batch prompt. Finalize the active\ngroup at the approval boundary and detach pending rows while preserving\nsingle-command duplicate suppression.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/3f2b94f6-67ee-d5d4-d2a5-250adeacac5e)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"74515fb83e44ff4b82daf504e0367bbea17579ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/74515fb83e44ff4b82daf504e0367bbea17579ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/814872492eb2bed4d5c382c6c1fe985ad4354b68","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV5V3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArZIQABzep33lkYSZP/5FTR/vOu3p\nGizYyJXvtUOhuE+D2zg+IFCY5zmx0hUgSUuaC+eVn+ylk25h1JPX0PEDoRDrv89I\nGD08ySJ3rcmZ9VddD+HsEo/tKj+gxNgQWnLTuDo0ZUrtP+bTeOI51ZL8hOKcMPif\ngHwGaTkR13EpQIa4yCnPKDBq/9zJ/A8hZy65idavlwFG5MM0dKjWToXKeDjrTSPq\noWRwCQiQiMbH1BheCMud2au1So59WTQcmRH4X6BljCIeIgODj+0io4i9LBx4F2AI\nFPu8G34/5jSRTicN6O5+QoGZ+oKvLDyRrP4l3IxbyWq44BZuj10o5qH8cHQLV12q\nMTxsun95TINXs02jlKigkn6/mwB6d4Hq7WHbvZ/tfoJwPH/LSRn5jBHYD/OgEdyv\nPbv2CXqbPaxkJAOBUeIpf+Ybe+q5EQ6DGelaqm0AH/sH7R3AhoX8BSqisOC1yf0O\nZrKBTfMKvdcgzv60s3GaNbWMgn/Yqv1cuU0VNg8iIfGgM2cNl5uxfR0wvJnZaKu3\nPVXZApqyq0j0RfV65mVr1g+YhqlnpPapHqWlUOLRULryyhk6ysoa2BRk66v/9hu4\nGMkbZjAtMbqYiDho8X5kjCczycXcUdUTYE4GMtUT7TUU0xfEsL0ibzai8gmOt3jF\nP7qQ1GFTlDj+nSAwE3PU\n=QyUf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 74515fb83e44ff4b82daf504e0367bbea17579ba\nparent ffab82a9458d2a03b95cbc515f883212090a6992\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1784124791 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784124791 -0400\n\nfix(code): surface tool calls awaiting approval (#4739)\n\n`dcode` now surfaces the tool calls that require approval instead of\nhiding them in a collapsed group.\n\n---\n\nApproval-blocked tool calls could remain hidden inside the collapsed\nlive group, leaving only a generic batch prompt. Finalize the active\ngroup at the approval boundary and detach pending rows while preserving\nsingle-command duplicate suppression.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/3f2b94f6-67ee-d5d4-d2a5-250adeacac5e)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-15T14:13:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/814872492eb2bed4d5c382c6c1fe985ad4354b68","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/814872492eb2bed4d5c382c6c1fe985ad4354b68","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/814872492eb2bed4d5c382c6c1fe985ad4354b68/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ffab82a9458d2a03b95cbc515f883212090a6992","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ffab82a9458d2a03b95cbc515f883212090a6992","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ffab82a9458d2a03b95cbc515f883212090a6992"}]},{"sha":"ffab82a9458d2a03b95cbc515f883212090a6992","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZmYWI4MmE5NDU4ZDJhMDNiOTVjYmM1MTVmODgzMjEyMDkwYTY5OTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-15T14:06:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T14:06:10Z"},"message":"feat(code): add \"always allow\" to project MCP approval prompt (#4562)\n\nThe project MCP server approval prompt now offers an \"always allow\"\noption that saves approved servers to `config.toml`, with an\nall/custom/none picker so you choose exactly which servers to persist.\n\n---\n\nThe project-level MCP server approval prompt (`dcode` startup) only\noffered per-session, fingerprint-based trust. This adds an \"always\nallow\" choice (`a`/`always`) that persists approved servers to\n`[mcp].enabled_project_servers` in the user-level `config.toml`, so they\nload by name on future runs without re-prompting — even if the config\ncontent changes.\n\nRather than presuming the whole list, \"always allow\" now lets you choose\n*which* servers to save via an `[a]ll / [c]ustom / [n]one` menu.\n`custom` reprints the servers numbered and accepts a `1,3`-style\nselection; a single prompted server skips the menu. The writer only ever\ntouches the user's home `config.toml` (never a repo file), preserving\nthe boundary that a committed `.mcp.json` can't self-approve.\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Breaking change (migration)\n\nThis branch evolved past the original design above. As shipped, \"always\nallow\" persists **fingerprint-scoped** approvals under\n`[mcp].enabled_project_server_approvals` (bound to project root +\nserver-definition fingerprint, so a changed command/URL re-prompts) via\nan arrow-key checkbox picker — not the flat, name-based\n`[mcp].enabled_project_servers` list or the `all/custom/none` text menu\ndescribed above.\n\nConsequences for anyone who adopted the previous per-server trust\nfeature (`[mcp].enabled_project_servers`, shipped in `0.1.33`/`0.1.34`):\n\n- The legacy `[mcp].enabled_project_servers` TOML key is now **ignored**\n(a debug-only log warns; the key is preserved on write, not deleted).\n- The env override `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ENABLED_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS` is\nrenamed to `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DANGEROUSLY_ENABLE_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS`\n(still name-based and project-agnostic — the explicit escape hatch).\n- **Interactive `dcode`:** affected servers move back to the approval\nprompt; re-approve once with `a`. Safe, mildly annoying.\n- **Non-interactive / `dcode mcp login`:** affected servers silently\nstop loading (no prompt in these surfaces). Re-run `dcode` in the\nproject to persist a scoped approval, or set\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DANGEROUSLY_ENABLE_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS` to keep the old\nname-based behavior.\n\nThis is fail-closed (no server loads with *less* scrutiny than before),\nso it is a safety-preserving break.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6cb9d698-5a31-5568-306a-9ff7a3f4356b)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"fde345168198020dde8bec815480771a5f84b9c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/fde345168198020dde8bec815480771a5f84b9c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ffab82a9458d2a03b95cbc515f883212090a6992","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV5PSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQZIQABi/sR6DqZraNGLqK0ALz35v\n6zBngUamBXSQzyTChrVsxa+q4c//Hczd4s7WvkbVsdWDlZRcJzqJ+Zc8aVUwqpND\n+F45qE0nQAcNANisiWPsW20+3EaGlu1B8ARvs3HN237FFWibT8N1s5hyBGPduMTi\nb6OkOR2PbbO94uUQokr4Tqz9Bw/8OLNr9XE8KtoitLbUnEs5vnHoiQO3tI9a9mQO\nV5t81UZTw99rxxo2ptya5v7MnLFL8KYqdNfd0wRC2ggg/QAHaiFhgTXjTt2pb+Ma\nSSyI9IO2SazFLKgO1ISBsQON7Hl+wwWf8j42xzM5aVF+Gr3gy5MRt8XmTHIOfHXs\n/GzV7ONk2Z6WY7teNAPuzslRmHt7ZrrDVBaGDDW2Z9BpSC+bx70pGOcg5cGVKA89\nVsCv/PpduIUpSNYnlvKL4QnZEkbjPiOAj1PNokL3WJpjWMvBJyACTg3JIWNebvYd\n/XgxDyhcbsV7in5XxwaM9pKycMBuhgqlq833wajrFG80AHN5xRKHuQ8JnWnYTdju\nPWIaf/An+476IUUBnNapmuSXSMyDCMIZY6O+lqoHoR6ELCBGV9ESo13+PbQxWEnY\nD9lT38BH1n71F3OrfUCxoSJQdflw3E9Vv6oWimUV64BYA/X0/3NI1YsZuaCW/qxb\nVwp5amiDX7iMTzibTJkj\n=i7ZD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fde345168198020dde8bec815480771a5f84b9c6\nparent 36c40241b85ec5b0452d9ca334e5f09b95dc16aa\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784124370 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784124370 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add \"always allow\" to project MCP approval prompt (#4562)\n\nThe project MCP server approval prompt now offers an \"always allow\"\noption that saves approved servers to `config.toml`, with an\nall/custom/none picker so you choose exactly which servers to persist.\n\n---\n\nThe project-level MCP server approval prompt (`dcode` startup) only\noffered per-session, fingerprint-based trust. This adds an \"always\nallow\" choice (`a`/`always`) that persists approved servers to\n`[mcp].enabled_project_servers` in the user-level `config.toml`, so they\nload by name on future runs without re-prompting — even if the config\ncontent changes.\n\nRather than presuming the whole list, \"always allow\" now lets you choose\n*which* servers to save via an `[a]ll / [c]ustom / [n]one` menu.\n`custom` reprints the servers numbered and accepts a `1,3`-style\nselection; a single prompted server skips the menu. The writer only ever\ntouches the user's home `config.toml` (never a repo file), preserving\nthe boundary that a committed `.mcp.json` can't self-approve.\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Breaking change (migration)\n\nThis branch evolved past the original design above. As shipped, \"always\nallow\" persists **fingerprint-scoped** approvals under\n`[mcp].enabled_project_server_approvals` (bound to project root +\nserver-definition fingerprint, so a changed command/URL re-prompts) via\nan arrow-key checkbox picker — not the flat, name-based\n`[mcp].enabled_project_servers` list or the `all/custom/none` text menu\ndescribed above.\n\nConsequences for anyone who adopted the previous per-server trust\nfeature (`[mcp].enabled_project_servers`, shipped in `0.1.33`/`0.1.34`):\n\n- The legacy `[mcp].enabled_project_servers` TOML key is now **ignored**\n(a debug-only log warns; the key is preserved on write, not deleted).\n- The env override `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ENABLED_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS` is\nrenamed to `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DANGEROUSLY_ENABLE_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS`\n(still name-based and project-agnostic — the explicit escape hatch).\n- **Interactive `dcode`:** affected servers move back to the approval\nprompt; re-approve once with `a`. Safe, mildly annoying.\n- **Non-interactive / `dcode mcp login`:** affected servers silently\nstop loading (no prompt in these surfaces). Re-run `dcode` in the\nproject to persist a scoped approval, or set\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DANGEROUSLY_ENABLE_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS` to keep the old\nname-based behavior.\n\nThis is fail-closed (no server loads with *less* scrutiny than before),\nso it is a safety-preserving break.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6cb9d698-5a31-5568-306a-9ff7a3f4356b)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-15T14:06:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ffab82a9458d2a03b95cbc515f883212090a6992","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ffab82a9458d2a03b95cbc515f883212090a6992","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ffab82a9458d2a03b95cbc515f883212090a6992/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"36c40241b85ec5b0452d9ca334e5f09b95dc16aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/36c40241b85ec5b0452d9ca334e5f09b95dc16aa","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/36c40241b85ec5b0452d9ca334e5f09b95dc16aa"}]},{"sha":"36c40241b85ec5b0452d9ca334e5f09b95dc16aa","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM2YzQwMjQxYjg1ZWM1YjA0NTJkOWNhMzM0ZTVmMDliOTVkYzE2YWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-15T13:49:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T13:49:39Z"},"message":"fix(code): targeted uv constraints for dcode prerelease deps (#4744)\n\nCloses #4524\n\n`dcode` updates that require a prerelease SDK dependency no longer allow\nunrelated optional providers to install prerelease versions, avoiding\nfailed upgrades from unbuildable release candidates.\n\n---\n\nStable `deepagents-code` releases can intentionally require an exact\nprerelease hard dependency (e.g. `deepagents==0.7.0a7`). The updater\nhandled this by adding a global `--prerelease allow`, which widens the\nresolver's candidate set for *every* package — so an unrelated optional\nprovider could float to an unbuildable prerelease. That is what caused\n#4524 (a `litellm` RC failing to build on Python 3.14).\n\n`perform_upgrade()` now identifies the mandatory, unconditional, exact\nprerelease pins from the target release's PyPI metadata, writes them to\na temporary uv constraints file, and runs with `--constraints <file>\n--prerelease if-necessary-or-explicit`. uv then admits only the named\nprerelease (e.g. the SDK alpha) while unrelated optional dependencies\nstay on their stable releases. The exact dcode target pin, installed\nextras, receipt `--with` packages, interpreter selection, and\ntransactional uv-tool behavior are all preserved. The explicit dcode\nprerelease-*channel* path (installed prerelease or `--prerelease`) is\nunchanged and still uses `--prerelease allow`.\n\nThe marker-agnostic boolean cache (`release_requires_prereleases`) is\nredesigned into a structured, versioned per-version pin cache\n(`release_prerelease_pins`); the legacy boolean key is never read as\nauthoritative. `release_requires_prereleases()` is kept as a\nbackward-compatible boolean wrapper for the display-only callers in\n`app.py`/`main.py`. The requirement classifier is deliberately limited\nto unconditional exact pins — marker-bearing pins (extra-gated or\ninterpreter/platform-gated) are ignored rather than evaluated against a\npossibly-wrong interpreter; this limit is documented in code and tests.\n\nConstraint-file lifecycle is a context manager: the file lives for the\nfull subprocess invocation and is removed in `finally`, tolerating\ncleanup errors without masking the install result. A\nconstraint-generation failure leaves the existing install untouched and\nreturns actionable output rather than silently reverting to a global\nallow.\n\nAudit of other receipt-aware/global-allow paths (scoped follow-ups, not\nfixed here to avoid broad refactoring and offline-install regressions):\n- `install_extra` / `install_package` build commands unconditionally use\n`--prerelease allow`; they pin the current version, so converting them\nsafely needs the same targeted-constraint plumbing plus offline-fallback\nhandling.\n- `dependency_refresh` only adds `--prerelease allow` when following the\nprerelease channel, so it does not exhibit the metadata-driven\nglobal-allow bug for stable installs (it fails safe instead).\n- `scripts/install.sh` still defaults `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_PRERELEASE=allow`\nfor fresh installs; porting the targeted strategy to bash is a larger\ninstaller change with its own tests.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/90a3f170-5a1a-ed8b-3c37-d97d6021c97d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"abc3f610fd1487757110701bdec83eb06135f540","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/abc3f610fd1487757110701bdec83eb06135f540"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/36c40241b85ec5b0452d9ca334e5f09b95dc16aa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV4/zCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjiYQAChn6fQCHzTpMi3hMDT2iRaI\nGeaPQ+X1O9te0p6kG5hpZBXb/F5Qp4hs7/qUzLOj9JVffQ4RnBLntiZHiS7ybvxw\nJdudl1r1ctKSAAzFNbKCA9PqtuI3tzKm9juIYImH9CCcCVMo5osyzzsMBV3UAiCB\nfIn2V3xc9dvch5gvt0GSe7u9ELC3Ws6WHAqmju4oEmRae9KOEczrzaHFhfS4TUxG\nRXM/HP6W2bgOqvv8522dLbnGbrVLmyQxDj7wz2hVWYbRRzawVLPPn7aZ73lI0+nM\n8zJz8/W7+BLZ3VeRb56sAzyQd/WUvZc7cFf9u/3UV/Z47RBmpELWkY0mDBQRgMfR\nAE9mbx9bR1I6O12+F46IDLmYzbxKt/kX1gn9EQiKkJMab1qIvawA7nvpwimSHXCo\nORXbx3a1jupAg9VXMpZU+IMu3LZGuJOwQRWwFJvBXgasPmoHy50Sxz4Y/hq8rji/\nnrjb46HU2Z0IwaofYBHewde2eDNGmbLMIGUpTcDvJA5zPWurJKjL9PPx6xOEHH6Q\n4SnlWQreqghTbZEZHe+2MecLpiBxDtcmqUl+3MeGWBGwGuBiQ9lfYcqzIMz2EHJj\nv7pEgtTGcMch1yARXu+KYZrZcvURO+gxNNNlM6njuG3PUjUr9am4VAnnI7uQr4fu\ntarFa7X+pIauU6xT2rUb\n=ILUn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree abc3f610fd1487757110701bdec83eb06135f540\nparent 36051e2a6cdcd9c22f6118f5cfc481e0540913ea\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784123379 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784123379 -0400\n\nfix(code): targeted uv constraints for dcode prerelease deps (#4744)\n\nCloses #4524\n\n`dcode` updates that require a prerelease SDK dependency no longer allow\nunrelated optional providers to install prerelease versions, avoiding\nfailed upgrades from unbuildable release candidates.\n\n---\n\nStable `deepagents-code` releases can intentionally require an exact\nprerelease hard dependency (e.g. `deepagents==0.7.0a7`). The updater\nhandled this by adding a global `--prerelease allow`, which widens the\nresolver's candidate set for *every* package — so an unrelated optional\nprovider could float to an unbuildable prerelease. That is what caused\n#4524 (a `litellm` RC failing to build on Python 3.14).\n\n`perform_upgrade()` now identifies the mandatory, unconditional, exact\nprerelease pins from the target release's PyPI metadata, writes them to\na temporary uv constraints file, and runs with `--constraints <file>\n--prerelease if-necessary-or-explicit`. uv then admits only the named\nprerelease (e.g. the SDK alpha) while unrelated optional dependencies\nstay on their stable releases. The exact dcode target pin, installed\nextras, receipt `--with` packages, interpreter selection, and\ntransactional uv-tool behavior are all preserved. The explicit dcode\nprerelease-*channel* path (installed prerelease or `--prerelease`) is\nunchanged and still uses `--prerelease allow`.\n\nThe marker-agnostic boolean cache (`release_requires_prereleases`) is\nredesigned into a structured, versioned per-version pin cache\n(`release_prerelease_pins`); the legacy boolean key is never read as\nauthoritative. `release_requires_prereleases()` is kept as a\nbackward-compatible boolean wrapper for the display-only callers in\n`app.py`/`main.py`. The requirement classifier is deliberately limited\nto unconditional exact pins — marker-bearing pins (extra-gated or\ninterpreter/platform-gated) are ignored rather than evaluated against a\npossibly-wrong interpreter; this limit is documented in code and tests.\n\nConstraint-file lifecycle is a context manager: the file lives for the\nfull subprocess invocation and is removed in `finally`, tolerating\ncleanup errors without masking the install result. A\nconstraint-generation failure leaves the existing install untouched and\nreturns actionable output rather than silently reverting to a global\nallow.\n\nAudit of other receipt-aware/global-allow paths (scoped follow-ups, not\nfixed here to avoid broad refactoring and offline-install regressions):\n- `install_extra` / `install_package` build commands unconditionally use\n`--prerelease allow`; they pin the current version, so converting them\nsafely needs the same targeted-constraint plumbing plus offline-fallback\nhandling.\n- `dependency_refresh` only adds `--prerelease allow` when following the\nprerelease channel, so it does not exhibit the metadata-driven\nglobal-allow bug for stable installs (it fails safe instead).\n- `scripts/install.sh` still defaults `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_PRERELEASE=allow`\nfor fresh installs; porting the targeted strategy to bash is a larger\ninstaller change with its own tests.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/90a3f170-5a1a-ed8b-3c37-d97d6021c97d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-15T13:49:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/36c40241b85ec5b0452d9ca334e5f09b95dc16aa","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/36c40241b85ec5b0452d9ca334e5f09b95dc16aa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/36c40241b85ec5b0452d9ca334e5f09b95dc16aa/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"36051e2a6cdcd9c22f6118f5cfc481e0540913ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/36051e2a6cdcd9c22f6118f5cfc481e0540913ea","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/36051e2a6cdcd9c22f6118f5cfc481e0540913ea"}]},{"sha":"36051e2a6cdcd9c22f6118f5cfc481e0540913ea","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM2MDUxZTJhNmNkY2Q5YzIyZjYxMThmNWNmYzQ4MWUwNTQwOTEzZWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-15T13:24:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T13:24:20Z"},"message":"fix(code): put local offloaded tool results on the real filesystem (#4740)\n\nIn dcode local mode, offloaded large tool results previously lived\nbehind a virtual `CompositeBackend` route backed by a hidden `mkdtemp`\n`FilesystemBackend`. Because `execute` always runs on the default\nbackend (never path-routed), the agent could not open those results with\n`jq`/`grep`/`python` by the path it was handed — the\n`/large_tool_results/` prefix wasn't a real inode, and the temp root was\nintentionally hidden.\n\nThis points `CompositeBackend.artifacts_root` at a stable, hardened\nper-user temp dir and drops the `/large_tool_results/` route, so\noffloaded results fall through to the default `LocalShellBackend` at a\nreal path. The agent can now inspect them with `execute` using the exact\npath the offload message hands it — no virtual-path translation, no\ncopy-out/in. Conversation history keeps a dedicated route to persistent\n`~/.deepagents` storage so `/offload` archives survive restarts, and its\naddress stays stable across restarts because the artifacts root is\ndeterministic per user.\n\nThis uses the existing `artifacts_root` support on `CompositeBackend`\n(already consumed by both the filesystem and summarization middleware),\nso it is a dcode-only change with no SDK edit. The artifacts dir is\ncreated `0o700` with an ownership/`S_ISDIR` guard and falls back to a\nprivate unique dir if the predictable path is squatted; consolidating on\none per-user dir also removes the old unbounded `mkdtemp`-per-session\nleak.\n\nThe rubric grader's read allow-list now derives its permitted prefix\nfrom `artifacts_root` rather than a hardcoded `/large_tool_results/`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e815e778-3188-4f2e-1068-e52819c024a7)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e815e778-3188-4f2e-1068-e52819c024a7/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4bf0a20abe7843cedd75b714f90cf07602da8b9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4bf0a20abe7843cedd75b714f90cf07602da8b9f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/36051e2a6cdcd9c22f6118f5cfc481e0540913ea","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV4oECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABFIQABYWE+8hHs5OB5ZQC+TVP4zs\nbCF+QH2+fcIyl7BSUWZlfkvm7fKeDgJYeEZoP8plFlvbk0qN6SwZBuFaQjWlyD45\nNQHukfJqFM4AlMRc9h2Rt3g5jyIJcRfAdNQ7JhFznngGv7hS0Oj5ZComp1qZPvYY\nkJc3SpUHLzxVaT9hUU0F8Obwok/BONo7lD2Bq5MxN0k0W4F4vT8TSeT9XmZ/y6YH\n+EyxC6OrQoM44ZqJhIDB2x1/LciwK/VpRUoZjc8V6t2wtPIX0LZOUyXOp1eK4iId\ntXTA18HI5mDWSiZjBMsBeHLGhkQexI4+t81oO36k4kgmtahscKC/ghd6SsnB5R1M\nqJh9a+VjXCx8Ot2mNpwfrGtBE9+SjcMmj+0yKxbN8yVcTso/5ZzcISqmovN6mPCi\ngPH3aHagXykUFFPO5KmkdAI4OgSHExeu0drU4kjzY2fT8s1yRzFYhLYKVOYbFYpt\nmOfI6cT73HvbpKpjtiOymoLEkKpyDRasvdDh3p0d/SRiWBL7Xh6f87g7VRgA9M0t\nLZCssnbGpfVTvRBzYTfwWlqy+CPOzki147vL8/OlNm6G5cZaiwfXqm1ymmQHaqkU\nUQ50m//1yz3hLTDRZPj29tSPnY6AtLivbFx4ePwAQ+MHxsfa19/wwy6hQsPhDOVa\n+5o+mQWx5bIlptAh0I63\n=E8b1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4bf0a20abe7843cedd75b714f90cf07602da8b9f\nparent 0187d14b83301c116a2f177e6e04ae7a8cc99ca7\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784121860 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784121860 -0400\n\nfix(code): put local offloaded tool results on the real filesystem (#4740)\n\nIn dcode local mode, offloaded large tool results previously lived\nbehind a virtual `CompositeBackend` route backed by a hidden `mkdtemp`\n`FilesystemBackend`. Because `execute` always runs on the default\nbackend (never path-routed), the agent could not open those results with\n`jq`/`grep`/`python` by the path it was handed — the\n`/large_tool_results/` prefix wasn't a real inode, and the temp root was\nintentionally hidden.\n\nThis points `CompositeBackend.artifacts_root` at a stable, hardened\nper-user temp dir and drops the `/large_tool_results/` route, so\noffloaded results fall through to the default `LocalShellBackend` at a\nreal path. The agent can now inspect them with `execute` using the exact\npath the offload message hands it — no virtual-path translation, no\ncopy-out/in. Conversation history keeps a dedicated route to persistent\n`~/.deepagents` storage so `/offload` archives survive restarts, and its\naddress stays stable across restarts because the artifacts root is\ndeterministic per user.\n\nThis uses the existing `artifacts_root` support on `CompositeBackend`\n(already consumed by both the filesystem and summarization middleware),\nso it is a dcode-only change with no SDK edit. The artifacts dir is\ncreated `0o700` with an ownership/`S_ISDIR` guard and falls back to a\nprivate unique dir if the predictable path is squatted; consolidating on\none per-user dir also removes the old unbounded `mkdtemp`-per-session\nleak.\n\nThe rubric grader's read allow-list now derives its permitted prefix\nfrom `artifacts_root` rather than a hardcoded `/large_tool_results/`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e815e778-3188-4f2e-1068-e52819c024a7)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e815e778-3188-4f2e-1068-e52819c024a7/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-15T13:24:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/36051e2a6cdcd9c22f6118f5cfc481e0540913ea","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/36051e2a6cdcd9c22f6118f5cfc481e0540913ea","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/36051e2a6cdcd9c22f6118f5cfc481e0540913ea/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0187d14b83301c116a2f177e6e04ae7a8cc99ca7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0187d14b83301c116a2f177e6e04ae7a8cc99ca7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0187d14b83301c116a2f177e6e04ae7a8cc99ca7"}]},{"sha":"0187d14b83301c116a2f177e6e04ae7a8cc99ca7","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDAxODdkMTRiODMzMDFjMTE2YTJmMTc3ZTZlMDRhZTdhOGNjOTljYTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-15T13:11:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T13:11:28Z"},"message":"feat(code): add plugin marketplace support (#4554)\n\n`deepagents-code` now supports experimental plugin marketplaces with\nnamespaced skills and MCP servers. Enable with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL=1`.\n\nDocs: https://github.com/langchain-ai/docs/pull/4905\n\n---\n\n`deepagents-code` can now manage experimental plugin marketplaces and\nload installed plugins that contribute namespaced skills and MCP\nservers. The new plugin manager establishes the `tui/modals`,\n`tui/screens`, and `tui/widgets` UI convention, with colocated styling\nand focused state/content modules.\n\n- Supports local, GitHub, Git, and marketplace JSON sources.\n- Adds install, enable, disable, uninstall, and safe marketplace removal\nthrough `/plugins` and `dcode plugin`.\n- Reloads plugin skills and plugin MCP configuration with `/reload` when\nexperimental mode is enabled.\n- Namespaces plugin skills as `{plugin_id}:{skill_name}` through a\ncode-local `PluginSkillsMiddleware` adapter, so no SDK changes are\nrequired.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/019f5dea-0f1f-73fe-9803-32d1b13fbd4c)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Olsen <aolsenjazz@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <215916821+open-swe[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"2475989c7ffa14935db3b2bf18d4ffe9b4abfbdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2475989c7ffa14935db3b2bf18d4ffe9b4abfbdc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0187d14b83301c116a2f177e6e04ae7a8cc99ca7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV4cACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHDwQABl2R6qCaA8Zp1mve4ffctHH\nVLrszRK/B9flKa5HdDojynj43Wdr3UkPctOYry2iUqm06KbLerEHOMaND7zL90p2\nt4g11YtNxh6qTz/ovF+3HGwwWX6SMhaMqg4o3w3LPM0yc/y2oWg0kolxkB5J20zO\nBEIuV5DUjkYSXNtD65q6iKKOFqxelzS20Agtbd6rUUhAkxUh3/WiXQB1CC9gH+2l\n3HDPPhNkLb3on2DTr9tgs5nW0S4298NzakHHZO22U/9+yjUPEn0aEtekBAn2P2/1\nsz8UGp3Ti56dimZCh6RGiuqqZSNCXnWDdL0Ab8wZBfb6hxYD/OTJqHgqtmF1u4N2\nL7mUzUHjevJzm9d8ylArLlkwMGNBAYCYK8VITD8xJwN1Y51SdIT6ziFf9zRK6sfb\nK9LGJd7WgGF7foJaJx8Pt18F+KiIUJJi3L2sKNdKhcx8sTT3KcT8re9idyQmHE5/\nLPrVhiT3wMRmzDy2loOTodmRRiTjfmVJwAVpK6GqC3ZHPlSpQMAqCcA1VjlYO3Tk\nlVTVohDpF5Yf4wVsqRnaGTy0FRAFXQ0SfNOEzzaM6HVZjJhjFOcTiRQIDQtIZl3R\nufoYe4EBLpoiHk26b43FNziam8nFgaToGFNa1hve+26BO2VcR0bh3ci+9ygzy4WA\nsxKSoCQlou4+M/Rsvp5N\n=+fnD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2475989c7ffa14935db3b2bf18d4ffe9b4abfbdc\nparent 9a6789ac19c48f8289593e92a3e34ffa8d201190\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1784121088 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784121088 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add plugin marketplace support (#4554)\n\n`deepagents-code` now supports experimental plugin marketplaces with\nnamespaced skills and MCP servers. Enable with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL=1`.\n\nDocs: https://github.com/langchain-ai/docs/pull/4905\n\n---\n\n`deepagents-code` can now manage experimental plugin marketplaces and\nload installed plugins that contribute namespaced skills and MCP\nservers. The new plugin manager establishes the `tui/modals`,\n`tui/screens`, and `tui/widgets` UI convention, with colocated styling\nand focused state/content modules.\n\n- Supports local, GitHub, Git, and marketplace JSON sources.\n- Adds install, enable, disable, uninstall, and safe marketplace removal\nthrough `/plugins` and `dcode plugin`.\n- Reloads plugin skills and plugin MCP configuration with `/reload` when\nexperimental mode is enabled.\n- Namespaces plugin skills as `{plugin_id}:{skill_name}` through a\ncode-local `PluginSkillsMiddleware` adapter, so no SDK changes are\nrequired.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/019f5dea-0f1f-73fe-9803-32d1b13fbd4c)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Olsen <aolsenjazz@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <215916821+open-swe[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-15T13:11:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0187d14b83301c116a2f177e6e04ae7a8cc99ca7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0187d14b83301c116a2f177e6e04ae7a8cc99ca7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0187d14b83301c116a2f177e6e04ae7a8cc99ca7/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9a6789ac19c48f8289593e92a3e34ffa8d201190","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9a6789ac19c48f8289593e92a3e34ffa8d201190","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9a6789ac19c48f8289593e92a3e34ffa8d201190"}]},{"sha":"9a6789ac19c48f8289593e92a3e34ffa8d201190","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDlhNjc4OWFjMTljNDhmODI4OTU5M2U5MmEzZTM0ZmZhOGQyMDExOTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alexander Olsen","email":"aolsenjazz@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-15T12:43:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T12:43:34Z"},"message":"chore(code): document UI component organization (#4707)\n\nCondenses the dcode UI file/folder conventions into durable agent\nguidance. It covers component directories, helper locality, stylesheet\nownership, and parent-child boundaries for new UI without mandating\nrefactors.\n\nVerified with `git diff --check`; documentation-only change.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/86e93c33-cf6f-b179-0a45-78ec90327b81)\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Olsen <13665641+aolsenjazz@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"71e5689fb75c0542cc9283787694eb88849cce73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/71e5689fb75c0542cc9283787694eb88849cce73"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9a6789ac19c48f8289593e92a3e34ffa8d201190","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV4B2CRC1aQ7uu5