n one line:\n`Previous thread: <id> (Resume with /threads -r)`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/ff603262-ead9-cde0-eca0-bb4deefda2f4)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T22:54:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/132f9f7a3059e67927beaac96fe841b7f132a8a3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/132f9f7a3059e67927beaac96fe841b7f132a8a3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/132f9f7a3059e67927beaac96fe841b7f132a8a3/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"625e601da8cd77e13b98b2b81626f320478108dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/625e601da8cd77e13b98b2b81626f320478108dc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/625e601da8cd77e13b98b2b81626f320478108dc"}]},{"sha":"625e601da8cd77e13b98b2b81626f320478108dc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDYyNWU2MDFkYThjZDc3ZTEzYjk4YjJiODE2MjZmMzIwNDc4MTA4ZGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T21:57:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T21:57:33Z"},"message":"fix(code): close subprocess transport on install teardown (#4735)\n\n`_terminate_install_process` reaped the install subprocess but never\nclosed its transport. On the timeout/cancellation paths stdout/stderr\nare abandoned before cleanup, so the pipes never reach EOF and the\n`BaseSubprocessTransport` lingers until GC — and if the event loop has\nclosed by then, `__del__` retries the close on a dead loop and raises\n`RuntimeError: Event loop is closed`, surfaced as a\n`PytestUnraisableExceptionWarning` (GC-attributed to whichever test is\nrunning, hence the timing/version sensitivity). Fix closes the transport\neagerly while the loop is still alive.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b9f0f3c9-273c-9b06-d5c9-e9dc9ca9ca2f)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5dbc97daeefd35aa19a219ed65912e4cde482239","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5dbc97daeefd35aa19a219ed65912e4cde482239"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/625e601da8cd77e13b98b2b81626f320478108dc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVrDNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATWwQALCj8SpUrD9AOJf9xC8XF40e\nCXerM16/fjW8loGoyL0YEjv7nu9oNbxtV6T5zypQK1uLUwKlQ1Ij6UlXAtzjgfDz\nJMfwuVWzqA1y8uXaESpepo5OKWLIj7zYTDEFSUVxRQmYYhUOE7Y+MgCbQzH1RH92\nqV8L2TQSx5kbZfroJskDSfMEpPbXv7xrQDVQ+UXOgQTIZMAnT5SFx3m9VbwdQ0AZ\n5hh2sAz2G8NEEHvS34856hFlFHf2Sgn6JjnWoxCdMbe/Q8tJN4mPLPg7+lG9jLVH\naRKvTC91shRzUQPrpuxGJPvYFAyJuLy/FnlP/wqz14irVS57VkvDqSo0Px3mGC0S\nmxwG3cvNIXIM+50lkCn6dCD5qcfvX4UAl0BAL14eNZOpVVgmJSljLf75wGwfSTvq\nDzvsiT5Q+xd7XmUo0k4f8k+jgfHAE4nzBfnlGjaeq4jjPs98L7oTRN4tY0b6BTkz\n7R1zOBIZ+9+Gr/1nFEZ6dY1WMCulDwmSNVbrttn7SvaLWJrJeNjNjigdQIxEf3BD\nzoH0FwF0jpzDMncyVhAEvOCCVsdnHpF2dIE3v2NpFNc3EC8T6sQLJ9kJKkOjf8Qo\nON5vg941lwk2mvUu/0/U/OifxcxnejCXLy6AkO5o4hFcv96u/6BG7WmqNtz6P+PZ\na7gkr4tmVhTtUxKSVI9B\n=pA/V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5dbc97daeefd35aa19a219ed65912e4cde482239\nparent 369ec6920af35cdec713b9e27d0d1816cafaf556\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784066253 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784066253 -0400\n\nfix(code): close subprocess transport on install teardown (#4735)\n\n`_terminate_install_process` reaped the install subprocess but never\nclosed its transport. On the timeout/cancellation paths stdout/stderr\nare abandoned before cleanup, so the pipes never reach EOF and the\n`BaseSubprocessTransport` lingers until GC — and if the event loop has\nclosed by then, `__del__` retries the close on a dead loop and raises\n`RuntimeError: Event loop is closed`, surfaced as a\n`PytestUnraisableExceptionWarning` (GC-attributed to whichever test is\nrunning, hence the timing/version sensitivity). Fix closes the transport\neagerly while the loop is still alive.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b9f0f3c9-273c-9b06-d5c9-e9dc9ca9ca2f)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T21:57:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/625e601da8cd77e13b98b2b81626f320478108dc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/625e601da8cd77e13b98b2b81626f320478108dc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/625e601da8cd77e13b98b2b81626f320478108dc/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"369ec6920af35cdec713b9e27d0d1816cafaf556","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/369ec6920af35cdec713b9e27d0d1816cafaf556","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/369ec6920af35cdec713b9e27d0d1816cafaf556"}]},{"sha":"369ec6920af35cdec713b9e27d0d1816cafaf556","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM2OWVjNjkyMGFmMzVjZGVjNzEzYjllMjdkMGQxODE2Y2FmYWY1NTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T21:50:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T21:50:16Z"},"message":"fix(code): share paste handling with inline free-text prompts (#4736)\n\nPasting into the inline ask-user and goal-review text fields now matches\nthe main input: multi-line pastes stay grouped instead of submitting\nearly, and large pastes collapse into a compact placeholder that expands\nto the full text on submit.\n\n---\n\nFollowing [#4724](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4724),\nthe inline free-text prompts (`AskUserTextArea`, `GoalReviewTextArea`)\nshould match the primary agent input. They didn't for paste: they fell\nback to bare `TextArea` insert, so a multi-line paste replayed as key\nevents could submit mid-stream (inline Enter submits), and large pastes\nwere never collapsed.\n\nThis extracts the chat input's paste-burst detection + Enter-suppression\nwindow and the large-paste collapse + placeholder storage into a shared\n`_paste_textarea` module (`PasteBurstTextArea` and\n`CollapsingPasteTextArea`), the single source of truth for the burst\nconstants and mechanism. `ChatTextArea` now subclasses the burst base —\nkeeping its owner-routed dispatch, history, slash-command, and media\nhandling — so its behavior is unchanged. `InlinePromptTextArea` gains:\nmulti-line pastes stay grouped instead of submitting on the first\nembedded newline, and a large paste collapses into a compact `[Pasted\ntext #N]` placeholder (atomically deletable) that expands to the full\ntext on submit via `submitted_value`. `ask_user` and goal review read\nthe expanded value so the agent receives the full pasted content, and\nthe same `collapse_pastes` setting is honored.\n\nImage/video *attachment* stays out of scope for inline fields: their\nresults are plain strings with no multimodal path, so parity here means\n\"no breakage / no premature submit,\" not attachment.\n\nReviewers: the main risk area is the `ChatTextArea` refactor onto the\nshared burst base — the existing chat-input paste tests were updated to\npatch the burst constants at their new home and all pass.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/39dd0369-5eba-9ec7-a376-a3c0347fbbf8)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/39dd0369-5eba-9ec7-a376-a3c0347fbbf8/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"fb71a73cfceff7e1734d8208316e09602d308786","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/fb71a73cfceff7e1734d8208316e09602d308786"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/369ec6920af35cdec713b9e27d0d1816cafaf556","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVq8YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWrcQAHHPBKRnB97du/a+d0YEcXhU\n/2GdrLJQzKU4ypLZKh21tIgo0yNSXmMKZ7ZpZazhywpQh3wLwFJDJJ9+gf8ZHhdA\n7eJSbtQ9FNWRs0cPsA2nB4L1i6zzlnB3ZhRXp3914iCXBWuBn9Qg92JDzCJWPNs2\nZara8+i6lw3jEr6fXH84GiX4KuCkoEikP6A54cvJ/RuDPUrb2XJ9M/dGxK4pGVIV\neXul1C3WfoqpoiB1AfLUZWM/wl4OTmdHpiL+NF/r6o0T3nIF6PrSACgiUBIfDfzg\nY0s6dXlXO6+Jq0bA+zufdeI7xKhJ3fQZf0Ni3Z2ELKnWLeWuS2q+NmPDRIcZU8e4\n/R6uTZRierwNKSWzzbzaEqizf5gLsERg+uoFOaDfp/7bbmBalybPJBK2xTUktiGS\n0mggCXvyJ/c33DEEmgtk3TFMljA4Yl2PvH2YaVQvjd3viGbIqSfsSZ9Pjb9J89hf\niExweKz0eVX2FfL24vWn3J7j1wDVNX88oIFeieGJQhkzOnNDKge3hf4LKCrprFYY\nSv5J1ATU6bQd1SI2NoUcJHn/KOaDPLGHG/hosfhoDLbRFLtc7AwxkvbwMzgMDSmw\nvtBU15iB3FhSDsBj4oLND/lEAI38jYGEoQPBHI1hVhnbyTu1ikJkt2LvfrT+Jj4D\naMT+vNphBepfhFvpE+ed\n=Q640\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fb71a73cfceff7e1734d8208316e09602d308786\nparent d8038e33c6bc3eec32bb221f4cb2d83926e70ad1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784065816 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784065816 -0400\n\nfix(code): share paste handling with inline free-text prompts (#4736)\n\nPasting into the inline ask-user and goal-review text fields now matches\nthe main input: multi-line pastes stay grouped instead of submitting\nearly, and large pastes collapse into a compact placeholder that expands\nto the full text on submit.\n\n---\n\nFollowing [#4724](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4724),\nthe inline free-text prompts (`AskUserTextArea`, `GoalReviewTextArea`)\nshould match the primary agent input. They didn't for paste: they fell\nback to bare `TextArea` insert, so a multi-line paste replayed as key\nevents could submit mid-stream (inline Enter submits), and large pastes\nwere never collapsed.\n\nThis extracts the chat input's paste-burst detection + Enter-suppression\nwindow and the large-paste collapse + placeholder storage into a shared\n`_paste_textarea` module (`PasteBurstTextArea` and\n`CollapsingPasteTextArea`), the single source of truth for the burst\nconstants and mechanism. `ChatTextArea` now subclasses the burst base —\nkeeping its owner-routed dispatch, history, slash-command, and media\nhandling — so its behavior is unchanged. `InlinePromptTextArea` gains:\nmulti-line pastes stay grouped instead of submitting on the first\nembedded newline, and a large paste collapses into a compact `[Pasted\ntext #N]` placeholder (atomically deletable) that expands to the full\ntext on submit via `submitted_value`. `ask_user` and goal review read\nthe expanded value so the agent receives the full pasted content, and\nthe same `collapse_pastes` setting is honored.\n\nImage/video *attachment* stays out of scope for inline fields: their\nresults are plain strings with no multimodal path, so parity here means\n\"no breakage / no premature submit,\" not attachment.\n\nReviewers: the main risk area is the `ChatTextArea` refactor onto the\nshared burst base — the existing chat-input paste tests were updated to\npatch the burst constants at their new home and all pass.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/39dd0369-5eba-9ec7-a376-a3c0347fbbf8)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/39dd0369-5eba-9ec7-a376-a3c0347fbbf8/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T21:50:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/369ec6920af35cdec713b9e27d0d1816cafaf556","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/369ec6920af35cdec713b9e27d0d1816cafaf556","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/369ec6920af35cdec713b9e27d0d1816cafaf556/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d8038e33c6bc3eec32bb221f4cb2d83926e70ad1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d8038e33c6bc3eec32bb221f4cb2d83926e70ad1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d8038e33c6bc3eec32bb221f4cb2d83926e70ad1"}]},{"sha":"d8038e33c6bc3eec32bb221f4cb2d83926e70ad1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ4MDM4ZTMzYzZiYzNlZWMzMmJiMjIxZjRjYjJkODM5MjZlNzBhZDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T21:23:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T21:23:30Z"},"message":"docs(code): define input surface nomenclature in AGENTS.md (#4738)\n\nThe `deepagents-code` REPL has many text-entry surfaces — the primary\nchat input, inline prompts, single-line modal fields, and picker filter\ninputs — so \"the input\" / \"the input box\" is ambiguous and routinely\nconfuses both humans and agents about which field is meant. This adds an\n**Input surface nomenclature** section to `libs/code/AGENTS.md` that\nfixes precise, function-based terms and maps each to a concrete class\n(`ChatInput`/`ChatTextArea`, `InlinePromptTextArea`, modal `Input`s,\nfilter `Input`s) so there is a single greppable referent per surface.\n\nDocs only; no behavior change. Naming is a judgment call, so wording is\nopen to bikeshedding in review.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d23898f0-cac9-2b5e-e737-69903b582d2d)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e40f6ec3db0312d853c334f84b95673f8ffb92aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e40f6ec3db0312d853c334f84b95673f8ffb92aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d8038e33c6bc3eec32bb221f4cb2d83926e70ad1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVqjSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIFIQAAaMs6KAqGHxk9V6cXG3VJwU\nHwnuqvDBZfaAifKtGbYE+mtG4nSDWJLEVgrl4/luGpfVoW4Dwg4OIz6OgGgCPt6P\nE8HA+xIqXYVNl6eT8i2f/Du10QlzwdVtDP19v1jefz4/obG9V1R1ixlUH7PqU8IF\ne42qYytZm/kUUOjRHSNMo2qXwG6gMbiY8XGxXOWaRmsLIcZCJ2eao9P7DlDWRdsI\n/9g/wN7+r0+cKFi6IKvaG2uPZ0K3wFOFG5ml84R4gbOAOLGru54GqGKvnbtHQaqQ\n1pH63U+UTY+rezRDxmkatNhcy+3lNMRQqXqrKiS9z+fjEyK40dMc4jalll6bnfrH\nSDFRcWe7VRjjKek6+mmk+JUdH1UQm+9IKGbSs7K+zHw5QLIz8tZiVrTaUCk6J4e/\nS4InGdzeodfZS4pVPO0TeGuLl7pg3mxQG/2XdWVfRnoNCkOaZx4rXXLUdcwfNb7D\nHYTeVjJbL8QyQOORBVO/B+urylLo1czwuxUXHXIraMcQ0NiPairIR/H+s94nVe9o\nTUh2oITTLRPmLlF0GSSiNoK1VI5CeT+wKcS2vt5F45hDyaxoIiBQzK7ekvP+/B6l\ni0YS6ao4b30flz/U7wqX8uvUV5xHEZDGfMiYNZtNvs0boiWQHaz1kPB5fvgoFNxo\nNSyeQj4Xyo9hLSIVI0GG\n=tVw0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e40f6ec3db0312d853c334f84b95673f8ffb92aa\nparent 8a6963ba52eee2ab8de5df2c14210f472c828d38\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784064210 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784064210 -0400\n\ndocs(code): define input surface nomenclature in AGENTS.md (#4738)\n\nThe `deepagents-code` REPL has many text-entry surfaces — the primary\nchat input, inline prompts, single-line modal fields, and picker filter\ninputs — so \"the input\" / \"the input box\" is ambiguous and routinely\nconfuses both humans and agents about which field is meant. This adds an\n**Input surface nomenclature** section to `libs/code/AGENTS.md` that\nfixes precise, function-based terms and maps each to a concrete class\n(`ChatInput`/`ChatTextArea`, `InlinePromptTextArea`, modal `Input`s,\nfilter `Input`s) so there is a single greppable referent per surface.\n\nDocs only; no behavior change. Naming is a judgment call, so wording is\nopen to bikeshedding in review.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d23898f0-cac9-2b5e-e737-69903b582d2d)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T21:23:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d8038e33c6bc3eec32bb221f4cb2d83926e70ad1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d8038e33c6bc3eec32bb221f4cb2d83926e70ad1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d8038e33c6bc3eec32bb221f4cb2d83926e70ad1/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8a6963ba52eee2ab8de5df2c14210f472c828d38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8a6963ba52eee2ab8de5df2c14210f472c828d38","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8a6963ba52eee2ab8de5df2c14210f472c828d38"}]},{"sha":"8a6963ba52eee2ab8de5df2c14210f472c828d38","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhhNjk2M2JhNTJlZWUyYWI4ZGU1ZGYyYzE0MjEwZjQ3MmM4MjhkMzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T20:51:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T20:51:10Z"},"message":"fix(code): match primary-input `Ctrl+D` behavior in inline free-text fields (#4729)\n\n`Ctrl+D` in the inline ask-user and goal-review text fields now deletes\nforward (like the main input) instead of immediately quitting while\nthere is text after the cursor.\n\n---\n\nFollowing [#4724](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4724),\nthe inline free-text prompts (`AskUserTextArea`, `GoalReviewTextArea`)\nshould behave like the primary agent input. They did not for `Ctrl+D`.\n\nThe `Ctrl+D` binding is a priority binding on the App, so it always runs\n`action_quit_app` before any focused-widget binding. That handler only\ndelegated forward-delete when the primary chat input was focused; a\nfocused inline free-text field fell straight through to quitting the app\neven mid-text. This generalizes the delete-target lookup\n(`_ctrl_d_delete_target`) so a focused `InlinePromptTextArea` gets the\nsame semantics as the chat input: delete a non-empty selection or the\ncontent right of the cursor, and only quit at the true end of the text\nwith no selection.\n\nThe primary chat input's existing behavior — including the nuance that a\ndraft hidden behind a modal keeps focus but must not be edited from\nunder it — is unchanged.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/39dd0369-5eba-9ec7-a376-a3c0347fbbf8)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/39dd0369-5eba-9ec7-a376-a3c0347fbbf8/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"59b4c82d80f4c572b098544032a96d8cb169bd11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/59b4c82d80f4c572b098544032a96d8cb169bd11"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8a6963ba52eee2ab8de5df2c14210f472c828d38","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVqE+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuVIQAFX8JRpqUAYWTKPmKyptFSd2\nL0MwZmVvr9qF89edUSD2h9HPJuDDW321HascGpDVx7WVCpxZ8nKUTPxRD0Q4i5/w\norASQwddGRKV52Up8AMKc8pKleicvnWqjcsQdPPzu124i8U4U9VvMv33/c26Rr34\n6CPmGp+ZASBsj5/EtDoRoUbYM/+yD7DOJJ6FE/DuQYFUCqD/5COLe+6oje//IPXc\npWjpZKzIwUYRPlBOfq56XzgxHZ8A8wCVYlpt8vgY3WINYgdo83mu0JY+8ZkOQtrb\nM47f943MWKRA2XNBLxLMOCk56PUoIyiWsAApYBz6TX6BmwfHjeU0reFqfiL4pMo+\nOzfNmM9xJ3Kdx6w/A2hB32NGLoDDwSIojzNnDpBwabrJqxtWAOU9vunOudMNEZkj\ntb3Euwq9Ey0mw7lxXQcpa5mK/Oi5yJDG8FQqXRIYVO3/2GJGXOOWSJZSIU8SCzsB\nz9vYlsZ272ZpOeRm6QbGVZK2rcPOXTffB3Rn7Tlh5triL70D7zJhFALWjkqEgwZ6\nP/n6fWA6aZpeEne9o74nDdgf2wORtbnHo8AewAq0HiWCYE1X4Rl2kyp7naRXSkHy\nO3S3VJeGPWUGJQMF+8ONNbfy5bLXzvYySfOLU10B80WLtcWmewt9Jt3Z5wTTCrfH\nM1YAGWGYdgpLpBsp3i9g\n=oW1X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 59b4c82d80f4c572b098544032a96d8cb169bd11\nparent c584dcfb3ad287446e0209b8bd4ca31cee587eea\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784062270 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784062270 -0400\n\nfix(code): match primary-input `Ctrl+D` behavior in inline free-text fields (#4729)\n\n`Ctrl+D` in the inline ask-user and goal-review text fields now deletes\nforward (like the main input) instead of immediately quitting while\nthere is text after the cursor.\n\n---\n\nFollowing [#4724](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4724),\nthe inline free-text prompts (`AskUserTextArea`, `GoalReviewTextArea`)\nshould behave like the primary agent input. They did not for `Ctrl+D`.\n\nThe `Ctrl+D` binding is a priority binding on the App, so it always runs\n`action_quit_app` before any focused-widget binding. That handler only\ndelegated forward-delete when the primary chat input was focused; a\nfocused inline free-text field fell straight through to quitting the app\neven mid-text. This generalizes the delete-target lookup\n(`_ctrl_d_delete_target`) so a focused `InlinePromptTextArea` gets the\nsame semantics as the chat input: delete a non-empty selection or the\ncontent right of the cursor, and only quit at the true end of the text\nwith no selection.\n\nThe primary chat input's existing behavior — including the nuance that a\ndraft hidden behind a modal keeps focus but must not be edited from\nunder it — is unchanged.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/39dd0369-5eba-9ec7-a376-a3c0347fbbf8)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/39dd0369-5eba-9ec7-a376-a3c0347fbbf8/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T20:51:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8a6963ba52eee2ab8de5df2c14210f472c828d38","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8a6963ba52eee2ab8de5df2c14210f472c828d38","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8a6963ba52eee2ab8de5df2c14210f472c828d38/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c584dcfb3ad287446e0209b8bd4ca31cee587eea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c584dcfb3ad287446e0209b8bd4ca31cee587eea","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c584dcfb3ad287446e0209b8bd4ca31cee587eea"}]},{"sha":"c584dcfb3ad287446e0209b8bd4ca31cee587eea","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM1ODRkY2ZiM2FkMjg3NDQ2ZTAyMDliOGJkNGNhMzFjZWU1ODdlZWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T20:50:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T20:50:43Z"},"message":"feat(code): persist reasoning effort across restarts (#4728)\n\n`dcode` now remembers your selected reasoning effort per model across\nrestarts.\n\n---\n\nReasoning effort was in-memory only (`_model_params_override`), so\nrelaunching `dcode` reset it to the model/provider default. This\npersists the selected effort *label* per model in a new\n`[effort.by_model]` table in `config.toml` — mirroring the existing\n`[models].default` persistence pattern — and restores it at startup and\non `/model` switch. Restoration always re-validates the stored label\nagainst the active model via `supported_efforts_for_model` /\n`model_params_for_effort`, so a label like `max` is never applied to a\nmodel that can't support it (invalid entries are pruned and the model\ndefault is used). Storing the label rather than raw provider params lets\nit be re-mapped per active model.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/028bd7f3-4eb6-351c-63e9-9af5c09c0281)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/028bd7f3-4eb6-351c-63e9-9af5c09c0281/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Johannes du Plessis <51395795+johannes117@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"20e91452806408486c2055b91174acf888fca1d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/20e91452806408486c2055b91174acf888fca1d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c584dcfb3ad287446e0209b8bd4ca31cee587eea","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVqEjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANiYQAF2YF34YYTKsjUzeSYKoMerO\nVaWmwcp1cuvFre6IV690Vv+9ra5saXiupUTV0nWD0tRIgOhMjtxg0G6z27prSEYm\ns1/fr4/oLRiy6IcKzCrJacsKx3hb3QZRWR+DvHkJCISl7zBvHUz16H7JuSOZBT1o\nnzU9LwYNvijdGaCY5QfgFfU5jGKoJTK4ROOk1CeDMrCA+kfZDtL21mGYt8x7n05e\nQOYmCvnm+17m3iROKTaVAK9VQCjs9ySaMuMmgmaiA00AO5o3qEwzbfVtrYaeE7De\ncaTh7PMgRt8Est8aUjBJOqSz1h0fZttfp9qPrFw/4jL30+Xw6OEpV/v+jC3k5xDg\nfjQop9ZYDTQ+DBBrCjeEyNCmMYcs7GfQ0Z/YNHCg4rhSLWS9iWloZ+chfSZHMLix\nSF93vZFcCCs/fP/AsrqrPLYPpeFIIRLqeBwNW70/P4BSez5NozqpKmcTQFRFObyv\n3FR6LH9NCEwlP20hE69GaTGy5akig/r1TalPmTxZpsRV9TwHiXryg9a8atnADeqI\nwksNiJkKRWqLwKlp1qBf6rOF6XIqGw8DtECpU6FM33x0QajsfqJQgAMTMpcol98b\nRT3sN6KFK5Q0cXpbV2WmNDj6Vi7q6FDzRNxk94mJVfX4S1sHufhY4gyNTG8PkCq8\nbTqVuHWU7z/rAw4VxcdW\n=ULkA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 20e91452806408486c2055b91174acf888fca1d7\nparent d61ae0c630939aed57e11ed9ff90dec0714741fc\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784062243 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784062243 -0400\n\nfeat(code): persist reasoning effort across restarts (#4728)\n\n`dcode` now remembers your selected reasoning effort per model across\nrestarts.\n\n---\n\nReasoning effort was in-memory only (`_model_params_override`), so\nrelaunching `dcode` reset it to the model/provider default. This\npersists the selected effort *label* per model in a new\n`[effort.by_model]` table in `config.toml` — mirroring the existing\n`[models].default` persistence pattern — and restores it at startup and\non `/model` switch. Restoration always re-validates the stored label\nagainst the active model via `supported_efforts_for_model` /\n`model_params_for_effort`, so a label like `max` is never applied to a\nmodel that can't support it (invalid entries are pruned and the model\ndefault is used). Storing the label rather than raw provider params lets\nit be re-mapped per active model.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/028bd7f3-4eb6-351c-63e9-9af5c09c0281)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/028bd7f3-4eb6-351c-63e9-9af5c09c0281/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Johannes du Plessis <51395795+johannes117@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T20:50:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c584dcfb3ad287446e0209b8bd4ca31cee587eea","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c584dcfb3ad287446e0209b8bd4ca31cee587eea","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c584dcfb3ad287446e0209b8bd4ca31cee587eea/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d61ae0c630939aed57e11ed9ff90dec0714741fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d61ae0c630939aed57e11ed9ff90dec0714741fc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d61ae0c630939aed57e11ed9ff90dec0714741fc"}]},{"sha":"d61ae0c630939aed57e11ed9ff90dec0714741fc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ2MWFlMGM2MzA5MzlhZWQ1N2UxMWVkOWZmOTBkZWMwNzE0NzQxZmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T20:23:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T20:23:34Z"},"message":"fix(infra): harden `dcode` release automation (#4732)\n\nRelease PR checks can start before the automatic curated-note draft is\npublished, immediately marking the PR red even though the draft is still\nbeing generated. Applying those notes can also report a stale-head\nfailure after successfully updating the release branch because the\npull-request API may lag behind the branch ref.\n\nThis makes the release flow tolerate those expected ordering delays\nwithout weakening its concurrency checks:\n\n- The required check waits for the initial automatic draft on PR events,\ndistinguishes a valid but unapplied draft from missing or stale\nmetadata, and continues through transient GitHub read failures.\n- Interrupted refresh runs explicitly close their in-progress check\ninstead of leaving it spinning indefinitely.\n- Post-apply validation reads the canonical release branch ref while\ncontinuing to reject PR-body edits, curated-draft edits, and concurrent\nbranch movement.\n- The prerelease SDK-pin warning points maintainers to `release-deps:\nacknowledged` when an intentional cross-package release sequence has not\nreached PyPI yet.\n\nRegression coverage exercises delayed draft publication, state changes\nduring polling, stale pull-request heads after apply, and concurrent\nrelease-branch updates.","tree":{"sha":"44b004b023aae367346d9078ccd5741e3ea80fc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/44b004b023aae367346d9078ccd5741e3ea80fc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d61ae0c630939aed57e11ed9ff90dec0714741fc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVprGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA35IQAKvw+HMg9/Y2zNRyyL0srZZY\nPK3uePK8DvGisdjEBYwK0xI+aEnrGNYAE+Xrs790PYdOH2Sh4BeUpIK4EVwolq99\nDpK13AcufMUU3b1MWflI80Sw4zecXjSY5Rc6MmKswKP2Kwatk+87xc5SoFj7ib37\nh1r9j2B//1vhm2zgwngfsKQ4CAqk1Qjreaalf3m9LDYFYzVl/qn0GkZf1MqJYH+s\nEf+J/GvCpcLk+HL2qHsQF+ET2/tMTbaudRB74j5qi5cvjIh2RCvuvqloJZvwP/bc\nr1aY/gVSYSWczUu1h/h+6k9a2iAS2DuPAZYWb+2wXbNSGtkNqnQ9m4k3vTzCbnOI\napp1S8bpG49hotkjzjWifVxSovegCr9pTq66dPEXDBdq1x3ihvC+ZDoAW7I0BN6E\n77oeNk6qLuSoSucHN8Ay66lz77JpyLH5P2bSdWqLTDzH8QfNNTqycicQX6A6in4t\nCw0DCqNWSSQriZ7bKaaJzD7hDeCQVf/8fZ0jkPRINx74yJbL0DquPHttNxdgk/Yg\n3+YmokGyMjJt8zb3anNt6Dzt+jRZ/n3veP81llBXJI51uHQfQYCqxAtzkIK2OfeV\nZb7kcCPK+AChQrxek+83SEOBWXhefFza4GoHT6Timt/X1nxW3XU3ZOS7EzUBucHs\ns3ygWVvZzWfVVjZy2oBq\n=yBh9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 44b004b023aae367346d9078ccd5741e3ea80fc3\nparent 02a246144c764a1c57b60223652ade8716c7529b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784060614 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784060614 -0400\n\nfix(infra): harden `dcode` release automation (#4732)\n\nRelease PR checks can start before the automatic curated-note draft is\npublished, immediately marking the PR red even though the draft is still\nbeing generated. Applying those notes can also report a stale-head\nfailure after successfully updating the release branch because the\npull-request API may lag behind the branch ref.\n\nThis makes the release flow tolerate those expected ordering delays\nwithout weakening its concurrency checks:\n\n- The required check waits for the initial automatic draft on PR events,\ndistinguishes a valid but unapplied draft from missing or stale\nmetadata, and continues through transient GitHub read failures.\n- Interrupted refresh runs explicitly close their in-progress check\ninstead of leaving it spinning indefinitely.\n- Post-apply validation reads the canonical release branch ref while\ncontinuing to reject PR-body edits, curated-draft edits, and concurrent\nbranch movement.\n- The prerelease SDK-pin warning points maintainers to `release-deps:\nacknowledged` when an intentional cross-package release sequence has not\nreached PyPI yet.\n\nRegression coverage exercises delayed draft publication, state changes\nduring polling, stale pull-request heads after apply, and concurrent\nrelease-branch updates.","verified_at":"2026-07-14T20:23:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d61ae0c630939aed57e11ed9ff90dec0714741fc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d61ae0c630939aed57e11ed9ff90dec0714741fc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d61ae0c630939aed57e11ed9ff90dec0714741fc/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"02a246144c764a1c57b60223652ade8716c7529b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/02a246144c764a1c57b60223652ade8716c7529b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/02a246144c764a1c57b60223652ade8716c7529b"}]},{"sha":"02a246144c764a1c57b60223652ade8716c7529b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDAyYTI0NjE0NGM3NjRhMWM1N2I2MDIyMzY1MmFkZTg3MTZjNzUyOWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T20:15:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T20:15:19Z"},"message":"fix(code): hydrate transcript tail when scrolled to the bottom edge (#4733)\n\nFix newest transcript messages sometimes failing to reappear when\nscrolling to the bottom of a long, virtualized chat history.\n\n---\n\n`test_scroll_down_hydrates_tail_below` was flaky (~30% `TimeoutError`)\nbecause scroll-driven tail hydration compared the message store's\n*estimated* `bottom_spacer_top` against the *real* DOM scroll geometry\n(`scroll_y`/`max_scroll_y`). When estimated spacer heights drift from\nthe rendered layout — which depends on the viewport height Textual\nhappens to allocate — the distance heuristic can sit exactly at its\nthreshold while the view is already parked at `max_scroll`, so\n`should_hydrate_below` returns `False` forever and the archived tail is\nnever remounted.\n\n`should_hydrate_below` now hydrates whenever the view is at the scroll\nedge but history remains archived below, mirroring how scrolling to\noffset 0 always hydrates above. This is a real user-facing fix, not just\na test tweak: a user who scrolls to the very bottom while the tail is\narchived would otherwise be stranded on a blank spacer.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/9bce6e12-3555-8aa4-3e10-0a96a898db03)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"199aefcaa59bf5496ec1850cc4bec5861c61f307","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/199aefcaa59bf5496ec1850cc4bec5861c61f307"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/02a246144c764a1c57b60223652ade8716c7529b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVpjXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxJYQAB2VD2J2fuoddtI86aRs6W3O\n9Cos+hIK20Gpw9fXvutyCFEFcHEzN/XbBKYVfyf0e0YVFIG1ayVu+ATrowUOJGD9\nfgMnsFe7lAajXzaGeRSUWNhO9kxQ8FHZpKsLLU2d1k+xcrwIl3WG1fupu+ZU4Q0C\n/QXLHBYg2EvncnesV+RzaQ3FyyOPUI1nE9HQVfOTltrV1OOmvrVxQ+1v2+OrafTA\nfJiGBdoRAa94M9g5S4JOZvShNzMixRWHesVj3k8pf8liFSEwM0hPn7Xvh+OGqcZW\n363kB93a/6QKL0aQ8+7ZUG+0e6kTL9rWBPAVkFCwhhvi4NIIm+yvlVwita6JH66v\niqldRNc+vCPU/Kwv1k3AncbdQ6fhMweoZmh0L1yRKDDxXGH2W9+a78Va4KH2EcVY\nyOqDKnX2YDQjhdDqTeJxmvjr+AOvyRPm8rVpwedHphT4IrsZ4k8oFBKDsQ+sW9Bt\nrSho6PQUYcrd2/okK6a1W6Z1IegPc1G5xh+StzDDhm0Oiqc/vESl+xo5Eirs9AQ3\nfV2UrUvs5bS3XZEQh2G2Da+ZFRfnGNoZqo6mKBbv24Cf6FJlMd6OLs/mjvLOIFOc\nAXMN84mi36Ruf2YCZO1Xw0MMqnAStRZiCXQaiF6pa2kyQnoxfta/vPRpGdlWqeTl\nLVoJj4BT1Yf9E8pSVJeL\n=EMyT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 199aefcaa59bf5496ec1850cc4bec5861c61f307\nparent 8eb909a59b8291b6e05fcf6f38cf93678f87a243\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784060119 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784060119 -0400\n\nfix(code): hydrate transcript tail when scrolled to the bottom edge (#4733)\n\nFix newest transcript messages sometimes failing to reappear when\nscrolling to the bottom of a long, virtualized chat history.\n\n---\n\n`test_scroll_down_hydrates_tail_below` was flaky (~30% `TimeoutError`)\nbecause scroll-driven tail hydration compared the message store's\n*estimated* `bottom_spacer_top` against the *real* DOM scroll geometry\n(`scroll_y`/`max_scroll_y`). When estimated spacer heights drift from\nthe rendered layout — which depends on the viewport height Textual\nhappens to allocate — the distance heuristic can sit exactly at its\nthreshold while the view is already parked at `max_scroll`, so\n`should_hydrate_below` returns `False` forever and the archived tail is\nnever remounted.\n\n`should_hydrate_below` now hydrates whenever the view is at the scroll\nedge but history remains archived below, mirroring how scrolling to\noffset 0 always hydrates above. This is a real user-facing fix, not just\na test tweak: a user who scrolls to the very bottom while the tail is\narchived would otherwise be stranded on a blank spacer.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/9bce6e12-3555-8aa4-3e10-0a96a898db03)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T20:15:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/02a246144c764a1c57b60223652ade8716c7529b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/02a246144c764a1c57b60223652ade8716c7529b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/02a246144c764a1c57b60223652ade8716c7529b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8eb909a59b8291b6e05fcf6f38cf93678f87a243","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8eb909a59b8291b6e05fcf6f38cf93678f87a243","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8eb909a59b8291b6e05fcf6f38cf93678f87a243"}]},{"sha":"8eb909a59b8291b6e05fcf6f38cf93678f87a243","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhlYjkwOWE1OWI4MjkxYjZlMDVmY2Y2ZjM4Y2Y5MzY3OGY4N2EyNDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-14T19:30:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T19:30:28Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.39 (#4725)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. The published GitHub release body is extracted from the\nmerged `CHANGELOG.md` by `release.yml`, not from this PR description._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.39](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.38...deepagents-code==0.1.39)\n(2026-07-14)\n\n### Bug fixes\n\n- Improved Debug Console log retention by partitioning retained logs by\nlevel ([#4718](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4718))\n([c6e3b35](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c6e3b351f1826aa6ea97be244acd867950a032ee)).\n- Fixed `/offload` to run server-side\n([#4696](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4696))\n([564e5a0](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/564e5a05bca5236ae33ce1147865111f931d257c)).\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"50b17fd3bbc1440d85d67c0c43645e23e916ec10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/50b17fd3bbc1440d85d67c0c43645e23e916ec10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8eb909a59b8291b6e05fcf6f38cf93678f87a243","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVo5UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/08QAHAeZVRKTFq5heTkjJc004m4\nOHsf8Vt0zYTD9RBHA/CtpRX1QF2Ct67hsLDIuz4H7Y4rgd2alYNKqWBqRwzMvj9f\n2m3wuVpq/Gf6YyKfVkQUM8iPg6KCqKymihdYRizEqjC6y98cgAORiPFb/WcLtnpc\nCnA1Y4nybBxzLmFOoCC72xGZloLK6dfOMDCyMyYs66lJNwxa2SVVtDLoLRuOzdjC\n2Ag4F++KsSEX+xEM0bt+coTzS1sp/Y476hSRZV+CkhmKsCqsmsQfC6EwqvSmJWrz\nc2D2Ft5uwDWCgQWdEzWDdoVECY9KDbOI6TSmgms5Hs2n5G9o0nOEnydxhjbey2tk\nVVWQi0WzUWMoXrO3KruBQV/yRrVwFTP53ZpMYjZVeveOzefdJDPp8eZA/4QscaVC\nb1UGt/gujzvPPxX/jUnov/ZSfVcEgthnZonWuvGzrUQaWfDDbyYgQZ86RDM0fuLW\n3j06wuabBmUPAOqEgT90QO7iLzmiFhCxFTCe3IPz1rSOHtcgHttA6aR44lhRmKlh\nPEt2pRNcOyleNydVAZTGpgqLhya7IrPhOrCsFcc0Us3GOlnPxII2yjnM3Q8b/sFH\nBaloNQpoKb0aZvGw47C+iGhMcDe08orkGtGMM79t+ft4D2/iJs5mzWhQLsIBYUt2\n7oYg5xT6XbuLbELqOz0f\n=pQS4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 50b17fd3bbc1440d85d67c0c43645e23e916ec10\nparent 564e5a05bca5236ae33ce1147865111f931d257c\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784057428 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784057428 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.39 (#4725)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. The published GitHub release body is extracted from the\nmerged `CHANGELOG.md` by `release.yml`, not from this PR description._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.39](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.38...deepagents-code==0.1.39)\n(2026-07-14)\n\n### Bug fixes\n\n- Improved Debug Console log retention by partitioning retained logs by\nlevel ([#4718](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4718))\n([c6e3b35](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c6e3b351f1826aa6ea97be244acd867950a032ee)).\n- Fixed `/offload` to run server-side\n([#4696](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4696))\n([564e5a0](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/564e5a05bca5236ae33ce1147865111f931d257c)).\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T19:30:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8eb909a59b8291b6e05fcf6f38cf93678f87a243","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8eb909a59b8291b6e05fcf6f38cf93678f87a243","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8eb909a59b8291b6e05fcf6f38cf93678f87a243/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"564e5a05bca5236ae33ce1147865111f931d257c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/564e5a05bca5236ae33ce1147865111f931d257c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/564e5a05bca5236ae33ce1147865111f931d257c"}]},{"sha":"564e5a05bca5236ae33ce1147865111f931d257c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDU2NGU1YTA1YmNhNTIzNmFlMzNjZTExNDc4NjUxMTFmOTMxZDI1N2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T19:03:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T19:03:45Z"},"message":"fix(code): run `/offload` server-side (#4696)\n\n`/offload` now stores archived conversation history through the agent's\nbackend.\n\n---\n\n`/offload` previously summarized and saved conversation history in the\nclient process. In server and sandbox modes, that process does not own\nthe backend used by the agent: persistence could fail against a\nread-only filesystem, and even a successfully written archive would not\nbe available to the agent through `read_file`.\n\nThis changes Deep Agents Code to run the existing `compact_conversation`\ntool through the active agent instead. The command seeds a tool call\ninto the thread, approves the expected human-in-the-loop interrupt\nbecause the user explicitly requested `/offload`, resumes the graph, and\nreads the persisted summarization event back from server state. The\narchive is therefore written through the agent's composite backend and\nremains readable by the agent in local, server, and sandbox runs.\n\nThe old client-side `perform_offload` helper (and its `OffloadResult` /\n`OffloadThresholdNotMet` / `OffloadModelError` result types) is removed,\nas summarization and persistence now run through the agent. In local\nmode, the `conversation_history` backend now roots under `~/.deepagents`\n(via `_offload_fallback_root`, with a hardened private-temp fallback\nwhen the home directory is not writable) instead of a throwaway\n`tempfile.mkdtemp` directory, so offloaded history persists across\nsessions.\n\nThe SDK's `compact_conversation` API is unchanged; this PR is confined\nto Deep Agents Code.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1cbc308e-b411-2a09-bd6b-541e606ca4c5)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"53df4576af18a496ac9c13da69a90815bc9a4b08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/53df4576af18a496ac9c13da69a90815bc9a4b08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/564e5a05bca5236ae33ce1147865111f931d257c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVogRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3hwQAF3ADOHgK59Ncj6bYvcijseF\nrZGxLli82r2PHwIcGl2ttyCkN5+j58wk0pQ5rO38o+PZ0gp+jHFVk/H2xO4kn9ae\nTf3MxpwosiINN38oS0xbJhiSc8TpzksY7w5+inFTKCuT2KeNMdxiTloWU0R5eT9l\nTDnD2yLEaC1+Vjiwe+z+9o9L4/q8aPA9sBqbxSV2pL0F5zwlTds7/IJRGhEbI0Zc\nR/VICpxnK8GDC7nmFDPzNzpWaaWHDZ90xLLfDe1I3Q4OtHFG5x79HomvBOzzyznJ\nAQdQUyjBHIk5XZ/zdN8+brVl1E3qDzIzxfeEwPxCGmIEFWm8QJ69gtLlGI4GnE9W\nL2xHpXuNMsEElXS4T3OxgpNtq3IIu2Fx24pwE+YvwxxXSGfkssAqJ8FYd5C3GFzo\nCNsg0yVkskD9tKte/PnSwKcVJLFHaeYA79oRb8mzsOIrGiTa4hIUulPfoBZDePBQ\nbK8gMxtBZdx5Jp8snZv+CXGw0KDXHLooQ+IYVw9bJuHlELzylDZy8D3GOHxh6f9Y\nElJBAyG0lZ5648ffCQ4nFqaVQ8AikVMhW4Wn6DedaffugwrWmbR267ydGiAi/YB7\nWOz5dVnTb2PCxFl4KZB3Ql66wHxE8nywLvagiZa6B3zFNpzeXnRg/ZytAenP2wFo\noErvzZ7Ms3TMRg9fhynE\n=3jKK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 53df4576af18a496ac9c13da69a90815bc9a4b08\nparent 0c7e58c508049db7fa04d388a3dad4d7dcc91b39\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784055825 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784055825 -0400\n\nfix(code): run `/offload` server-side (#4696)\n\n`/offload` now stores archived conversation history through the agent's\nbackend.\n\n---\n\n`/offload` previously summarized and saved conversation history in the\nclient process. In server and sandbox modes, that process does not own\nthe backend used by the agent: persistence could fail against a\nread-only filesystem, and even a successfully written archive would not\nbe available to the agent through `read_file`.\n\nThis changes Deep Agents Code to run the existing `compact_conversation`\ntool through the active agent instead. The command seeds a tool call\ninto the thread, approves the expected human-in-the-loop interrupt\nbecause the user explicitly requested `/offload`, resumes the graph, and\nreads the persisted summarization event back from server state. The\narchive is therefore written through the agent's composite backend and\nremains readable by the agent in local, server, and sandbox runs.\n\nThe old client-side `perform_offload` helper (and its `OffloadResult` /\n`OffloadThresholdNotMet` / `OffloadModelError` result types) is removed,\nas summarization and persistence now run through the agent. In local\nmode, the `conversation_history` backend now roots under `~/.deepagents`\n(via `_offload_fallback_root`, with a hardened private-temp fallback\nwhen the home directory is not writable) instead of a throwaway\n`tempfile.mkdtemp` directory, so offloaded history persists across\nsessions.\n\nThe SDK's `compact_conversation` API is unchanged; this PR is confined\nto Deep Agents Code.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1cbc308e-b411-2a09-bd6b-541e606ca4c5)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T19:03:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/564e5a05bca5236ae33ce1147865111f931d257c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/564e5a05bca5236ae33ce1147865111f931d257c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/564e5a05bca5236ae33ce1147865111f931d257c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0c7e58c508049db7fa04d388a3dad4d7dcc91b39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0c7e58c508049db7fa04d388a3dad4d7dcc91b39","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0c7e58c508049db7fa04d388a3dad4d7dcc91b39"}]},{"sha":"0c7e58c508049db7fa04d388a3dad4d7dcc91b39","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDBjN2U1OGM1MDgwNDlkYjdmYTA0ZDM4OGEzZGFkNGQ3ZGNjOTFiMzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T18:52:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T18:52:53Z"},"message":"refactor(code): share inline prompt infrastructure (#4724)\n\n`ask_user` and goal review independently implemented the same inline\nprompt mechanics, which made their shared lifecycle and input behavior\nharder to maintain consistently.\n\nThis refactor introduces small neutral primitives for prompt text entry,\noption rendering, one-shot future resolution, prompt chrome, and\napplication-level mounting, scrolling, cleanup, and focus restoration.\nEach flow continues to own its domain state machine: `ask_user` retains\narbitrary text and multiple-choice LangGraph interrupt handling, while\ngoal review retains its accepted, edited, rejected, and cancelled\noutcomes and shortcuts.\n\nThe existing appearance, key controls, result payloads, interruption\nbehavior, replacement policies, and cancellation semantics remain\nunchanged. Coverage exercises both consumers independently, including\nnavigation, text submission, cancellation, focus, cleanup races, and\nfuture resolution.","tree":{"sha":"be78781605fc736c455399e739bae5714dab5f60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/be78781605fc736c455399e739bae5714dab5f60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0c7e58c508049db7fa04d388a3dad4d7dcc91b39","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVoWFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA70QAKI8nhmJBxKL5//hpBqocN1A\nV//TezfpSAcRj7plT0+UsXFYYPz7pA9b7OB5C4tahw/oTSQWnxXZfik10uEeXw2m\nm0bh9ippbcovE2tV1TwBtF3q/qyvGwUGVHHYTH0ZSEJ9THVzADR5KJRWpdcJUDyk\ncw9wWwvv0Pf1x8SjnCsmP7beoxOfrsNiHyeZwSaGUktVeDB+QVDCRIVlrfOlzI2x\nuOKjJ0BGpnDb80oogDMZ/aTgQQ0GfDdE2mYNASjpBWeAVY9rnsZtCV/1y7Tq7Qfh\nxaY2n44UivdlWXMOG0kjmji8DI2ly8uGPZYdz+U2PzaKHQP+2/6X6qMklK83/6S3\n2Sh7O08vx3nLiR8CJY4BbU8Fq34wd6KXgFPV38N+KR9g+nwye5qV2TNbv7avqfqr\nlZ1Cq8l86CAVonPBZM1tsPhyQiTZwbKaXVv2Q+juxYEQ95Jjmu/B+nzvoQXMPPNQ\nUt4JqkRiCQJJuE+VwGqhXSASJiR6cPUuZNsUgRoKrNKAmFHH2ukKur8ONso+f1B4\nqoU/4nGXwYnS9/ibniqd6UVmaua+Wh0fvFLRVwV86y/ur/sslg7dGuQa5vVir032\nk1NJlNSraO4197lcT3a3n1oJIGJl0IgMwHW9IM9e1mQx0CR1yPoFDgzVPlrjzdml\nvVM4GZO2dSJi7m/15I+j\n=rbb1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree be78781605fc736c455399e739bae5714dab5f60\nparent 1d1912f13979f6503b399a2ef5a6b0c833d34325\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784055173 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784055173 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): share inline prompt infrastructure (#4724)\n\n`ask_user` and goal review independently implemented the same inline\nprompt mechanics, which made their shared lifecycle and input behavior\nharder to maintain consistently.\n\nThis refactor introduces small neutral primitives for prompt text entry,\noption rendering, one-shot future resolution, prompt chrome, and\napplication-level mounting, scrolling, cleanup, and focus restoration.\nEach flow continues to own its domain state machine: `ask_user` retains\narbitrary text and multiple-choice LangGraph interrupt handling, while\ngoal review retains its accepted, edited, rejected, and cancelled\noutcomes and shortcuts.\n\nThe existing appearance, key controls, result payloads, interruption\nbehavior, replacement policies, and cancellation semantics remain\nunchanged. Coverage exercises both consumers independently, including\nnavigation, text submission, cancellation, focus, cleanup races, and\nfuture resolution.","verified_at":"2026-07-14T18:52:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0c7e58c508049db7fa04d388a3dad4d7dcc91b39","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0c7e58c508049db7fa04d388a3dad4d7dcc91b39","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0c7e58c508049db7fa04d388a3dad4d7dcc91b39/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1d1912f13979f6503b399a2ef5a6b0c833d34325","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1d1912f13979f6503b399a2ef5a6b0c833d34325","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1d1912f13979f6503b399a2ef5a6b0c833d34325"}]},{"sha":"1d1912f13979f6503b399a2ef5a6b0c833d34325","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDFkMTkxMmYxMzk3OWY2NTAzYjM5OWEyZWY1YTZiMGM4MzNkMzQzMjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T18:49:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T18:49:03Z"},"message":"feat(infra): curate `dcode` release notes (#4639)\n\n`deepagents-code` release PRs currently expose release-please's\ngenerated changelog directly. Maintainers need a durable place to turn\nthose generated entries into concise, user-facing notes without losing\ntheir edits the next time release-please refreshes the PR.\n\nWhen a `deepagents-code` release PR moves from draft to ready for\nreview, the release bot posts a marked comment containing a polished\ndraft. Maintainers can edit that comment while preserving the generated\nversion heading, then run `@dcode-release-bot apply` to copy the\nfinalized section into both `libs/code/CHANGELOG.md` and the release PR\npreview.\n\nFor a ready, non-bypassed release PR, the `curated release notes` check\nbinds the latest valid bot-authored draft to its applied metadata,\nrequires the current version section in `libs/code/CHANGELOG.md` and the\nPR-body preview to match that draft, and verifies that the recorded\ndraft and apply commits remain in the current release branch's ancestry.\nUnrelated descendant commits are allowed. If release-please regenerates\nthe curated section or adds generated entries, the check fails until a\nmaintainer runs `@dcode-release-bot draft` and then `@dcode-release-bot\napply` again. While a release PR is still a draft, the check passes\nwithout validating curation and the manual commands are disabled. The\nexact `release: dangerously skip curated notes` label remains an\nexplicit escape hatch for exceptional releases.\n\nDrafting makes one non-agentic request to one of three fixed provider\nAPI endpoints, using a repository-configured model. The model receives\nisolated release-note input and no callable tools. The trusted helper\nreads that prepared input, writes the draft output, and sends the\nrequest using only the selected provider key; the output is structurally\nvalidated and the release snapshot is rechecked before the draft is\npublished. Privileged curation changes use a short-lived installation\ntoken minted from the existing organization-membership GitHub App, while\nworkflow feedback and refreshed check runs use the scoped\n`GITHUB_TOKEN`. Manual commands require repository write access.\n\n## Required repository setup\n\n- Ensure the installed organization-membership GitHub App credentials\nare available as repository secrets `ORG_MEMBERSHIP_APP_CLIENT_ID` and\n`ORG_MEMBERSHIP_APP_PRIVATE_KEY`, and that the App grants read/write\naccess to contents, issues, and pull requests.\n- Add repository variables `DCODE_RELEASE_BOT_LOGIN` and\n`DCODE_RELEASE_BOT_ID` for the installed App's `<app-slug>[bot]`\nidentity.\n- Configure the `release-dcode` environment without required reviewers\nor other deployment approval rules. Set `DCODE_RELEASE_MODEL` to an\n`openai:<model>`, `anthropic:<model>`, or `google_genai:<model>` value,\nand add the matching provider API key as an environment secret\n(`OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, or `GOOGLE_API_KEY`).\n- Add the literal `curated release notes` job name to `main`'s required\nstatus checks. Without it, failures are visible but do not block a stale\nor unapplied release PR from merging.\n\nThe release guide includes the exact identity lookup and setup\ninstructions.","tree":{"sha":"c0482b01b0ac1beb43cb7dc348d7cc76d78951b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c0482b01b0ac1beb43cb7dc348d7cc76d78951b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1d1912f13979f6503b399a2ef5a6b0c833d34325","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVoSfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5TAQAAT+1SKvii7RQPJaLcMhAsQs\nNn/1QgOqKZl7EpnPC0wM4rrYM0LxqHTFOiorWCQUpb3TZUlF78hhM0rOjMkQ7E0/\nHiR1NL2BRFcGic7BYorAsfapimrgcweeXGfxr21fHKnA8Bp1bJPRBWHLWKuRCd4M\nR+0qW7jhSLhz1yXuQwovfrMLkFRW99qQjYoUdIW84nermrzRVlpbvPbm2L3APLNf\n8pyp0XMFd9VFlUKWc21ArzzdvPvqwW+30tCgI9tCbraf/+4PaP4Y+GHj3iuhjabU\nT0q0KjzREu/uy6HPK4HfB+uKD57vffAQHjaEa538i2LI0BDkjNWyGV9hL+5vs39n\nDqK/lUtuRfsjG++5F+Am/9rkcuXUoY51hy92QiYI3SIPhABlW9VGJ2YIIXJMCZVP\nf/ySS1OxJr+n/D8cr2MHyMwEi2NhwInbHLuTAMqoqHKVxrvvh1DZbB/Uxqn+e7tJ\nC7V8/54SIaIweLgJL4/msDwUl+qNXLVdOdDGAiQhu2YRvkSslTgeg7ddAfgl3nKs\nez96GVMpSszM9Yk6lVE//tNNUtkyT3B8GEOz3YGpD0Y6QKjobN6IqlM3ttvcT8lW\nDokSm++4XaVXXTHh8JcJO4KyRM6g38oeNVhHutCcckl+7N2Vvr87YswJvpK0PJ9B\n+V6ElcpHWtPYiGfXRLwz\n=Gme3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c0482b01b0ac1beb43cb7dc348d7cc76d78951b6\nparent 9972614f57c19f6165f6a82e7dfbb665b15e9289\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784054943 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784054943 -0400\n\nfeat(infra): curate `dcode` release notes (#4639)\n\n`deepagents-code` release PRs currently expose release-please's\ngenerated changelog directly. Maintainers need a durable place to turn\nthose generated entries into concise, user-facing notes without losing\ntheir edits the next time release-please refreshes the PR.\n\nWhen a `deepagents-code` release PR moves from draft to ready for\nreview, the release bot posts a marked comment containing a polished\ndraft. Maintainers can edit that comment while preserving the generated\nversion heading, then run `@dcode-release-bot apply` to copy the\nfinalized section into both `libs/code/CHANGELOG.md` and the release PR\npreview.\n\nFor a ready, non-bypassed release PR, the `curated release notes` check\nbinds the latest valid bot-authored draft to its applied metadata,\nrequires the current version section in `libs/code/CHANGELOG.md` and the\nPR-body preview to match that draft, and verifies that the recorded\ndraft and apply commits remain in the current release branch's ancestry.\nUnrelated descendant commits are allowed. If release-please regenerates\nthe curated section or adds generated entries, the check fails until a\nmaintainer runs `@dcode-release-bot draft` and then `@dcode-release-bot\napply` again. While a release PR is still a draft, the check passes\nwithout validating curation and the manual commands are disabled. The\nexact `release: dangerously skip curated notes` label remains an\nexplicit escape hatch for exceptional releases.\n\nDrafting makes one non-agentic request to one of three fixed provider\nAPI endpoints, using a repository-configured model. The model receives\nisolated release-note input and no callable tools. The trusted helper\nreads that prepared input, writes the draft output, and sends the\nrequest using only the selected provider key; the output is structurally\nvalidated and the release snapshot is rechecked before the draft is\npublished. Privileged curation changes use a short-lived installation\ntoken minted from the existing organization-membership GitHub App, while\nworkflow feedback and refreshed check runs use the scoped\n`GITHUB_TOKEN`. Manual commands require repository write access.\n\n## Required repository setup\n\n- Ensure the installed organization-membership GitHub App credentials\nare available as repository secrets `ORG_MEMBERSHIP_APP_CLIENT_ID` and\n`ORG_MEMBERSHIP_APP_PRIVATE_KEY`, and that the App grants read/write\naccess to contents, issues, and pull requests.\n- Add repository variables `DCODE_RELEASE_BOT_LOGIN` and\n`DCODE_RELEASE_BOT_ID` for the installed App's `<app-slug>[bot]`\nidentity.\n- Configure the `release-dcode` environment without required reviewers\nor other deployment approval rules. Set `DCODE_RELEASE_MODEL` to an\n`openai:<model>`, `anthropic:<model>`, or `google_genai:<model>` value,\nand add the matching provider API key as an environment secret\n(`OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, or `GOOGLE_API_KEY`).\n- Add the literal `curated release notes` job name to `main`'s required\nstatus checks. Without it, failures are visible but do not block a stale\nor unapplied release PR from merging.\n\nThe release guide includes the exact identity lookup and setup\ninstructions.","verified_at":"2026-07-14T18:49:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1d1912f13979f6503b399a2ef5a6b0c833d34325","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1d1912f13979f6503b399a2ef5a6b0c833d34325","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1d1912f13979f6503b399a2ef5a6b0c833d34325/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9972614f57c19f6165f6a82e7dfbb665b15e9289","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9972614f57c19f6165f6a82e7dfbb665b15e9289","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9972614f57c19f6165f6a82e7dfbb665b15e9289"}]},{"sha":"9972614f57c19f6165f6a82e7dfbb665b15e9289","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk5NzI2MTRmNTdjMTlmNjE2NWY2YTgyZTdkZmJiNjY1YjE1ZTkyODk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T17:02:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T17:02:41Z"},"message":"style(code): rename \"auto\" approval-mode label to \"YOLO\" (#4726)\n\nThe interactive TUI now labels the enabled auto-approve mode as \"YOLO\"\nin the status bar.\n\n---\n\nRenames the user-facing auto-approve mode indicator shown in the TUI\nstatus bar from `auto` to `YOLO`. This is a display-string-only change\nin `libs/code/deepagents_code/tui/widgets/status.py`; internal\nidentifiers (`auto_approve`), the `--auto-approve` CLI flag, the\n`dangerously-auto` config value, and env vars are intentionally left\nunchanged to avoid breaking changes.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e160ef65-607d-d8db-2c0e-c8d2b1824b5d)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b0dbbae782e6e1d945ea33f9dbef5fe79f76cdcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b0dbbae782e6e1d945ea33f9dbef5fe79f76cdcb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9972614f57c19f6165f6a82e7dfbb665b15e9289","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVmuxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQWAQAGP5X+S4kSzH3sA8OoQvd1Gq\nd/YNPmC+TI1vn07uU1StWwH64MixGl2TMBplgEEou4Bio9dMulUostXNqJWhMgE7\n7OYCkcm0iFvX+Fw5EBm4CUulyF9/AxA3sxINNJEuEZfi50zxW0x6jvhNqh24Ghv9\nqT5pu47g91PQBeeMRXLksWj5Cm8GR1C+nqxgS4D6+45Qla6Ru4x7BJbJE9MWKmDd\nUKRYtTpMVT5elxeuwP16xJIohX6IdT/ttZgDhsDLTUMJEzxVIp+Y1f2RgwwPh2tg\nRPoapisxs94OEXpZ4moICo0V9S1i49x7EfBgNIWUllkv6M9s+B11EE3gV3R0jtc3\nJ3hyWapkwlS7J1QnjUV/0qy4e5rwYQ7g7Wd/aixF2hgmo73cbWtRT77zdIUzMl2G\njXan9QnOJVg25kLsNSj+5cEosK1gAUK2Gu4I+2x+Ml07iNg7k+yc6pfd0JF/KiZk\nOmPyeylHTWb4StK7823jUjzceefTE7oIVLJmDiZHbvLV7WoMKEniDc4c8OPrQeTV\nA63w9raiIYfi7aLxEaNQPFXexjivlmYQD88tnZxLxEJp6I0VFmlEd3bdC5EH+Y3g\nmb/HlJqgzXgsNgf6rY2S6/HkMcYDv+Oy5VuQ1yE67D8QU508mYD3Iza9gmOcLxJu\nrDuCwMGzrJVUEKYqczGj\n=DqC2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b0dbbae782e6e1d945ea33f9dbef5fe79f76cdcb\nparent 7473d958a25d08bc8d1cab8f1de8389627478850\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784048561 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784048561 -0400\n\nstyle(code): rename \"auto\" approval-mode label to \"YOLO\" (#4726)\n\nThe interactive TUI now labels the enabled auto-approve mode as \"YOLO\"\nin the status bar.\n\n---\n\nRenames the user-facing auto-approve mode indicator shown in the TUI\nstatus bar from `auto` to `YOLO`. This is a display-string-only change\nin `libs/code/deepagents_code/tui/widgets/status.py`; internal\nidentifiers (`auto_approve`), the `--auto-approve` CLI flag, the\n`dangerously-auto` config value, and env vars are intentionally left\nunchanged to avoid breaking changes.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e160ef65-607d-d8db-2c0e-c8d2b1824b5d)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T17:02:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9972614f57c19f6165f6a82e7dfbb665b15e9289","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9972614f57c19f6165f6a82e7dfbb665b15e9289","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9972614f57c19f6165f6a82e7dfbb665b15e9289/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7473d958a25d08bc8d1cab8f1de8389627478850","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7473d958a25d08bc8d1cab8f1de8389627478850","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7473d958a25d08bc8d1cab8f1de8389627478850"}]},{"sha":"7473d958a25d08bc8d1cab8f1de8389627478850","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc0NzNkOTU4YTI1ZDA4YmM4ZDFjYWI4ZjFkZTgzODk2Mjc0Nzg4NTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T15:29:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T15:29:54Z"},"message":"feat(evals,infra): default unified evals to bare harness, add dcode option + run-config summary (#4697)\n\nAdds a README for the unified evals CI job and makes the deep-agents\nharness configurable. The full rationale (benchmarks, categories, task\nselection, and when to use this vs. the pytest eval suite) lives in\n`libs/evals/UNIFIED_EVALS.md`.\n\n## Code changes\n- `unified_prep.py`: autonomous and context now default to the `bare`\n`create_deep_agent` harness (conversation stays `tau3`). A new\n`agent_impl` override selects `dcode` for the deep-agents categories\nonly, validated against `{bare, dcode}`.\n- `unified_evals.yml`: new `agent_impl` choice input (default `bare`,\noptions `bare`/`dcode`) threaded to prep, plus a prep-job step that\nwrites a run-configuration summary of every dispatch input (with the\nresolved model list and effective `shard_parallel`) to the run summary\nfor debuggability.\n- `test_unified_prep.py`, `test_unified_workflow.py`: cover the bare\ndefaults, the `dcode` override applying only to the deep-agents\ncategories, invalid-harness rejection, and the new input / prep-env /\nsummary wiring.\n- `libs/evals/UNIFIED_EVALS.md`: new doc.\n\nTests: 31 passed (`test_unified_prep.py`, `test_unified_workflow.py`).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"96aba1d361ad67a05da12c2de54ffff9e51de474","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/96aba1d361ad67a05da12c2de54ffff9e51de474"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7473d958a25d08bc8d1cab8f1de8389627478850","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVlXyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYhgQADUGdCRUhn8tTmqqNpqVbCqf\nuqxGATqgPxSwlwtV7aQW0b0Ii9woeXNClAYip/2O0QLGb4gtMp0HF1Z23yCplyX/\nYucx+Ya16uaiwcuSo6/scnuIwxobo8qEBGlOdVMwZtqK9vNUL09RLH8HgXv5H5Fb\niFFKfPPur45psMrv/+xnQ9hP8ajsK+Fm6A1qaGCdR4xxPtLiOGRQbEGydSBae/xp\nVNhzPHLnMhcHI0h+7UfhP+/4IjZbqqWIt1AvTyW3wuGRK/Fvzy84i8m7VxLF42o3\nlht3LYJlnfLFYoza3C5FEm6jEEVoE3IzStYHXCC27rlSLZZ/uxT5MKCkVzD+cUJV\nBDqDz7/oITb3OAdGBijbfGWFs8P8lzj4ueXj5VU8XCRcLW+VBR4N6zgdijQEcSEp\nspDFAN8Puv4LXWllyECbcsRBIIUENFlIWcNbfh71JbVl5pMwzpD0V4k8bpbLEgeu\nBTXhv+JaPkXoyUB+bje8+lJTBrd0mmOk0LKTbn0o8ajrJr2w5b7FMFe5H2LaMWq4\nV+F9sZ8JDARrNmUrU27nggm9fzcP3IPE4ZdfsJjkI17ZpiXZ7LUkvEHo20E1rU18\nst3LdI1Zr24thsmmOKIpmHQ5mjhM2HFuNBVGOneDcVgJqJrU4NqM4KGtO3N0Jr+P\nd/LcWo/G/TI7nkWu12oY\n=Lvhs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 96aba1d361ad67a05da12c2de54ffff9e51de474\nparent c6e3b351f1826aa6ea97be244acd867950a032ee\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1784042994 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784042994 -0400\n\nfeat(evals,infra): default unified evals to bare harness, add dcode option + run-config summary (#4697)\n\nAdds a README for the unified evals CI job and makes the deep-agents\nharness configurable. The full rationale (benchmarks, categories, task\nselection, and when to use this vs. the pytest eval suite) lives in\n`libs/evals/UNIFIED_EVALS.md`.\n\n## Code changes\n- `unified_prep.py`: autonomous and context now default to the `bare`\n`create_deep_agent` harness (conversation stays `tau3`). A new\n`agent_impl` override selects `dcode` for the deep-agents categories\nonly, validated against `{bare, dcode}`.\n- `unified_evals.yml`: new `agent_impl` choice input (default `bare`,\noptions `bare`/`dcode`) threaded to prep, plus a prep-job step that\nwrites a run-configuration summary of every dispatch input (with the\nresolved model list and effective `shard_parallel`) to the run summary\nfor debuggability.\n- `test_unified_prep.py`, `test_unified_workflow.py`: cover the bare\ndefaults, the `dcode` override applying only to the deep-agents\ncategories, invalid-harness rejection, and the new input / prep-env /\nsummary wiring.\n- `libs/evals/UNIFIED_EVALS.md`: new doc.\n\nTests: 31 passed (`test_unified_prep.py`, `test_unified_workflow.py`).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T15:29:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7473d958a25d08bc8d1cab8f1de8389627478850","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7473d958a25d08bc8d1cab8f1de8389627478850","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7473d958a25d08bc8d1cab8f1de8389627478850/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c6e3b351f1826aa6ea97be244acd867950a032ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c6e3b351f1826aa6ea97be244acd867950a032ee","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c6e3b351f1826aa6ea97be244acd867950a032ee"}]},{"sha":"c6e3b351f1826aa6ea97be244acd867950a032ee","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM2ZTNiMzUxZjE4MjZhYTZlYTk3YmUyNDRhY2Q4Njc5NTBhMDMyZWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T15:17:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T15:17:46Z"},"message":"fix(code): partition Debug Console log retention by level (#4718)\n\nDebug Console level filters now surface recent `INFO`/`WARNING`/`ERROR`\nlogs even when `DEBUG` output dominates the window; a `DEBUG` flood no\nlonger evicts higher-severity records.\n\n---\n\nThe in-app Debug Console (`Ctrl+\\`) tails an always-on in-memory ring\nbuffer that kept a **single** `deque` shared across every level. When\n`DEBUG` logging is enabled, verbose `DEBUG` output quickly filled that\nwindow and evicted the rarer `INFO`/`WARNING`/`ERROR` records before the\nuser ever picked a level filter — so selecting \"INFO\" turned up nothing\neven though `INFO` records had been emitted this session. The filter\n*matching* was correct; *retention* was discarding the records the\nfilter needed.\n\nThis partitions retention by level: each level keeps its own bounded\n`deque`, so a burst at one level can no longer evict another. Each\nretained record is tagged with its monotonic emission sequence so\nsnapshots stay chronologically ordered across levels, preserving the\nexisting `snapshot_records_since` contract (absolute resume index,\n`(records, total)` shape, negative-index behavior). Non-standard level\nnames share one bounded fallback bucket so nothing is silently dropped.\nThe console's own retained copy applies the same per-level cap so it\nisn't re-flattened.\n\nAs intended, the `All`/`min:*` views can now show more than the\nper-level capacity in total (up to capacity per level) and interleave\nolder high-severity records that previously fell off the single window —\nwhich is the point. Memory stays bounded (~capacity × number of levels).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/da1fb4b1-3886-27df-551a-84c49759fbb6)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/da1fb4b1-3886-27df-551a-84c49759fbb6/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c47737d24ec5d09690c2b64c715b90880d5a806d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c47737d24ec5d09690c2b64c715b90880d5a806d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c6e3b351f1826aa6ea97be244acd867950a032ee","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVlMaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq0AQAIGGVv7w71RAy/OZQTmZhRfJ\nRe0oXvuwIu+PEy+Rs0U3n+F9nGRsco5f3BYuCw76B7I9upTanuMINge+KLinoEiB\nfNqy8mOXiIbSVLVmoYbj1S+NPGSxvW5CfRPqjV/86leqSmwfWswwF6Ev6Vh7ye5q\nai7Z/f19z1PCFA6VrV/ns8hNznzkLMcbTO8CqLCgMcDY0f2k5ugQ+Bx8v/V0ofky\nEEt1bgFnBJH57rtl31EWP1/kynxd2ozIK164oZhIPcYrNiewrwHvD6nGt/Fbwx0/\nxBKlGuKBvDtU6mDWwZj/8C6CvcVKUKOcrvnz6wn3fGFPvjGkH5zChqUZIW32u36A\n74P99ZXiHh6/QuNDsjbPt0wcl5JZYmL/soRFbFObR+aZblx7XUhDlH+QrqVw00/w\nNrNT30tcE2McGCAoS3x5hEX29QdiCTN5jNLekqf3Rl/6AEXv3d53Hbw01PRd2eXW\nmariyYDgJcvg+KiVwbAH/ieRU8MqW/SbNxBsbWNK8ADhkeWwCtleyPcY6A8JQFmd\nD/BqynTklmuiy6pTp6IPNhhfmb/ixGHSy9fH2cdZkNIxSMP/3630ygBPHTxQLsh2\nmAxqxbSEZohkXAQCG61PsNaROhu9IP54/Wd2eCskf+d9wEaV0rPtGo55gl5kTrtD\nz3fmHAye/GNtazlyxIbv\n=Bfrq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c47737d24ec5d09690c2b64c715b90880d5a806d\nparent 970952550e8f53cd89a64a4ee98969ce757693ff\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784042266 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784042266 -0400\n\nfix(code): partition Debug Console log retention by level (#4718)\n\nDebug Console level filters now surface recent `INFO`/`WARNING`/`ERROR`\nlogs even when `DEBUG` output dominates the window; a `DEBUG` flood no\nlonger evicts higher-severity records.\n\n---\n\nThe in-app Debug Console (`Ctrl+\\`) tails an always-on in-memory ring\nbuffer that kept a **single** `deque` shared across every level. When\n`DEBUG` logging is enabled, verbose `DEBUG` output quickly filled that\nwindow and evicted the rarer `INFO`/`WARNING`/`ERROR` records before the\nuser ever picked a level filter — so selecting \"INFO\" turned up nothing\neven though `INFO` records had been emitted this session. The filter\n*matching* was correct; *retention* was discarding the records the\nfilter needed.\n\nThis partitions retention by level: each level keeps its own bounded\n`deque`, so a burst at one level can no longer evict another. Each\nretained record is tagged with its monotonic emission sequence so\nsnapshots stay chronologically ordered across levels, preserving the\nexisting `snapshot_records_since` contract (absolute resume index,\n`(records, total)` shape, negative-index behavior). Non-standard level\nnames share one bounded fallback bucket so nothing is silently dropped.\nThe console's own retained copy applies the same per-level cap so it\nisn't re-flattened.\n\nAs intended, the `All`/`min:*` views can now show more than the\nper-level capacity in total (up to capacity per level) and interleave\nolder high-severity records that previously fell off the single window —\nwhich is the point. Memory stays bounded (~capacity × number of levels).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/da1fb4b1-3886-27df-551a-84c49759fbb6)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/da1fb4b1-3886-27df-551a-84c49759fbb6/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T15:17:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c6e3b351f1826aa6ea97be244acd867950a032ee","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c6e3b351f1826aa6ea97be244acd867950a032ee","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c6e3b351f1826aa6ea97be244acd867950a032ee/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"970952550e8f53cd89a64a4ee98969ce757693ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/970952550e8f53cd89a64a4ee98969ce757693ff","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/970952550e8f53cd89a64a4ee98969ce757693ff"}]},{"sha":"970952550e8f53cd89a64a4ee98969ce757693ff","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk3MDk1MjU1MGU4ZjUzY2Q4OWE2NGE0ZWU5ODk2OWNlNzU3NjkzZmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nishitha M","email":"32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-14T13:37:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T13:37:33Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): remove excluded tools from `ToolNode` (#4698)\n\nfixes #3952 \n\n### Problem\n\n`FilesystemMiddleware(tools=[...])` only hid excluded tools from the\nmodel, it didn't unregister them. All tools remained executable, so a\n`ToolCall` for an excluded tool could still be dispatched and run.\n\n### Fix\n\n`FilesystemMiddleware` now only registers enabled tools during\ninitialization:\n\n```python\nself.tools = [\n    factory()\n    for name, factory in tool_factories\n    if self._enabled_tools is None or name in self._enabled_tools\n]\n```\n\nExcluded tools are no longer present in `ToolNode.tools_by_name`, making\nthem non-executable rather than merely hidden. The existing\n`wrap_model_call` filtering remains for backend capability checks (e.g.\n`execute`/`delete` on unsupported backends).","tree":{"sha":"10cc1d9d6ba3b773118fc94e0fb0d7fcca4ea2e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/10cc1d9d6ba3b773118fc94e0fb0d7fcca4ea2e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/970952550e8f53cd89a64a4ee98969ce757693ff","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVjudCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ/wQAGo9plavWD6wsLGgurLQbs9G\nJSz5sVZ15yWIpQ6T8HkUYfiR+wFLXJPmdZqzfTanMlTbtXFXJgf+JIQHKEqjk9Nm\ncQ6og9elLHWvI76wBhEx5ud9HZfSsYjM5F/+9TLJzB1B851YcBT+wzTmUKPUz81D\ndtQSyB6HbgYwtC0u3tmOi+zUpnxz1epuFtabr4MlR1/uwFh2q7Uq5hfyqxMyLGtB\nlZ+NBwKQnltpr2U7PzaE5Y9+1o9nX3JFNxBzXtZQUZCxDMuEomzWM1mIWXnai96n\nFuY3hUfLQfEu13LLqBBkWJpgGtKdvmmETjmYa5ZpTSRGYTBwLWNyG18ydTJ+9yID\nWB6r2ZFR1O2cao5KQecuf8ZOwwkcA/Vn+2RoGGfb1utCT0ZnrHBa9XCR1TWV9D7C\nSMkivCG7YSomcLXO7vnmjHks99Wy4cXPomxMog//lLWKDtE+K0sqVMQwiNs45WNn\n5CySQ/f8f4IvX1JwEj8uRSVETikLm2IFm1yO5ZW0lv+jFSAkYTTYLtg8JNUaiVzG\nil6N7SDdep9xhjviUe6HYOdZvDgqNl2ZiJGerQiWibto8nv0iTfYXrmK3yV3AZ22\nwvOMsEM+L4zClnbw5RoPSSLnmB5BIYgEf+cEX/9DWOnFuEe4Z/HT7MNxvOzdn+A/\nIyge7pzLTB4qnv5lvnMJ\n=h/kI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 10cc1d9d6ba3b773118fc94e0fb0d7fcca4ea2e7\nparent 4338671aa1d9bd1fd70f20069aac5468697606bf\nauthor Nishitha M <32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com> 1784036253 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784036253 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): remove excluded tools from `ToolNode` (#4698)\n\nfixes #3952 \n\n### Problem\n\n`FilesystemMiddleware(tools=[...])` only hid excluded tools from the\nmodel, it didn't unregister them. All tools remained executable, so a\n`ToolCall` for an excluded tool could still be dispatched and run.\n\n### Fix\n\n`FilesystemMiddleware` now only registers enabled tools during\ninitialization:\n\n```python\nself.tools = [\n    factory()\n    for name, factory in tool_factories\n    if self._enabled_tools is None or name in self._enabled_tools\n]\n```\n\nExcluded tools are no longer present in `ToolNode.tools_by_name`, making\nthem non-executable rather than merely hidden. The existing\n`wrap_model_call` filtering remains for backend capability checks (e.g.\n`execute`/`delete` on unsupported backends).","verified_at":"2026-07-14T13:37:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/970952550e8f53cd89a64a4ee98969ce757693ff","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/970952550e8f53cd89a64a4ee98969ce757693ff","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/970952550e8f53cd89a64a4ee98969ce757693ff/comments","author":{"login":"imnishitha","id":32355027,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzU1MDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32355027?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha","html_url":"https://github.com/imnishitha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4338671aa1d9bd1fd70f20069aac5468697606bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4338671aa1d9bd1fd70f20069aac5468697606bf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4338671aa1d9bd1fd70f20069aac5468697606bf"}]},{"sha":"4338671aa1d9bd1fd70f20069aac5468697606bf","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQzMzg2NzFhYTFkOWJkMWZkNzBmMjAwNjlhYWM1NDY4Njk3NjA2YmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T08:08:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T08:08:56Z"},"message":"hotfix(code): stabilize scroll hydration test (#4720)\n\nUnblocks the failed `deepagents-code==0.1.38` pre-release check in [run\n29315182859](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/29315182859).\n\nThe scroll-up hydration test uses a deliberately tiny virtualized\nwindow. As head hydration swaps older rows in, it archives rows below;\nleaving the opposite hydration check active lets layout-driven scroll\nevents schedule tail hydration and move the visible range back after the\nwait loop briefly observes that the head is fully hydrated.\n\nThis isolates the test to upward hydration, matching the existing\ndownward test's isolation of upward hydration. It still exercises the\nreal scroll notification path and verifies that `m0` is remounted.","tree":{"sha":"5749cb0928e13bcdc4fe68c968efc04d88205607","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5749cb0928e13bcdc4fe68c968efc04d88205607"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4338671aa1d9bd1fd70f20069aac5468697606bf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVe6YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANxYQAFL1KiBjpg75/zx4LVmR+2dv\ntCfo0l/ofOQ6d1B4uM/MsRF4UZt0fX+oG3jWYOmnDsu053Dje5b3FwVoC6pMomJP\nq+sSJiCJb5si7n4T+AdCPJKUdt6Sz62ZWX6miRXm5/aJPu5WYkV/N9Wxm4Z6c7iO\n0uiakFaJLkdLsdwbLr+yVH1+hQ+CF0W3DOmSeCb6LfEna3EC36mQOeXU+C/YaDEY\n1mR0SNUiICn97GHVbG5sxcFux54JeUYndN3n3iAbgg5UzTUT/V+I205BMnsaitgP\n+7zD2MIP8eEMpNTuknwEdUs+xphP7xbW+cKvUKRh5lFLRugCfv5xyYZXVDJDZZ9v\nrE5FTyM+6QL/uuzHcaAxcw5DO0zp1N26VNfOV7RM5mZSB+eJQIAXpko9mMGNaE/A\n+Hj64Td4hWigbhgDviOl6FKpez1N3t9a1nlTS4VM6Nsi0O1+g+tRw5qAc4wV8o02\n6veID3g5iN2c3AWud1v+lcnNQBBd8Aa8VKpT+J/nDj+M1DeKAniLzwUivpmLA+Lm\n9ErhEPHyDgPrOvqtu5y+JOTB8fL2wx4p1j9/vbp8bOtoT45l28mE6v40aKjk3Py1\nNgC5wapp1Cc1THS7DjYw7Ex0lM+GMUNOl9cSvaYrD/HlS4NnurkUhF/od8Dt6QCk\nDIxoa3aDWgZ790prIaBr\n=hnOT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5749cb0928e13bcdc4fe68c968efc04d88205607\nparent 98eb51238fb6b5289abf90178dfbe59414309f1d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784016536 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784016536 -0400\n\nhotfix(code): stabilize scroll hydration test (#4720)\n\nUnblocks the failed `deepagents-code==0.1.38` pre-release check in [run\n29315182859](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/29315182859).\n\nThe scroll-up hydration test uses a deliberately tiny virtualized\nwindow. As head hydration swaps older rows in, it archives rows below;\nleaving the opposite hydration check active lets layout-driven scroll\nevents schedule tail hydration and move the visible range back after the\nwait loop briefly observes that the head is fully hydrated.\n\nThis isolates the test to upward hydration, matching the existing\ndownward test's isolation of upward hydration. It still exercises the\nreal scroll notification path and verifies that `m0` is remounted.","verified_at":"2026-07-14T08:08:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4338671aa1d9bd1fd70f20069aac5468697606bf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4338671aa1d9bd1fd70f20069aac5468697606bf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4338671aa1d9bd1fd70f20069aac5468697606bf/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"98eb51238fb6b5289abf90178dfbe59414309f1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/98eb51238fb6b5289abf90178dfbe59414309f1d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/98eb51238fb6b5289abf90178dfbe59414309f1d"}]},{"sha":"98eb51238fb6b5289abf90178dfbe59414309f1d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk4ZWI1MTIzOGZiNmI1Mjg5YWJmOTAxNzhkZmJlNTk0MTQzMDlmMWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T08:01:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T08:01:02Z"},"message":"hotfix(code): trim startup tips (#4719)\n\nStartup tips should prioritize broadly useful actions rather than\ndetailed shortcuts and command variants.\n\nThis trims low-value tips and simplifies the wording for `/copy`, `/mcp\nlogin`, and `/effort`, keeping the randomized startup guidance concise.","tree":{"sha":"af4795c93034eb71bf7745b329f3717506de7b3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/af4795c93034eb71bf7745b329f3717506de7b3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/98eb51238fb6b5289abf90178dfbe59414309f1d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVey+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKdwQAFRHpwUKxZO1APL1v7n6ubMU\n9pIhZJnpOQWjaAGjMmWs0li0cT46nEN/dgK5wGQHmER1eowg7A5dYer+DpX7/T8u\nC6LqEVEYW0Qwx36UHqv1PgTHHUc8bWj2kQ0EleQqmKT/aR/VUSTA3uAC5A+uSVsR\nupWQtkZLI56CwZRQULccf/sFW26sy8DcLjD1xsNQbx3sEUTKZ0IGXBZ+E2LmXyas\n0