hain-ai/deepagents/commit/f9915db4206ef2d794ad07fdccbdd4ee58963142))\n* Hydrate virtualized transcript on scroll offset changes\n([#4646](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4646))\n([f77eeb0](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f77eeb0a036281f84bf7d0b05ea60e02630f55c1))\n* Keep TODO and edit tools expanded\n([#4704](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4704))\n([1d549d3](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1d549d3f3c9bb60c3ce39d4a0c913bcefe9610d5))\n* Make `/goal` completion and grading reliable\n([#4691](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4691))\n([9da63c6](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9da63c64a59503e3366e9bc7224cb1251af476be))\n* Preflight Ollama host reachability before discovery probe\n([#4702](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4702))\n([96fe71a](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/96fe71a3815e1020edeb3be1af70b0cadb85931c))\n* Quiet expected non-repo `git ls-files` logging\n([#4701](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4701))\n([3d499db](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3d499db8a6c76743810a8983107d7c7d7bdb35e6))\n* Rename `ls_agent_kind` to `ls_agent_purpose`\n([#4708](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4708))\n([2678b16](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2678b1680d8928e72e8efae00632a694c9b2737a))\n* Run MCP login during a run, queue the restart\n([#4643](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4643))\n([65e1ee8](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/65e1ee802e2f69762a6d8e6c7c6d37060161ea5a))\n* Show \"Took &lt;duration&gt;\" when `task` tool completes\n([#4638](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4638))\n([19538e0](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/19538e0a46a5c2c050412b79fd45608a63cdde52))\n* Support unambiguous `read_file` gutters\n([#4711](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4711))\n([2089b54](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2089b54e2a674ede313e790b59febf9dc6f22571))\n\n---\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T07:36:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/73bd9735697b95c664727657128708022fbe04cf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/73bd9735697b95c664727657128708022fbe04cf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/73bd9735697b95c664727657128708022fbe04cf/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"06f46fffe36efa9f3adcb331b07df283d8bed874","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/06f46fffe36efa9f3adcb331b07df283d8bed874","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/06f46fffe36efa9f3adcb331b07df283d8bed874"}]},{"sha":"06f46fffe36efa9f3adcb331b07df283d8bed874","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDA2ZjQ2ZmZmZTM2ZWZhOWYzYWRjYjMzMWIwN2RmMjgzZDhiZWQ4NzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T07:12:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T07:12:00Z"},"message":"feat(code): improve `/goal` criteria UX (#4694)\n\n`/goal` now proposes shorter, outcome-focused acceptance criteria, can\nuse bounded read-only repository context when needed, and presents\nclearer grader statuses with expandable complete feedback.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user starts a `/goal`, dcode currently drafts acceptance criteria\nfrom the objective alone. That can produce long, repetitive checklists,\nwhile grader feedback can blur the difference between incomplete work,\nan invalid rubric, and a grader failure.\n\nThis change keeps goal criteria focused on the minimum observable\noutcomes needed to decide whether the goal is complete. Explicit user\nconstraints are preserved, and the generator can consult narrowly scoped\nrepository context when a referenced file or existing behavior needs\nclarification. Repository inspection is read-only and bounded;\nunavailable context falls back to drafting from the goal alone.\nUser-supplied `/rubric` criteria are unchanged.\n\nGrader results now use distinct status copy and keep the transcript\ncompact. Complete unmet-criteria explanations and next steps remain\navailable in an expandable, scrollable detail view, including after\ntranscript virtualization.\n\n## User stories and before/after examples\n\n<details>\n<summary>Goal criteria stay concise and describe outcomes instead of\nimplementation work</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user starting a goal, I want a short checklist of\nthe outcomes that matter so I can review it quickly and avoid committing\nto work I did not request.\n\n**Before**\n\nFor a goal such as “Add a compact goal-status indicator, keep `/rubric`\nunchanged, and display exactly `No goal set` when inactive,” the\nproposed rubric could repeat the same behavior across several criteria\nand add broad implementation, documentation, refactoring, or testing\nrequirements.\n\n**After**\n\nThe proposal is usually a flat list of 2–5 short criteria centered on\nobservable results, for example:\n\n- The compact goal-status indicator reflects whether a goal is active.\n- The inactive state displays exactly `No goal set`.\n- Existing `/rubric` behavior is unchanged.\n\nExplicit names, paths, commands, wording, and other user constraints are\npreserved where practical. User-authored `/rubric` criteria are not\nrewritten by this change.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Goals can use targeted repository context when the objective\ndepends on existing behavior</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user referring to an existing file, symbol,\ncommand, or behavior, I want the proposed criteria grounded in the\nrepository instead of made generic or based on guessed implementation\ndetails.\n\n**Before**\n\nA goal such as “Make the interactive grader statuses match the existing\nheadless statuses” is drafted from that sentence alone. The resulting\ncriteria may say only that the statuses should match, without\nidentifying the outcomes already represented in the codebase.\n\n**After**\n\nWhen clarification is necessary, the criteria generator can inspect the\nrelevant repository context before drafting. That allows it to\ndistinguish observable outcomes such as unmet criteria, an invalid\nrubric, and a failed acceptance-criteria check without turning\nrepository details into new requirements.\n\nInspection is limited to read-only `ls` and `read_file` calls within the\nrepository, with at most 25 tool calls and strict limits on file reads,\ndirectory listings, and returned text. If repository context is\nunavailable or unusable, `/goal` still proposes criteria from the\nobjective alone.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Grader statuses distinguish unfinished work from rubric and\ngrader failures</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user reviewing a grader result, I want the summary\nto identify what kind of outcome occurred so I know whether to continue\nthe work, revise the rubric, or retry the check.\n\n**Before**\n\nStatus wording could focus on “changes,” a generic grader failure, or an\niteration limit without consistently naming the acceptance-criteria\noutcome. It was harder to tell whether the work was incomplete, the\nrubric could not be evaluated, or the check itself failed.\n\n**After**\n\nInteractive and headless output use outcome-specific summaries:\n\n- `Acceptance criteria not yet satisfied`\n- `Acceptance criteria not yet satisfied (iteration limit reached)`\n- `Rubric is invalid or cannot be evaluated`\n- `Acceptance criteria check failed`\n\nEach result provides a corresponding next step: address unmet criteria,\nreview or replace the rubric, retry with a different grader model, or\ncontinue/amend/clear an active goal after the iteration limit.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Complete grader feedback remains available without filling the\ntranscript</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user with long grader feedback, I want a compact\ntranscript by default while retaining every explanation and\ncriterion-level gap when I need it.\n\n**Before**\n\nThe explanation, every unmet criterion, and recovery guidance were\nrendered inline with the result, so a detailed evaluation could occupy a\nlarge portion of the transcript.\n\n**After**\n\nThe transcript initially shows one concise result line. Clicking it or\npressing `Ctrl+O` opens a scrollable detail view containing the complete\nexplanation, all unmet criteria and gaps, and the recommended next step.\nThe details are not truncated, and their expanded or collapsed state is\nrestored if transcript virtualization temporarily removes and remounts\nthe message.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"ec62fb8385b28ae4cb1013e71d34c12b92bc91c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ec62fb8385b28ae4cb1013e71d34c12b92bc91c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/06f46fffe36efa9f3adcb331b07df283d8bed874","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVeFACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9K4QAEHtFvipPdc2nhE6vPrXnmnu\nxYyDrlFONWQEBOJAkTm5NrU85AyXHOhKY+m/1QTtu1Sgs44voXaUnp5XyZ/2qQis\n7fL/BiqfFCxOZ//j4RDcmj7gfPetV/t4MCl7r0lX73n6XU1Y2sKqjNsfykRZq36B\nTf5yRDtWWvQkz6WOEPyGTd7tJFr3w1//H8g4Eg40X2qLfkDsp5lUqKq8n5640BA0\ncRq6BaId/9oWP6OyfMprbKK2o09h2UTDdTvS4dKtyBySRlzrpqFfCkbMVeA4uJuG\nIgZQxVCsNwxV5ta8/HsCrh1/USh3Cc0ir9UxjeimApOddoogL5n9ktRuitdChPGM\nw8r1IX3Z0S1H9a6SsN2aRymsvcjv/Xkzw+Ne44KYlRVRORWdykJ/k7m3y/T2vXu0\nxH9FiEg+aB5dDII/ya7J90oiHIUKzA3wAdBuPsoN8nN06yvwoAdF5olL58DQY4wM\n0Q2hH8EyFc34atkf9IVrbYMpd6cO7MeVrd6D/WImONFF8sSOsP/rcIjse3WR2zdl\n310c5zfnKK6xFypcULTkL2DrF1IIJeFjvND4+ZBIFxkUv5cLj+SQZ7mpFuGDUbYU\n/TEVvFzVNUrvFi+6vCQxpAVaMENxuJe71fVk6uoafSOAP2EMT0TblwkR5V5CL6uJ\nod/CE+tnWGnRBilgRm1p\n=7TBm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ec62fb8385b28ae4cb1013e71d34c12b92bc91c2\nparent 5016ed6a8da381488252d4fb97a7ca78a6685a2c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784013120 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784013120 -0400\n\nfeat(code): improve `/goal` criteria UX (#4694)\n\n`/goal` now proposes shorter, outcome-focused acceptance criteria, can\nuse bounded read-only repository context when needed, and presents\nclearer grader statuses with expandable complete feedback.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user starts a `/goal`, dcode currently drafts acceptance criteria\nfrom the objective alone. That can produce long, repetitive checklists,\nwhile grader feedback can blur the difference between incomplete work,\nan invalid rubric, and a grader failure.\n\nThis change keeps goal criteria focused on the minimum observable\noutcomes needed to decide whether the goal is complete. Explicit user\nconstraints are preserved, and the generator can consult narrowly scoped\nrepository context when a referenced file or existing behavior needs\nclarification. Repository inspection is read-only and bounded;\nunavailable context falls back to drafting from the goal alone.\nUser-supplied `/rubric` criteria are unchanged.\n\nGrader results now use distinct status copy and keep the transcript\ncompact. Complete unmet-criteria explanations and next steps remain\navailable in an expandable, scrollable detail view, including after\ntranscript virtualization.\n\n## User stories and before/after examples\n\n<details>\n<summary>Goal criteria stay concise and describe outcomes instead of\nimplementation work</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user starting a goal, I want a short checklist of\nthe outcomes that matter so I can review it quickly and avoid committing\nto work I did not request.\n\n**Before**\n\nFor a goal such as “Add a compact goal-status indicator, keep `/rubric`\nunchanged, and display exactly `No goal set` when inactive,” the\nproposed rubric could repeat the same behavior across several criteria\nand add broad implementation, documentation, refactoring, or testing\nrequirements.\n\n**After**\n\nThe proposal is usually a flat list of 2–5 short criteria centered on\nobservable results, for example:\n\n- The compact goal-status indicator reflects whether a goal is active.\n- The inactive state displays exactly `No goal set`.\n- Existing `/rubric` behavior is unchanged.\n\nExplicit names, paths, commands, wording, and other user constraints are\npreserved where practical. User-authored `/rubric` criteria are not\nrewritten by this change.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Goals can use targeted repository context when the objective\ndepends on existing behavior</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user referring to an existing file, symbol,\ncommand, or behavior, I want the proposed criteria grounded in the\nrepository instead of made generic or based on guessed implementation\ndetails.\n\n**Before**\n\nA goal such as “Make the interactive grader statuses match the existing\nheadless statuses” is drafted from that sentence alone. The resulting\ncriteria may say only that the statuses should match, without\nidentifying the outcomes already represented in the codebase.\n\n**After**\n\nWhen clarification is necessary, the criteria generator can inspect the\nrelevant repository context before drafting. That allows it to\ndistinguish observable outcomes such as unmet criteria, an invalid\nrubric, and a failed acceptance-criteria check without turning\nrepository details into new requirements.\n\nInspection is limited to read-only `ls` and `read_file` calls within the\nrepository, with at most 25 tool calls and strict limits on file reads,\ndirectory listings, and returned text. If repository context is\nunavailable or unusable, `/goal` still proposes criteria from the\nobjective alone.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Grader statuses distinguish unfinished work from rubric and\ngrader failures</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user reviewing a grader result, I want the summary\nto identify what kind of outcome occurred so I know whether to continue\nthe work, revise the rubric, or retry the check.\n\n**Before**\n\nStatus wording could focus on “changes,” a generic grader failure, or an\niteration limit without consistently naming the acceptance-criteria\noutcome. It was harder to tell whether the work was incomplete, the\nrubric could not be evaluated, or the check itself failed.\n\n**After**\n\nInteractive and headless output use outcome-specific summaries:\n\n- `Acceptance criteria not yet satisfied`\n- `Acceptance criteria not yet satisfied (iteration limit reached)`\n- `Rubric is invalid or cannot be evaluated`\n- `Acceptance criteria check failed`\n\nEach result provides a corresponding next step: address unmet criteria,\nreview or replace the rubric, retry with a different grader model, or\ncontinue/amend/clear an active goal after the iteration limit.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Complete grader feedback remains available without filling the\ntranscript</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user with long grader feedback, I want a compact\ntranscript by default while retaining every explanation and\ncriterion-level gap when I need it.\n\n**Before**\n\nThe explanation, every unmet criterion, and recovery guidance were\nrendered inline with the result, so a detailed evaluation could occupy a\nlarge portion of the transcript.\n\n**After**\n\nThe transcript initially shows one concise result line. Clicking it or\npressing `Ctrl+O` opens a scrollable detail view containing the complete\nexplanation, all unmet criteria and gaps, and the recommended next step.\nThe details are not truncated, and their expanded or collapsed state is\nrestored if transcript virtualization temporarily removes and remounts\nthe message.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T07:12:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/06f46fffe36efa9f3adcb331b07df283d8bed874","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/06f46fffe36efa9f3adcb331b07df283d8bed874","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/06f46fffe36efa9f3adcb331b07df283d8bed874/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5016ed6a8da381488252d4fb97a7ca78a6685a2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5016ed6a8da381488252d4fb97a7ca78a6685a2c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5016ed6a8da381488252d4fb97a7ca78a6685a2c"}]},{"sha":"5016ed6a8da381488252d4fb97a7ca78a6685a2c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDUwMTZlZDZhOGRhMzgxNDg4MjUyZDRmYjk3YTdjYTc4YTY2ODVhMmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T06:23:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T06:23:59Z"},"message":"fix(infra): compare prereleases to previous prerelease (#4715)\n\nAlpha releases are cut from throwaway branches, so the previous alpha\ntag is a sibling of the next release commit rather than its ancestor.\nThe release workflow therefore rejected `deepagents==0.7.0a6` while\npreparing `0.7.0a7` and fell back to the latest stable tag, producing\n“Git log since deepagents==0.6.12”.\n\nThis makes prerelease resolution prefer the highest earlier prerelease\ntag with the same base version. Sibling tags are accepted when they\nshare history with the release commit and are not ahead of it; the first\nprerelease still falls back to the base-version or latest stable tag.\nFor example, `deepagents==0.7.0a7` now produces “Git log since\ndeepagents==0.7.0a6”.\n\nThe release setup summary also distinguishes an omitted `release-sha`\ninput from the canonical commit selected by the workflow, so alpha runs\nshow the exact commit they publish instead of only `(empty)`.\n\nThe workflow shell coverage exercises sibling branches, future-tag\nrejection, prerelease phase and serial ordering, stable fallbacks,\nmalformed prereleases, and canonical release-target summaries.","tree":{"sha":"a912b4436119878f9b04628bfe63404d2df84283","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a912b4436119878f9b04628bfe63404d2df84283"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5016ed6a8da381488252d4fb97a7ca78a6685a2c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVdYACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnhsQAKqOuCYFrIdVIdmCYcRlBchv\niUNiVoFp2AK9xcOxgv7VAtHz39MYQRSkjKsCVAPd9xlfQolRMN6Re6Kv9snyr+tu\n4R5I7pP9U95pFIW07W8fbHifvZ45S00dmuGuzP1VQdfigw6S04MxU6Sv7kQU7vnZ\noVa/tnfI0fRCDMBT8Kc8h4UkxjhDXDCEBNXiLwiJSY3RRMYu04RGqATEizImrGkV\nEAauyRFbriMgJeCEIa81Q/dfpdQP43Y35TZgQncrxp94fvNJGqJvqUS3cbanQt+y\n4nVpxhqYyTCr2dysqJQy4IXJHHIjUr6jgyRuKayMwp/HJOTjkAzSQ6y5dgkp69Nk\ntW2ex8AYNMHIKSotAp7+lk5V0NzfLlGiMXx0+L8buHzjklzGD2VWpx28MLbsPe2E\ni8gAnZBXBNvoJ5l4D85WOi0WBkjAgSWUzGXibf0lqxRi7BPdqbzc85Bi99AIv4OU\n56FYvrhcrI4OFVyPzjPCjfxjQx5vFXOBxbSgGybgJWAxSjYEwN8A+IaPFqjjxtAB\nCipMGodJca3IfhYdcTKbkaqCeICMvHv5il2XFEgduD12WK/KbdKPtrEgeZ7u0TpA\n0pH4gdEraVjzEuN0O3xjEaybKM3+m3aEqNPbhHG3ifxc20VGz1cP0etJ+68mGgo5\n03m8pbO1GzXp/uAj4Zat\n=xFCS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a912b4436119878f9b04628bfe63404d2df84283\nparent 64205e238c280ae05b2bf9253ac40c6f85ffb49c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784010239 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784010239 -0400\n\nfix(infra): compare prereleases to previous prerelease (#4715)\n\nAlpha releases are cut from throwaway branches, so the previous alpha\ntag is a sibling of the next release commit rather than its ancestor.\nThe release workflow therefore rejected `deepagents==0.7.0a6` while\npreparing `0.7.0a7` and fell back to the latest stable tag, producing\n“Git log since deepagents==0.6.12”.\n\nThis makes prerelease resolution prefer the highest earlier prerelease\ntag with the same base version. Sibling tags are accepted when they\nshare history with the release commit and are not ahead of it; the first\nprerelease still falls back to the base-version or latest stable tag.\nFor example, `deepagents==0.7.0a7` now produces “Git log since\ndeepagents==0.7.0a6”.\n\nThe release setup summary also distinguishes an omitted `release-sha`\ninput from the canonical commit selected by the workflow, so alpha runs\nshow the exact commit they publish instead of only `(empty)`.\n\nThe workflow shell coverage exercises sibling branches, future-tag\nrejection, prerelease phase and serial ordering, stable fallbacks,\nmalformed prereleases, and canonical release-target summaries.","verified_at":"2026-07-14T06:24:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5016ed6a8da381488252d4fb97a7ca78a6685a2c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5016ed6a8da381488252d4fb97a7ca78a6685a2c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5016ed6a8da381488252d4fb97a7ca78a6685a2c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"64205e238c280ae05b2bf9253ac40c6f85ffb49c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/64205e238c280ae05b2bf9253ac40c6f85ffb49c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/64205e238c280ae05b2bf9253ac40c6f85ffb49c"}]},{"sha":"64205e238c280ae05b2bf9253ac40c6f85ffb49c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY0MjA1ZTIzOGMyODBhZTA1YjJiZjkyNTNhYzQwYzZmODVmZmI0OWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T05:49:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T05:49:18Z"},"message":"feat(code): add interactive goal management (#4693)\n\nDeep Agents Code now supports amending, pausing, and resuming persistent\ngoals while keeping their status visible above the input. Amendments are\nreviewed before they apply, and paused goals remain saved without\ndriving work or grading until resumed.\n\n---\n\nDeep Agents Code now keeps goals visible above the input and lets users\nsteer ongoing goal-driven work without cancelling the current task and\nreplaying work.\n\n- `/goal amend <feedback>` proposes coordinated updates to the objective\nand acceptance criteria while preserving unaffected criteria and\nexplicit constraints. The inline review supports accepting, editing,\nrejecting, or cancelling the proposal before it becomes canonical state.\n- `/goal pause` saves the goal without letting it drive work or grading.\n`/goal resume` continues from the existing conversation and checkpoint\nrather than resubmitting the original task.\n- The goal panel shows the current objective and its active, paused,\nblocked, or completed state.\n- Ordinary messages submitted during active goal work retain queue and\ninterruption ordering and steer the next turn under the current goal.\n\nGoal checkpoint changes wait for graph execution and turn-end\nreconciliation to reach a safe boundary. A goal update accepted during\nexecution applies after the current turn finishes and before a\nsubsequent turn begins. If a user message is already queued, it runs\nunder the updated goal before any synthetic continuation turn.\n\n## User stories and before/after examples\n\n<details>\n<summary>Amend a goal without restarting the work</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user whose requirements change during a\nlong-running task, I want to update the current objective and acceptance\ncriteria without discarding context or repeating work that is already\ncomplete.\n\n**Before**\n\n1. I start a goal to “Add CSV and JSON export with tests.”\n2. Partway through, I decide that JSON export is out of scope and CSV\nmust also support streaming.\n3. There is no goal-specific amendment flow. I must replace or clear the\ngoal and describe the revised work again, without a review that\npreserves unaffected criteria and constraints.\n\n**After**\n\n1. I run `/goal amend Remove JSON export, add streaming CSV support, and\nkeep the existing CSV test requirements`.\n2. dcode drafts a coordinated revision of both the objective and\ncriteria while preserving requirements that the feedback did not change.\n3. The inline review lets me accept the proposal, edit its criteria,\nrequest another revision, or cancel it.\n4. Once accepted, dcode continues from the existing conversation and\nwork instead of replaying the original task.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pause a goal while keeping it available to resume</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user who needs to switch to unrelated work\ntemporarily, I want to pause my current goal so it remains saved but\ndoes not affect the intervening prompts.\n\n**Before**\n\n1. I have an active multi-turn goal.\n2. To stop that goal from driving later work and grading, I must clear\nit.\n3. Returning to it requires creating the goal again and redrafting its\nacceptance criteria.\n\n**After**\n\n1. `/goal pause` saves the objective and criteria with a paused status.\n2. Unrelated prompts run without the paused goal driving work or\ngrading.\n3. `/goal resume` reactivates the saved goal and continues from the\nexisting conversation and checkpoint without resubmitting the original\nobjective.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>See the current goal and lifecycle state while\nworking</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user working across multiple turns, I want the\ncurrent goal and its status to remain visible so I can tell what dcode\nis working toward and whether it needs my input.\n\n**Before**\n\nThe current objective is not persistently visible above the input. I\nmust use `/goal show` or infer its state from earlier transcript\nmessages.\n\n**After**\n\n- A persistent panel above the input shows the current objective.\n- The panel distinguishes active, paused, blocked, and completed states.\n- The display follows checkpoint restoration and lifecycle changes, so\nreopening a thread or changing the goal state keeps the visible status\naligned with the saved goal.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Apply in-flight goal changes without reordering queued\ninput</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user who amends a goal while the agent is still\nworking, I want the current turn to finish safely and my next message to\nrun under the accepted revision in the order I submitted it.\n\n**Before**\n\nThere is no accepted amendment to coordinate with graph execution,\ncheckpoint writes, and messages already waiting in the queue.\n\n**After**\n\n1. If I accept a goal update during an active turn, dcode waits until\nthat turn and its reconciliation finish before changing the saved goal.\n2. The accepted update is applied before a subsequent turn begins.\n3. If I already submitted another message, that message runs first under\nthe updated goal; dcode does not race ahead with a synthetic\ncontinuation turn.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"0e6a1f3f3cbc7cd100244d80c76455f3abcbc452","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0e6a1f3f3cbc7cd100244d80c76455f3abcbc452"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/64205e238c280ae05b2bf9253ac40c6f85ffb49c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVc3eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/nQQAH7XMNimEtXwi16Iq3oyX+SC\nZvTSMxT6y5p9KFkI8Ghb5cHem6fLKmeoFw481Y48hnlDm2RfXvGsO2g7zeMtrZJq\n4LqjIr/jvtSZUJzIZBauSyGlqfM95EnOCgrR6GVXf+da/Aq4fASK7FELWaD183L4\ndrJitydMcDYu9Uo2g+rDd4f7w7E5HZE8NjTJ3tmcvITYjrq5AOKLv1bLpTCfQBIi\nE/EzOuQGLiUoAdqitVcpd6K/26+wRSbELkTBvPbRTyvI0ypYaL82ABTiWtREfZ26\nB1RuatnLoYTXTPUQrISDC1yPdthfFoXc/2jvtT3tFNOziZof8ZmKOLDcscLacSi/\nqs3uZ7aI9ori0BXoBsVjOI5XN4xIH5zHECl0D353NrktAh21Gjx8UhXzTwYkeCne\nvg/b+raE6URcDESc5n7yMhGT47nsWEl9FbF75dWjiQzT+J2OcNM0Jdr3Wx3OWunH\nO2od7yCV+A9USSC5QxEn/CPdi7U0f3kAfz1RxUY4QZVdWHLCBIZczQx4m6DuFQO8\noNj8yqoJ9tp1WtzDE+xGlyDbIx58Ki9j6KvQyS3syZL0riau+FcTqMo3M6lrB84o\ntKwUG5AWxXD5K7s3T7Y1MQw9r/730QLBvH0oIEF/3tb1C+60LS1VsWmK/Vxoga4n\n0ehChi4r2XpNxj8JVgfO\n=upoF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0e6a1f3f3cbc7cd100244d80c76455f3abcbc452\nparent 5d878bf1341afc3f96398733b7ef18eec4b66139\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784008158 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784008158 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add interactive goal management (#4693)\n\nDeep Agents Code now supports amending, pausing, and resuming persistent\ngoals while keeping their status visible above the input. Amendments are\nreviewed before they apply, and paused goals remain saved without\ndriving work or grading until resumed.\n\n---\n\nDeep Agents Code now keeps goals visible above the input and lets users\nsteer ongoing goal-driven work without cancelling the current task and\nreplaying work.\n\n- `/goal amend <feedback>` proposes coordinated updates to the objective\nand acceptance criteria while preserving unaffected criteria and\nexplicit constraints. The inline review supports accepting, editing,\nrejecting, or cancelling the proposal before it becomes canonical state.\n- `/goal pause` saves the goal without letting it drive work or grading.\n`/goal resume` continues from the existing conversation and checkpoint\nrather than resubmitting the original task.\n- The goal panel shows the current objective and its active, paused,\nblocked, or completed state.\n- Ordinary messages submitted during active goal work retain queue and\ninterruption ordering and steer the next turn under the current goal.\n\nGoal checkpoint changes wait for graph execution and turn-end\nreconciliation to reach a safe boundary. A goal update accepted during\nexecution applies after the current turn finishes and before a\nsubsequent turn begins. If a user message is already queued, it runs\nunder the updated goal before any synthetic continuation turn.\n\n## User stories and before/after examples\n\n<details>\n<summary>Amend a goal without restarting the work</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user whose requirements change during a\nlong-running task, I want to update the current objective and acceptance\ncriteria without discarding context or repeating work that is already\ncomplete.\n\n**Before**\n\n1. I start a goal to “Add CSV and JSON export with tests.”\n2. Partway through, I decide that JSON export is out of scope and CSV\nmust also support streaming.\n3. There is no goal-specific amendment flow. I must replace or clear the\ngoal and describe the revised work again, without a review that\npreserves unaffected criteria and constraints.\n\n**After**\n\n1. I run `/goal amend Remove JSON export, add streaming CSV support, and\nkeep the existing CSV test requirements`.\n2. dcode drafts a coordinated revision of both the objective and\ncriteria while preserving requirements that the feedback did not change.\n3. The inline review lets me accept the proposal, edit its criteria,\nrequest another revision, or cancel it.\n4. Once accepted, dcode continues from the existing conversation and\nwork instead of replaying the original task.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pause a goal while keeping it available to resume</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user who needs to switch to unrelated work\ntemporarily, I want to pause my current goal so it remains saved but\ndoes not affect the intervening prompts.\n\n**Before**\n\n1. I have an active multi-turn goal.\n2. To stop that goal from driving later work and grading, I must clear\nit.\n3. Returning to it requires creating the goal again and redrafting its\nacceptance criteria.\n\n**After**\n\n1. `/goal pause` saves the objective and criteria with a paused status.\n2. Unrelated prompts run without the paused goal driving work or\ngrading.\n3. `/goal resume` reactivates the saved goal and continues from the\nexisting conversation and checkpoint without resubmitting the original\nobjective.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>See the current goal and lifecycle state while\nworking</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user working across multiple turns, I want the\ncurrent goal and its status to remain visible so I can tell what dcode\nis working toward and whether it needs my input.\n\n**Before**\n\nThe current objective is not persistently visible above the input. I\nmust use `/goal show` or infer its state from earlier transcript\nmessages.\n\n**After**\n\n- A persistent panel above the input shows the current objective.\n- The panel distinguishes active, paused, blocked, and completed states.\n- The display follows checkpoint restoration and lifecycle changes, so\nreopening a thread or changing the goal state keeps the visible status\naligned with the saved goal.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Apply in-flight goal changes without reordering queued\ninput</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user who amends a goal while the agent is still\nworking, I want the current turn to finish safely and my next message to\nrun under the accepted revision in the order I submitted it.\n\n**Before**\n\nThere is no accepted amendment to coordinate with graph execution,\ncheckpoint writes, and messages already waiting in the queue.\n\n**After**\n\n1. If I accept a goal update during an active turn, dcode waits until\nthat turn and its reconciliation finish before changing the saved goal.\n2. The accepted update is applied before a subsequent turn begins.\n3. If I already submitted another message, that message runs first under\nthe updated goal; dcode does not race ahead with a synthetic\ncontinuation turn.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T05:49:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/64205e238c280ae05b2bf9253ac40c6f85ffb49c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/64205e238c280ae05b2bf9253ac40c6f85ffb49c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/64205e238c280ae05b2bf9253ac40c6f85ffb49c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5d878bf1341afc3f96398733b7ef18eec4b66139","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5d878bf1341afc3f96398733b7ef18eec4b66139","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5d878bf1341afc3f96398733b7ef18eec4b66139"}]},{"sha":"5d878bf1341afc3f96398733b7ef18eec4b66139","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDVkODc4YmYxMzQxYWZjM2Y5NjM5ODczM2I3ZWYxOGVlYzRiNjYxMzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T04:39:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T04:39:50Z"},"message":"feat(sdk): use `FireworksPromptCachingMiddleware` for session affinity (#4598)\n\nDeep Agents now automatically enables Fireworks prompt-cache session\naffinity for main agents and subagents when a compatible version of\n`langchain-fireworks` is installed.\n\n---\n\nDeep Agents should automatically improve Fireworks prompt-cache reuse\nwithout owning Fireworks-specific request behavior or requiring every\nuser to install the integration.\n\n`create_deep_agent` now lazily imports\n`FireworksPromptCachingMiddleware` from `langchain-fireworks` and adds\nit to the prompt-caching stack when the integration is installed. The\nmiddleware is configured to ignore unsupported models, so the same stack\nworks when main agents and subagents use different providers.\n\nThe provider-specific middleware implementation and its handling of\n`prompt_cache_key`, `x-session-affinity`, existing caller settings, and\nthe active `thread_id` live in `langchain-fireworks`. This keeps Deep\nAgents independent of the Fireworks integration while still enabling\naffinity automatically once the corresponding integration release is\ninstalled.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e01727ebebb0acb9407e6be6c424fd654c72e04d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e01727ebebb0acb9407e6be6c424fd654c72e04d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5d878bf1341afc3f96398733b7ef18eec4b66139","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVb2WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASTQQAEBIti3jnVW9jrO3bqwnDvWC\n5dy8XPACU/h7l6RFaFWC2G3R7JnwCPHHM3UyKybaFkGDtxFJhflv1FxDgdTBrREa\nvJk7jgHjCuc3wh7Cq1ZBvCqUeyGm5ZATrnBvZhNdCUWP0ymtZ/lwrkW9dIjuCCmK\ndWg/FdOSR/a/j/Zb3iRjXigSfLn9uMB3ZjVpU3cGB7AOYQY6HP2WkMdZGgylEh8a\nf38Dm8geCbOXTth6bboo0m4kUjoVzkOsudtcoTwHf4WYRr5V+j3f9LqZACWkEi5w\n2k0nYAS1gwSqOzPrLun3sa+R3ilWMXQN+dQDl8txtBgnrma8fa372qPLAkd7eiYN\ngv8Fvg4khk7UV48nX2GK7BxCNPIgrtKM1VE7leOT0EdsbuHIHu120GzJSk/yxPiz\nSTa16gGGlO21NitfxNRwRlm79X1DHnjgQR+VzOWXhQ3/K4AbPUDkJJyJFIvMjDK7\nqbTAV6wCV0btKJowweZXrJVY9k/ZWuHDbihE+kFfmBDa+eveIONIUD3Nz210mA2v\nPDw9Lqu6hhtlfnwBPKLlKDrGuCGRKnsX68hUKg5Av0/MWk8yCH8VA+Z+ndlLzM7p\npFrvgoUE+kcm+J0xMTZCZhgWlCWmO95z/YpMez3x5x8njaon5z9GUA1BJBtMhmWE\no2ecmRFfUI1pemDPR/K8\n=btX3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e01727ebebb0acb9407e6be6c424fd654c72e04d\nparent 267d7fd3959e7f648d434313e33d7c1815c72acc\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784003990 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784003990 -0400\n\nfeat(sdk): use `FireworksPromptCachingMiddleware` for session affinity (#4598)\n\nDeep Agents now automatically enables Fireworks prompt-cache session\naffinity for main agents and subagents when a compatible version of\n`langchain-fireworks` is installed.\n\n---\n\nDeep Agents should automatically improve Fireworks prompt-cache reuse\nwithout owning Fireworks-specific request behavior or requiring every\nuser to install the integration.\n\n`create_deep_agent` now lazily imports\n`FireworksPromptCachingMiddleware` from `langchain-fireworks` and adds\nit to the prompt-caching stack when the integration is installed. The\nmiddleware is configured to ignore unsupported models, so the same stack\nworks when main agents and subagents use different providers.\n\nThe provider-specific middleware implementation and its handling of\n`prompt_cache_key`, `x-session-affinity`, existing caller settings, and\nthe active `thread_id` live in `langchain-fireworks`. This keeps Deep\nAgents independent of the Fireworks integration while still enabling\naffinity automatically once the corresponding integration release is\ninstalled.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T04:39:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5d878bf1341afc3f96398733b7ef18eec4b66139","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5d878bf1341afc3f96398733b7ef18eec4b66139","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5d878bf1341afc3f96398733b7ef18eec4b66139/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"267d7fd3959e7f648d434313e33d7c1815c72acc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/267d7fd3959e7f648d434313e33d7c1815c72acc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/267d7fd3959e7f648d434313e33d7c1815c72acc"}]},{"sha":"267d7fd3959e7f648d434313e33d7c1815c72acc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI2N2Q3ZmQzOTU5ZTdmNjQ4ZDQzNDMxM2UzM2Q3YzE4MTVjNzJhY2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T04:37:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T04:37:49Z"},"message":"style(code): inline confirmation after MCP `/mcp login` (#4597)\n\n`/mcp login` now leaves an inline \"Logged in to '<server>'.\" message in\nthe transcript on success.\n\n---\n\nAfter a successful `/mcp login <server>` OAuth flow, the only\nconfirmation was the login modal and reconnect toasts — both transient.\nThis mounts a persistent `AppMessage` in the transcript (`Logged in to\n'<server>'.`) so there's a lasting record once those dismiss.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b6757761-527b-a793-94a3-41fa5727eb66)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f63fd69a815785b71b294521ca365251ae9cbb19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f63fd69a815785b71b294521ca365251ae9cbb19"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/267d7fd3959e7f648d434313e33d7c1815c72acc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVb0dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEEAQAEvDv/VKDs1CF1mfD8D3csWp\nH07aDmOi4OhdAfwDacf2xlpVZ1N0GVz/p6+gCurddcJ4hcMJ99jLzAsVAyJJ6JUZ\nt+Xj/iWs4+e58d4Up2Z26u/jKoEXWTgdwecPj8XlsCsT/vvHKtjLztGCt7+um/uS\n0vjxivOMImVWVx+Wpg3sJMnkpNv+w+QZOU+EE+AekW1jByim+jsZEoq5zxX/BBTw\nt8739IxWMjBFnzApXjVr/Av/B0hQZ7yAUhS7QXhJSsfVEPTsuzzP0TjLZykULkBK\nNt08hlobZteaQSVhUT6FURXewc0GFhiFDYF6vYXmV5NnJbhMIOP+Pf6IYftj3MSu\ndBtpZOyjxgGF2Kolge+npvWfD1YxY5w3BjDB/5I5tN88m/pnFmNq+VtzPpEeGo2l\nj4OnQjRo/TUCXRCTEgzQet3tkS3kfEUaqB2tkx0cUaIWfn+/gauvevyPmhW2M2FV\nAHh7s9F3S0TlHArgxeSELkJtr7+9EfkGFx2HmidsmYLs6u9SA1ik6OCDW/mcjDQb\nWPRP10mxXeafq2nYT2mly089d+N4zGFiadOW75Hoo3YvlnUrv8ntp7KiWHpz6Vyt\na8AMffOuFM5I6DxPKGMGmSwMsDDnb5IR0x37R5ZTwhkHM6/0mKWahUNT8LyLVa7E\nnIOFg7gbHUpN2ndhnwSA\n=RIdH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f63fd69a815785b71b294521ca365251ae9cbb19\nparent 9da63c64a59503e3366e9bc7224cb1251af476be\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784003869 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784003869 -0400\n\nstyle(code): inline confirmation after MCP `/mcp login` (#4597)\n\n`/mcp login` now leaves an inline \"Logged in to '<server>'.\" message in\nthe transcript on success.\n\n---\n\nAfter a successful `/mcp login <server>` OAuth flow, the only\nconfirmation was the login modal and reconnect toasts — both transient.\nThis mounts a persistent `AppMessage` in the transcript (`Logged in to\n'<server>'.`) so there's a lasting record once those dismiss.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b6757761-527b-a793-94a3-41fa5727eb66)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T04:37:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/267d7fd3959e7f648d434313e33d7c1815c72acc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/267d7fd3959e7f648d434313e33d7c1815c72acc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/267d7fd3959e7f648d434313e33d7c1815c72acc/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9da63c64a59503e3366e9bc7224cb1251af476be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9da63c64a59503e3366e9bc7224cb1251af476be","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9da63c64a59503e3366e9bc7224cb1251af476be"}]},{"sha":"9da63c64a59503e3366e9bc7224cb1251af476be","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDlkYTYzYzY0YTU5NTAzZTMzNjZlOWJjNzIyNGNiMTI1MWFmNDc2YmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T04:29:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T04:29:26Z"},"message":"fix(code): make `/goal` completion and grading reliable (#4691)\n\nFixed `/goal` so completed objectives no longer grade later prompts,\nwhile unfinished goals and completion requests that could not be saved\nremain recoverable with clear guidance about what happens next.\n\n---\n\n`/goal` turns a plain-language objective into acceptance criteria and\nkeeps checking each follow-up turn until the work is done. This PR fixes\nwhat happens when that lifecycle ends—or when grading or checkpoint\npersistence fails.\n\nPreviously, a goal could remain active even after its completion was\napproved. The next prompt would then still be graded against work that\nwas already finished.\n\nGrader connection failures also looked like unmet criteria, and reaching\nthe grading iteration limit did not explain what was left to do.\n\nNow, an approved completion clears the goal and its rubric after that\ntransition is saved, so later prompts start clean and `/goal show`\nreports that no goal is set. The completion message and evidence remain\nin the thread transcript. Blocked goals stay active because they still\nneed user input and should remain resumable.\n\nIf the completion cannot be saved, dcode restores the active goal and\nits pending completion request instead of letting the UI diverge from\nthe thread checkpoint. The request is graded again on the next turn.\n\nGrading is also more reliable and actionable:\n\n- A transient mid-response transport failure retries the grader once\nwithout rerunning the agent turn, so edits and tool calls are not\nrepeated.\n- A persistent grader or infrastructure failure is identified as such\nand leaves the unfinished goal intact for a safe retry.\n- If grading reaches its iteration limit, dcode shows the unmet criteria\nand how to resume, amend, or clear the goal. Headless runs show the same\ncriterion-level gaps.\n\n## User stories and before/after examples\n\n<details>\n<summary>Completed goals stop grading unrelated follow-up\nprompts</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user who has finished a goal, I want it cleared so\nlater prompts start clean and `/goal show` reflects that there is no\ncurrent goal.\n\n**Before**\n\n1. I complete “Add refresh-token support,” and dcode approves the\ncompletion.\n2. I ask, “Now explain how cache eviction works.”\n3. dcode still grades that explanation against the refresh-token\nacceptance criteria.\n\n**After**\n\n1. Once completion is approved and saved, dcode clears the goal, rubric,\nstatus, and pending completion state.\n2. “Now explain how cache eviction works” runs without the completed\ngoal attached.\n3. `/goal show` reports “No goal set.” The earlier completion message\nand evidence remain in the thread transcript.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>A completion that cannot be saved remains safe to\nretry</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user whose thread checkpoint is temporarily\nunavailable, I want dcode’s displayed state to match the saved thread so\nresuming cannot silently lose or misreport my goal.\n\n**Before**\n\n1. The grader approves completion, but saving the completed state fails.\n2. dcode can look complete in the current session even though the thread\nstill contains an active goal and pending completion.\n\n**After**\n\n1. dcode restores the active goal, rubric, and pending completion\nrequest in the UI.\n2. It reports: “Goal completion could not be saved, so the goal remains\nactive and its completion request is still pending for retry.”\n3. The completion request is graded again on the next turn.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>A dropped grader response retries grading without repeating the\nwork</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user whose grader connection drops while reading a\nresponse, I want dcode to retry the check without rerunning edits or\ntool calls that already succeeded.\n\n**Before**\n\n1. The agent finishes the requested work.\n2. The grader connection closes partway through its response.\n3. The grading attempt ends even though the agent turn itself succeeded.\n\n**After**\n\n1. dcode retries the grader once for recognized mid-response transport\nfailures.\n2. Only the grading subagent runs again; the task agent’s edits and tool\ncalls are not repeated.\n3. If the retry succeeds, the normal rubric result is used.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Persistent grader failures are not presented as missing user\nwork</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user facing a grader or infrastructure outage, I\nwant dcode to identify the outage instead of telling me that my\nimplementation failed its criteria.\n\n**Before**\n\nA grader connection failure can look like an unmet rubric, leaving it\nunclear whether the implementation or the grading service failed.\n\n**After**\n\n- The transcript identifies a persistent transport problem as\n“Grader/infrastructure failure.”\n- If the grader cannot evaluate the rubric, dcode says so explicitly\nrather than reporting ordinary unmet criteria.\n- The goal remains active. For an infrastructure failure, its completion\nrequest also remains pending and is re-graded on the next turn.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Iteration limits show the remaining gaps and recovery\nchoices</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user whose goal reaches the grading limit, I want\nto know what is still missing and how to continue.\n\n**Before**\n\n> ⚠ Acceptance criteria not satisfied (iteration limit reached)\n\nThe message does not identify the failing criteria or explain what\nhappens to the goal.\n\n**After**\n\n> ⚠ Iteration limit reached with unmet acceptance criteria  \n> ✗ Refresh-token tests — the expiration case is still failing  \n> The goal remains active. Continue with another prompt to resume or\nretry, use `/goal <objective>` to amend it, or `/goal clear` to clear\nit.\n\nInteractive and headless runs both show criterion-level gaps, and the\nunfinished goal remains available for the next action.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"9e53030eee60a8d7f1133b494091c70ddf72eaf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9e53030eee60a8d7f1133b494091c70ddf72eaf2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9da63c64a59503e3366e9bc7224cb1251af476be","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVbsmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlwQQAKvY5OqY+QB6Y+77eE/Ry25N\nyjX5/j5bRQi240PvRNwT7JmpNzOCYy+3OmqZ5ZvX+oy22mRShFf6ooNB3ctUeawp\nrLkYU/6y7yiIRJOEJ4z3EnAHFQWMViENlDsbtr4yrxJ5ow8vguxAO6RWpE1W/WJJ\nSpHIKm4ZH8e1qsZ7sdJaO6mq8QBmXYZf/E7vnpEelVAa+eEELPVDZrRfK/thzgnP\n5rT0vGH6tLwHKIIp7oQMyUNzMEih5JqmQRxg1YlhyPPSr62oTurGWUTJD9Wgcirq\nltuqcVE+bvOVGD9Bumnbwgi2nyfAJWfYMWP+cm57NID797psz+5GIlt+u+Pb4Oek\npHypt6aRUY8wT/XENaMWr7yeRL6TKAwNdx0ZSKo1W3hwuddsfOwBDzaE+76gtSuW\n61IsoiYy4V3JcshDV/GkEcCLNqgqW99WsmQdc6Yabl22lCGbWN6GLxCNLi+Aqey4\n27Y+hHLbip7gIGgI0uBUIhDi4BmYR7avwZOMX34igyVhBWoSR95hhV+z8jO5LX0G\n11J6KTeFXAcYNpBJ15eD09lhw2imGho1ia/juzSPKiTp93016488pjLkHOHVdqGk\nL29L4O/1Bxsk/0qZlVtz0Uc0knWWeRFV7qr++NXM2eY1Iwayt2xxYtpibKR1X5+K\nlNfhXCAHdOOlGdn+H/vo\n=fM6t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9e53030eee60a8d7f1133b494091c70ddf72eaf2\nparent 65e1ee802e2f69762a6d8e6c7c6d37060161ea5a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784003366 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784003366 -0400\n\nfix(code): make `/goal` completion and grading reliable (#4691)\n\nFixed `/goal` so completed objectives no longer grade later prompts,\nwhile unfinished goals and completion requests that could not be saved\nremain recoverable with clear guidance about what happens next.\n\n---\n\n`/goal` turns a plain-language objective into acceptance criteria and\nkeeps checking each follow-up turn until the work is done. This PR fixes\nwhat happens when that lifecycle ends—or when grading or checkpoint\npersistence fails.\n\nPreviously, a goal could remain active even after its completion was\napproved. The next prompt would then still be graded against work that\nwas already finished.\n\nGrader connection failures also looked like unmet criteria, and reaching\nthe grading iteration limit did not explain what was left to do.\n\nNow, an approved completion clears the goal and its rubric after that\ntransition is saved, so later prompts start clean and `/goal show`\nreports that no goal is set. The completion message and evidence remain\nin the thread transcript. Blocked goals stay active because they still\nneed user input and should remain resumable.\n\nIf the completion cannot be saved, dcode restores the active goal and\nits pending completion request instead of letting the UI diverge from\nthe thread checkpoint. The request is graded again on the next turn.\n\nGrading is also more reliable and actionable:\n\n- A transient mid-response transport failure retries the grader once\nwithout rerunning the agent turn, so edits and tool calls are not\nrepeated.\n- A persistent grader or infrastructure failure is identified as such\nand leaves the unfinished goal intact for a safe retry.\n- If grading reaches its iteration limit, dcode shows the unmet criteria\nand how to resume, amend, or clear the goal. Headless runs show the same\ncriterion-level gaps.\n\n## User stories and before/after examples\n\n<details>\n<summary>Completed goals stop grading unrelated follow-up\nprompts</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user who has finished a goal, I want it cleared so\nlater prompts start clean and `/goal show` reflects that there is no\ncurrent goal.\n\n**Before**\n\n1. I complete “Add refresh-token support,” and dcode approves the\ncompletion.\n2. I ask, “Now explain how cache eviction works.”\n3. dcode still grades that explanation against the refresh-token\nacceptance criteria.\n\n**After**\n\n1. Once completion is approved and saved, dcode clears the goal, rubric,\nstatus, and pending completion state.\n2. “Now explain how cache eviction works” runs without the completed\ngoal attached.\n3. `/goal show` reports “No goal set.” The earlier completion message\nand evidence remain in the thread transcript.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>A completion that cannot be saved remains safe to\nretry</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user whose thread checkpoint is temporarily\nunavailable, I want dcode’s displayed state to match the saved thread so\nresuming cannot silently lose or misreport my goal.\n\n**Before**\n\n1. The grader approves completion, but saving the completed state fails.\n2. dcode can look complete in the current session even though the thread\nstill contains an active goal and pending completion.\n\n**After**\n\n1. dcode restores the active goal, rubric, and pending completion\nrequest in the UI.\n2. It reports: “Goal completion could not be saved, so the goal remains\nactive and its completion request is still pending for retry.”\n3. The completion request is graded again on the next turn.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>A dropped grader response retries grading without repeating the\nwork</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user whose grader connection drops while reading a\nresponse, I want dcode to retry the check without rerunning edits or\ntool calls that already succeeded.\n\n**Before**\n\n1. The agent finishes the requested work.\n2. The grader connection closes partway through its response.\n3. The grading attempt ends even though the agent turn itself succeeded.\n\n**After**\n\n1. dcode retries the grader once for recognized mid-response transport\nfailures.\n2. Only the grading subagent runs again; the task agent’s edits and tool\ncalls are not repeated.\n3. If the retry succeeds, the normal rubric result is used.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Persistent grader failures are not presented as missing user\nwork</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user facing a grader or infrastructure outage, I\nwant dcode to identify the outage instead of telling me that my\nimplementation failed its criteria.\n\n**Before**\n\nA grader connection failure can look like an unmet rubric, leaving it\nunclear whether the implementation or the grading service failed.\n\n**After**\n\n- The transcript identifies a persistent transport problem as\n“Grader/infrastructure failure.”\n- If the grader cannot evaluate the rubric, dcode says so explicitly\nrather than reporting ordinary unmet criteria.\n- The goal remains active. For an infrastructure failure, its completion\nrequest also remains pending and is re-graded on the next turn.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Iteration limits show the remaining gaps and recovery\nchoices</summary>\n\n**User story:** As a user whose goal reaches the grading limit, I want\nto know what is still missing and how to continue.\n\n**Before**\n\n> ⚠ Acceptance criteria not satisfied (iteration limit reached)\n\nThe message does not identify the failing criteria or explain what\nhappens to the goal.\n\n**After**\n\n> ⚠ Iteration limit reached with unmet acceptance criteria  \n> ✗ Refresh-token tests — the expiration case is still failing  \n> The goal remains active. Continue with another prompt to resume or\nretry, use `/goal <objective>` to amend it, or `/goal clear` to clear\nit.\n\nInteractive and headless runs both show criterion-level gaps, and the\nunfinished goal remains available for the next action.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T04:29:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9da63c64a59503e3366e9bc7224cb1251af476be","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9da63c64a59503e3366e9bc7224cb1251af476be","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9da63c64a59503e3366e9bc7224cb1251af476be/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"65e1ee802e2f69762a6d8e6c7c6d37060161ea5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/65e1ee802e2f69762a6d8e6c7c6d37060161ea5a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/65e1ee802e2f69762a6d8e6c7c6d37060161ea5a"}]},{"sha":"65e1ee802e2f69762a6d8e6c7c6d37060161ea5a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY1ZTFlZTgwMmUyZjY5NzYyYTZkOGU2YzdjNmQzNzA2MDE2MWVhNWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T04:12:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T04:12:36Z"},"message":"fix(code): run MCP login during a run, queue the restart (#4643)\n\n`/mcp login` now runs during an active generation instead of waiting for\nit to finish; if you accept the reconnect, the server restart is queued\nand applied automatically once the current task completes.\n\n---\n\n`/mcp login` previously deferred the *entire* OAuth flow until an active\nagent or shell task finished. But only the final server restart\n(`_restart_server_for_mcp_refresh` → `_respawn_server`) actually\nconflicts with a live run — the OAuth handshake and on-disk token write\nnever touch the running server. This starts login immediately even\nduring a generation and queues only the restart, so the user can\nauthenticate without waiting for the turn to end.\n\nWhen the user accepts \"reconnect\" on the post-login prompt while a run\nis active, the restart is queued as a new `mcp_reconnect` deferred\naction (drained by the existing `_maybe_drain_deferred` on agent/shell\ncleanup) instead of tearing down the in-flight generation. The reconnect\nis marked pending in the meantime so `/mcp reconnect` and the splash\nbanner stay accurate, and the queued action re-checks the pending flag\nto avoid a redundant restart if a manual `/mcp reconnect` already ran.\nWhen idle, behavior is unchanged (immediate restart).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4defa6fb-fe26-d47b-9fa0-10b5a9c29dcd)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2036b391d6f69a6584d8871c44b21b7b8a5d9903","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2036b391d6f69a6584d8871c44b21b7b8a5d9903"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/65e1ee802e2f69762a6d8e6c7c6d37060161ea5a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVbc0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9ygQADm8V9HcKeLBH9x2TRy7Z+2t\nAv4PYbBeawUbpw/5lOR/3ALfDgtlLd4sgISXPWcPueERHhJOw309gE3OKcgKftw3\n6/iwXbFGNS3hLbqQuysBxXpQsj8/PchzGINohAOJ7nCLNa6UJr4Z6vZ/rSW0YB8i\nNdsZS5Jh+4wQQehAzQ0IMiTpQgl0IH7irDoeY9jK+LrgRfWaV82Gq/1jspTihWKj\nKkIDSAlEkpSWHlbqk2D9R1fKFIqi3m4lbMRglNwQLLvcTXPTxOrW64WRYlE0BrkC\ns7LL0CbZch3HdBpoHPxZiFPM/TqeyhOkHV09zTcdqYDton0+P2lta+UGnDx5o9YC\nUJclk0dBPZB6sIkfb0gtoQGLsjB2eYk0n5r2vqB+Uam6jgxxBpBbiivSIGwWQF3X\nt579kELqv9e31nrrNGyPdYhMTiQNsFXpbPyyFBAs8FVi9mqSxGkCE6JEBqy9qYQe\nWsNj58J7gulJlKd89Rw3QJK5ON3xcAKXAI/sdpKol/zrSIBnTmtOwT4KOOxYFSCm\nWvbYZL0Zxn+ZoQUk0fY8SGKxpnQhqAvoK4EWD3y8224SggyclOFuEsWBMG/RHjPc\nEn49HbDsh8uZuTWwQ2IEaTlP3cp+ikmiL4mjQUYoSPOIlra2JfP1FuxExSXYXk7s\nZEywJiIdTI819LQeYykh\n=Uwiz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2036b391d6f69a6584d8871c44b21b7b8a5d9903\nparent f9915db4206ef2d794ad07fdccbdd4ee58963142\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784002356 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784002356 -0400\n\nfix(code): run MCP login during a run, queue the restart (#4643)\n\n`/mcp login` now runs during an active generation instead of waiting for\nit to finish; if you accept the reconnect, the server restart is queued\nand applied automatically once the current task completes.\n\n---\n\n`/mcp login` previously deferred the *entire* OAuth flow until an active\nagent or shell task finished. But only the final server restart\n(`_restart_server_for_mcp_refresh` → `_respawn_server`) actually\nconflicts with a live run — the OAuth handshake and on-disk token write\nnever touch the running server. This starts login immediately even\nduring a generation and queues only the restart, so the user can\nauthenticate without waiting for the turn to end.\n\nWhen the user accepts \"reconnect\" on the post-login prompt while a run\nis active, the restart is queued as a new `mcp_reconnect` deferred\naction (drained by the existing `_maybe_drain_deferred` on agent/shell\ncleanup) instead of tearing down the in-flight generation. The reconnect\nis marked pending in the meantime so `/mcp reconnect` and the splash\nbanner stay accurate, and the queued action re-checks the pending flag\nto avoid a redundant restart if a manual `/mcp reconnect` already ran.\nWhen idle, behavior is unchanged (immediate restart).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4defa6fb-fe26-d47b-9fa0-10b5a9c29dcd)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T04:12:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/65e1ee802e2f69762a6d8e6c7c6d37060161ea5a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/65e1ee802e2f69762a6d8e6c7c6d37060161ea5a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/65e1ee802e2f69762a6d8e6c7c6d37060161ea5a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f9915db4206ef2d794ad07fdccbdd4ee58963142","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f9915db4206ef2d794ad07fdccbdd4ee58963142","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f9915db4206ef2d794ad07fdccbdd4ee58963142"}]},{"sha":"f9915db4206ef2d794ad07fdccbdd4ee58963142","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY5OTE1ZGI0MjA2ZWYyZDc5NGFkMDdmZGNjYmRkNGVlNTg5NjMxNDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T04:12:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T04:12:26Z"},"message":"fix(code): align context diff rows with changed rows (#4714)\n\nFixed a one-character horizontal misalignment between unchanged and\nchanged lines in the interactive diff view.\n\n---\n\nIn the terminal diff widget, unchanged (context) rows put two spaces\nafter the right-aligned line number while added/removed rows use one.\nThat made unchanged content render one column to the right of changed\ncontent, so the diff body looked misaligned by a single character.\nStandardizing on a single separator space for every row type lines the\ncontent up vertically.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/408eb040-6f08-7f47-c9d0-3ebf4693c6a5)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"197d079a71f9eec0bc50c9892bcdd10330fae2eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/197d079a71f9eec0bc50c9892bcdd10330fae2eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f9915db4206ef2d794ad07fdccbdd4ee58963142","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVbcqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAx7IQAHZ6l0KXn4COMVWPgzK749Sb\nm2Hd59VVIyiGmtZO+mSMjPqNcLmZUWXVv7gCYCZYWgAcnwCMStwqVkNaO+soMAX1\nKkQllE+Bc65p8uFkURdyjuNalqF/N/KNZEIyUHdk6OBZav+gT6A9SqT4JUwLfXbw\nrNkwXsKwP9V3jQ139LTmECmFR1lWry28ZdSuUrolVUYUn06Dv8b5763cIo+goU77\nXT8S/fpUXbOanSHMJg5qHplETyy16ZO8DTM6ff1fkdY1tMCnc/5tyC+UiipKDu0m\n9OuhkwxXd1UL66KEAXOHB73W1ZBe4cujJ+KxHkihcNj5mf/aGoDgrkFDH++Y+BB+\nrtpjdUWPyJ4Vl2OjND7+ZyNQ8GgatCMa37LrF1Iev7foFIoCKeyd2UwAUgMneQKD\nbgiom9owQmz35uL4S1hcCav/+eVR9yNwR6m/Xu+V0f+kb/XAcaJLpsUPVyt66bn2\nMUCJT4glZmWJAPJM1vJh/kNAU/FtiYu33TpFcPOl1xKjDdHPHaUI7/biEnHaCvz2\nrei4pGJP6JTFsu3fFx3sp2bWDLXR1qSwxjRTfauCsDpqeogwX8UA4F4la0lCw9iL\noTu+DFOvA0GfAizenzI0dyKlDeYKfPPARcyeRe3uvDILNf12iLIdmL59RG4QGwpj\nkC2N9usf9xR8qaqfl1QN\n=ntUS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 197d079a71f9eec0bc50c9892bcdd10330fae2eb\nparent 8e86f5ecc8908762a2c748880287f190dde70600\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784002346 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784002346 -0400\n\nfix(code): align context diff rows with changed rows (#4714)\n\nFixed a one-character horizontal misalignment between unchanged and\nchanged lines in the interactive diff view.\n\n---\n\nIn the terminal diff widget, unchanged (context) rows put two spaces\nafter the right-aligned line number while added/removed rows use one.\nThat made unchanged content render one column to the right of changed\ncontent, so the diff body looked misaligned by a single character.\nStandardizing on a single separator space for every row type lines the\ncontent up vertically.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/408eb040-6f08-7f47-c9d0-3ebf4693c6a5)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T04:12:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f9915db4206ef2d794ad07fdccbdd4ee58963142","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f9915db4206ef2d794ad07fdccbdd4ee58963142","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f9915db4206ef2d794ad07fdccbdd4ee58963142/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8e86f5ecc8908762a2c748880287f190dde70600","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e86f5ecc8908762a2c748880287f190dde70600","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8e86f5ecc8908762a2c748880287f190dde70600"}]},{"sha":"8e86f5ecc8908762a2c748880287f190dde70600","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhlODZmNWVjYzg5MDg3NjJhMmM3NDg4ODAyODdmMTkwZGRlNzA2MDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T04:11:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T04:11:34Z"},"message":"feat(sdk): add total match cap and streaming to grep (#4570)\n\nCloses #2834\n\n`FilesystemMiddleware`'s `grep` tool now returns at most **1000 matches\nby default** (previously unbounded). When the cap is hit, results are\ntruncated and a note tells the model to narrow the search or raise\n`max_count`. This bounds memory and context size on very large\nrepositories.\n\n- The model can raise or lower the cap per call via the new `max_count`\nargument on the `grep` tool.\n- To restore the previous unbounded behavior, construct\n`FilesystemMiddleware(..., grep_max_count=None)`.\n- Direct backend callers (`backend.grep(...)`) are unaffected:\n`max_count` defaults to `None` (no cap) unless explicitly passed.\n\n---\n\nDeep Agents' filesystem `grep` was already timeout-bounded, but it could\nstill buffer an unbounded number of matches: the local ripgrep path ran\n`subprocess.run(capture_output=True)`, so a broad pattern on a huge repo\n(e.g. the Linux kernel) could buffer gigabytes of stdout before the tool\nlayer got a chance to truncate, risking OOM.\n\nThis adds a total-match cap and makes the local ripgrep path stream:\n\n- New keyword-only `max_count: int | None = None` on\n`BackendProtocol.grep`/`agrep` and every backend implementation\n(`filesystem`, `state`, `store`, `sandbox`, `composite`, `context_hub`).\nIt is a total cap across all files, not per-file. Defaulting to `None`\nkeeps existing direct-backend behavior unchanged.\n- `LocalFilesystemBackend` now streams ripgrep's `--json` output via\n`subprocess.Popen` line-by-line, stops and `terminate()`s the process\nonce the cap is reached, and passes `-m` as a cheap secondary per-file\nguard. A `threading.Timer` watchdog preserves the existing time-limit\nbehavior. The Python fallback early-returns at the cap.\n- `CompositeBackend` enforces the cap globally across routed backends,\nshort-circuiting remaining routes once it is met.\n- `GrepResult.truncated` (already present) is set when the cap is hit,\nand `FilesystemMiddleware` gains a `grep_max_count` default of `1000`\n(configurable, and overridable per call via the tool's `max_count`\nargument). The truncation note shown to the model now covers both the\ntime-limit and match-cap cases.\n\nReviewers may want to focus on the rewritten `_ripgrep_search`\nstreaming/termination/watchdog logic and the composite cross-route\nbudget accounting.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/389434e7-284f-e1ff-11ba-8c65c21683af)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6069e60b969884fcecf73235bb32f8a1807b627f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6069e60b969884fcecf73235bb32f8a1807b627f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8e86f5ecc8908762a2c748880287f190dde70600","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVbb2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0mMQAJBjzYpEuZChECaaQXnwpH65\nhC157du0s3qUaZg2qms/Rgl5ueN64q1t+lUXKgcKZm6CbjArbiH4GTHmhmlmYQV5\n6pXfJ2nWDHalH/dwznFRzFJNbD0r+8bxcVzsJfeMB2pYTlheBO4xJ96jg3jMq1MZ\nv+WRP1v/Bh9WeLcsaNmKhajDqKWdUEKEfIrupp+lKMRp3hMr6gJ6wnq2V7wSk0P3\nDbTFevZR6xFz3TvRXkctGB9Afyc7Sqbrpr9SRSHt06g8srXn6m90Bp9EfVwA8wWC\nHa9KCkA2OUA7cH1UIDOzQz5C1ibretYFp+9LnZHbXpKOn7YwHZnoHCUuPCAfA12u\nj048mHVDyXl0JEG0lCmoQXQ/81uSz32TeM+Ft1cAKOMq1hCxEvg0J8g7ze9jvFNp\naf2V5viDlX7mBMTawnxOVWFvQDSssssnsjOH2mtz9n2Wy+qsVLUnqLJj7fPqcPRp\nt1k+alxyY++bOSEeYrPOPpcwj0mjkuliuFLQF2TJyEnkqM24QipE2LW+8C1m2XU/\n3aTd5LhQw4IYuDX+nvk2W0/LZGABj+NDMtFbXvlU7UJ2EvKu0md/BnE+Vb7Ra898\n2yH5rzNtC7Kgxp6ePFKqAxqa3a+iQlTk8ROl/BgPH765bDYDV+vey4B2qMs8LA4q\n7SF7pOJAVtImx7MoRSDw\n=n4Tt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6069e60b969884fcecf73235bb32f8a1807b627f\nparent 19538e0a46a5c2c050412b79fd45608a63cdde52\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784002294 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784002294 -0400\n\nfeat(sdk): add total match cap and streaming to grep (#4570)\n\nCloses #2834\n\n`FilesystemMiddleware`'s `grep` tool now returns at most **1000 matches\nby default** (previously unbounded). When the cap is hit, results are\ntruncated and a note tells the model to narrow the search or raise\n`max_count`. This bounds memory and context size on very large\nrepositories.\n\n- The model can raise or lower the cap per call via the new `max_count`\nargument on the `grep` tool.\n- To restore the previous unbounded behavior, construct\n`FilesystemMiddleware(..., grep_max_count=None)`.\n- Direct backend callers (`backend.grep(...)`) are unaffected:\n`max_count` defaults to `None` (no cap) unless explicitly passed.\n\n---\n\nDeep Agents' filesystem `grep` was already timeout-bounded, but it could\nstill buffer an unbounded number of matches: the local ripgrep path ran\n`subprocess.run(capture_output=True)`, so a broad pattern on a huge repo\n(e.g. the Linux kernel) could buffer gigabytes of stdout before the tool\nlayer got a chance to truncate, risking OOM.\n\nThis adds a total-match cap and makes the local ripgrep path stream:\n\n- New keyword-only `max_count: int | None = None` on\n`BackendProtocol.grep`/`agrep` and every backend implementation\n(`filesystem`, `state`, `store`, `sandbox`, `composite`, `context_hub`).\nIt is a total cap across all files, not per-file. Defaulting to `None`\nkeeps existing direct-backend behavior unchanged.\n- `LocalFilesystemBackend` now streams ripgrep's `--json` output via\n`subprocess.Popen` line-by-line, stops and `terminate()`s the process\nonce the cap is reached, and passes `-m` as a cheap secondary per-file\nguard. A `threading.Timer` watchdog preserves the existing time-limit\nbehavior. The Python fallback early-returns at the cap.\n- `CompositeBackend` enforces the cap globally across routed backends,\nshort-circuiting remaining routes once it is met.\n- `GrepResult.truncated` (already present) is set when the cap is hit,\nand `FilesystemMiddleware` gains a `grep_max_count` default of `1000`\n(configurable, and overridable per call via the tool's `max_count`\nargument). The truncation note shown to the model now covers both the\ntime-limit and match-cap cases.\n\nReviewers may want to focus on the rewritten `_ripgrep_search`\nstreaming/termination/watchdog logic and the composite cross-route\nbudget accounting.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/389434e7-284f-e1ff-11ba-8c65c21683af)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T04:11:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e86f5ecc8908762a2c748880287f190dde70600","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8e86f5ecc8908762a2c748880287f190dde70600","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e86f5ecc8908762a2c748880287f190dde70600/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"19538e0a46a5c2c050412b79fd45608a63cdde52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/19538e0a46a5c2c050412b79fd45608a63cdde52","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/19538e0a46a5c2c050412b79fd45608a63cdde52"}]},{"sha":"19538e0a46a5c2c050412b79fd45608a63cdde52","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE5NTM4ZTBhNDZhNWMyYzA1MDQxMmI3OWZkNDU2MDhhNjNjZGRlNTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T04:09:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T04:09:17Z"},"message":"fix(code): show \"Took <duration>\" when `task` tool completes (#4638)\n\nThe completed `task` subagent tool widget now reports its elapsed run\ntime (`Took <duration>`), matching `execute`.\n\n---\n\nThe completed `task` (subagent) tool widget never displayed a `Took\n<duration>` line the way `execute` does. On success, `task` fell through\nto `_show_success_status`, which hides the status row entirely when the\ntool produced output — so the elapsed run time was lost. This\ngeneralizes the timing branch in `set_success` to a\n`_TIMED_SUCCESS_TOOLS` set covering both `execute` and `task`, so\nlong-running subagent dispatches now report how long they ran once the\nspinner stops.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e4c0f49c-071d-bd35-7a89-d4b1fdb67244)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"96e4c82746484610ae386463b6450397302ef5d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/96e4c82746484610ae386463b6450397302ef5d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/19538e0a46a5c2c050412b79fd45608a63cdde52","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVbZtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGngQAK7whfelfnOz7vmeOkik0auP\n+h7UtCvZWrBOWD41i7nA5YdASK6opUvApCgvC8PwMuE66o6+rmgp+9qFyV05MCTF\nuJDryxQoeFg/F1iQgIXWcbTMlAIygWz6y83l57rQAlVNe40VdUBucDsLILOeE+90\nqMxW2by7sPu+Fejz1I7EwTfJXUPDRtcE1Eolt49PVs9mNdk3QHEWuEo3OrmBZx5r\nm7zSHhAEWX6L2MFAzWRA7B8TC2cK2vbPQBI9biEbFcR1wdJZWYGejRGdXiveiygy\nUmVatzNpjBDoffeGLC4JfJ0S1loYXgtW4fG2O/P1AkXzL5ykUvUu8xtvgjahWL5w\nMXP3VD7k9NJpqxb93b4nK3JbFQxkQ//vCCeehnbBudpEP0K2yIgmtZHG8RqwLFPq\nZIGU3g5fVfRlzSaX8RHchFuBjwrvLM2jLZcKlTvV66IXnwvxTH6CkikW7gC0moo7\n64vcRzlJWqBwjT+yNmZ+tdJktkQ5ehIlbTaqAnTGvJ3RVswQUG93qTa/rHjCAkJ4\nI4lijnl0CECYIdajFRBWkOwSPaBdEpXeRT35zL85a4ag5vE8iA9P8gkBdz2LEoBj\nyXpY1zNyaYoBHBQwcUpr8hyZ+bfd4Xz80X5C9rhG2xuJd020OoAap+1IIkOpK+x5\n/WN/kl+bHxr/XLZSj5pX\n=pGiH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 96e4c82746484610ae386463b6450397302ef5d6\nparent 2089b54e2a674ede313e790b59febf9dc6f22571\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784002157 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784002157 -0400\n\nfix(code): show \"Took <duration>\" when `task` tool completes (#4638)\n\nThe completed `task` subagent tool widget now reports its elapsed run\ntime (`Took <duration>`), matching `execute`.\n\n---\n\nThe completed `task` (subagent) tool widget never displayed a `Took\n<duration>` line the way `execute` does. On success, `task` fell through\nto `_show_success_status`, which hides the status row entirely when the\ntool produced output — so the elapsed run time was lost. This\ngeneralizes the timing branch in `set_success` to a\n`_TIMED_SUCCESS_TOOLS` set covering both `execute` and `task`, so\nlong-running subagent dispatches now report how long they ran once the\nspinner stops.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e4c0f49c-071d-bd35-7a89-d4b1fdb67244)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T04:09:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/19538e0a46a5c2c050412b79fd45608a63cdde52","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/19538e0a46a5c2c050412b79fd45608a63cdde52","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/19538e0a46a5c2c050412b79fd45608a63cdde52/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2089b54e2a674ede313e790b59febf9dc6f22571","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2089b54e2a674ede313e790b59febf9dc6f22571","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2089b54e2a674ede313e790b59febf9dc6f22571"}]},{"sha":"2089b54e2a674ede313e790b59febf9dc6f22571","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDIwODliNTRlMmE2NzRlZGUzMTNlNzkwYjU5ZmViZjlkYzZmMjI1NzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T04:01:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T04:01:46Z"},"message":"fix(code): support unambiguous `read_file` gutters (#4711)\n\nDepends on #4561.\n\nDeep Agents Code now displays both legacy and current `read_file` line\ngutters without dropping tab-based source indentation.\n\n---\n\nDeep Agents Code compacts `read_file` line-number gutters before\ndisplaying tool output. The SDK change in #4561 replaces the ambiguous\ntab separator with two spaces, but the TUI parser currently recognizes\nonly the legacy format.\n\nTeach the parser to recognize both formats while consuming only the\ngutter separator. This preserves tabs that belong to source indentation\nand keeps compatibility with older string backends that still emit `cat\n-n`-style output.","tree":{"sha":"8c5b7b0b9a22e0214d19422f34087da4f41a5556","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8c5b7b0b9a22e0214d19422f34087da4f41a5556"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2089b54e2a674ede313e790b59febf9dc6f22571","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVbSqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAibcQAEV3sFNKayB06i6DEaOnvzu0\nqMgySRDKieB1xaHkwS/3V1trzPsCvoZibFeJxpUOmTI5dmJJuD0SATPVifWPLmT/\nQeH8XB4/Rr/vjkO3md6tuVwGhNcwlW+ncmsVeOFJ3nsHawoD7+kMPPUNiat7RD7L\n5vsGOP9JsSmCbyRjwv0oGEkgV1Huye9rar+9IvL+rS7Ieb/Qc6OP8VmRBKgDL224\n1HXOwnBPHDkOrMvPMf46TN+oBrTHmXLpKbWoqgOB4OZ112Lw9XDzw4N5d1crW1dI\n316b6LW5cf6DJrPt3E2y04KhJhb9YZ77INye+aN9IoEn2Ehy9pivBqzm6ELmayzM\nDIpXdlz3S8eJvg2q7fDyiOtlkzzP8XGPaC6/4ab7lD0BxAYYO93AHXQSiEpM2hvt\nY/kSXkaVB7MG3VOJmyi7gdtE7Lu4mFZEyD1ogzMMnMqCFLydseqJcmzUOGM5xVUP\nt+c535GFJDmhA4cofH9qdn1UAbFJsBdwJ7fLSbU7pXfhKzrxKNd1MdGyTwDtm3SU\nbXviG0uB2UAaSFuR0AgV7HPpe0fkxTTadrInj0S+5miBpJmMJ/Cgxg4nWAl7URWY\nrO5oSaJQ6+r1H4gCoZ4+iLVrVr45Bo5NIFpZS4xB2lr9HHmApUYSpMLpGEaNJXEO\nYPlTQ8L/1xtH8tafM309\n=5yp/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8c5b7b0b9a22e0214d19422f34087da4f41a5556\nparent cf057b4bcdb77ad67014f7dabe71e71f2366c95e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784001706 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784001706 -0400\n\nfix(code): support unambiguous `read_file` gutters (#4711)\n\nDepends on #4561.\n\nDeep Agents Code now displays both legacy and current `read_file` line\ngutters without dropping tab-based source indentation.\n\n---\n\nDeep Agents Code compacts `read_file` line-number gutters before\ndisplaying tool output. The SDK change in #4561 replaces the ambiguous\ntab separator with two spaces, but the TUI parser currently recognizes\nonly the legacy format.\n\nTeach the parser to recognize both formats while consuming only the\ngutter separator. This preserves tabs that belong to source indentation\nand keeps compatibility with older string backends that still emit `cat\n-n`-style output.","verified_at":"2026-07-14T04:01:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2089b54e2a674ede313e790b59febf9dc6f22571","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2089b54e2a674ede313e790